L0000:	db	'"Well met, seeker. I am Dracothraxus. Thy test, and I fear, '
	db	'thy defeat lies before thee. For thou shouldst know that I a'
	db	'm made immortal by the Keeper of Courage. \'Twould take a tr'
	db	'uly powerful artifact to destroy me... one that does not exi'
	db	'st." The great dragon paws the earth in expectation of your '
	db	'imminent battle.'
	db	00
L013C:	db	'Dracothraxus sniffs the air distastefully, "I sense my doom '
	db	'nearby. Perhaps I am to be released at long last. I wish the'
	db	'e good luck mortal. Defend thyself!"  With that, the dragon '
	db	'leaps at you.'
	db	00
L01FE:	db	'Dracothraxus sniffs the air distastefully, "I sense my doom '
	db	'nearby. Perhaps I am to be released at long last. I wish the'
	db	'e good luck mortal. Defend thyself!"  With that, the dragon '
	db	'leaps at you.'
	db	00
L02C0:	db	'"Thou hast returned to test thy mettle, little one. Thy cour'
	db	'age does thee honor, however, I think that thou shalt take t'
	db	'hine honor to the grave with thee."*'
	db	00
L035D:	db	'The dragon lets out a searing sigh, "Released at last. I go '
	db	'now to seek my reward, for this has been a test of my courag'
	db	'e as well as thine. Thy reward lies beyond the door to the n'
	db	'orth. Enter the blue gate and the Amulet of Courage will be '
	db	'thine."*'
	db	00
L0456:	db	'"Well done, little human. Thou art as powerful as thou art c'
	db	'ourageous. Do not think that thou hast destroyed me, thou ha'
	db	'st merely bested me. And for this wonderous feat, I think th'
	db	'ou dost deserve a reward. I have a truly magnificent gem tha'
	db	't I would give to thee, if thy courage can but continue for '
	db	'a bit." Dracothraxus opens her mouth wide. Within, you can s'
	db	'ee a multitude of teeth, each one needle sharp. Also, near t'
	db	'he back, you see a small but brilliant blue gem. Do you reac'
	db	'h in and take it?'
	db	00
L0648:	db	'As you place your hand in the furnace that is the dragon\'s '
	db	'maw, you can\'t help but wonder if a small gem is worth the '
	db	'risk.'
	db	00
L06C4:	db	'Nevertheless, you persevere and retrieve the lovely little g'
	db	'em.'
	db	00
L0704:	db	'Just as you are about to pluck the gem literally from the ja'
	db	'ws of death, the dragon gently places it within her nest. Dr'
	db	'acothraxus closes her mouth and winks at you. "\'Twas merely'
	db	' a test of thy courage, little one."'
	db	00
L07DC:	db	'"Tis a pity thy courage goes only so far as bravery in battl'
	db	'e, and not to trust of an honorable opponent. However, thou '
	db	'hast earned thy reward, and here it is." The dragon pushes t'
	db	'he gem forward with her tongue, and removes it from her mout'
	db	'h. She then places it gently within her nest.'
	db	00
L08FA:	db	'"I go now to rest, but I shall return. The door will not ope'
	db	'n until thou hast found a way to best me for good and for al'
	db	'l. Farewell, little mortal.*'
	db	00
