L0000:	db	'This is not a valid scroll'
	db	00
L001B:	db	'From the Desk of Lord British'
	db	00
L0039:	db	'How to keep the Avatar busy for hours looking for a clue--'
	db	00
L0074:	db	'(please scroll forward)*'
	db	00
L008D:	db	'How to keep the Avatar very busy for hours looking for a clu'
	db	'e--'
	db	00
L00CD:	db	'(please scroll forward)*'
	db	00
L00E6:	db	'How to keep the Avatar very very busy for hours looking for '
	db	'a clue --'
	db	00
L012C:	db	'(please scroll forward)*'
	db	00
L0145:	db	'How to keep the Avatar very -very- very busy for hours looki'
	db	'ng for a clue --'
	db	00
L0192:	db	'(please scroll forward)*'
	db	00
L01AB:	db	'How to keep the Avatar so very -very- very incredibly busy f'
	db	'or hours looking for a clue --'
	db	00
L0206:	db	'(please scroll forward)*'
	db	00
L021F:	db	'How to keep the Avatar so very -very- absolutely unbelievabl'
	db	'y and incredibly busy for hours looking for a clue --'
	db	00
L0291:	db	'(please scroll forward)*'
	db	00
L02AA:	db	'When thou art not so busy, thou shouldst seek out Margareta '
	db	'the gypsy in Minoc and have thy fortune told!'
	db	00
L0314:	db	'Signed -  Chuckles'
	db	00
L0327:	db	'KEEP BRITANNIA CLEAN -- SEND THE GARGOYLES BACK! ~~ ~~ ~~ Pa'
	db	'id for by the Britannian Purity League'
	db	00
L038A:	db	'The cutting down of Silverleaf Trees will be done no longer '
	db	'by you. Your compliance is desired. You are thanked, Woodsma'
	db	'n.~~Salamon~~ ~~Ben, the logger'
	db	00
L0422:	db	'The cutting down of Silverleaf Trees will be done no longer '
	db	'by you. Your compliance is desired. You are thanked, Woodsma'
	db	'n.~~Salamon'
	db	00
L04A6:	db	'Bill of Punative Action for the Distribution of Waste Produc'
	db	'ts in Lock Lake~~78934979.S3, section 835~~'
	db	00
L050E:	db	'Whereby the members of the offending party shall be immersed'
	db	' in the lake, heretofore refered to as Lock Lake, up to thei'
	db	'r necks for not more than three consecutive days and not few'
	db	'er than...'
	db	00
L05CD:	db	'"Thou hast received payment. Make the delivery tonight."'
	db	00
L0606:	db	'Once the construction is complete, store the blackrock in th'
	db	'e hold of The Crown Jewel.'
	db	00
L065D:	db	'Finster - Britain (x)'
	db	00
L0673:	db	'Duncan - Buccaneer\'s Den (x)'
	db	00
L0690:	db	'Christopher - Trinsic (x)'
	db	00
L06AA:	db	'Frederico - Minoc (x)'
	db	00
L06C0:	db	'Tania - Minoc (x)'
	db	00
L06D2:	db	'Alagner - New Magincia  (x)'
	db	00
L06EE:	db	'Lord British - Britain ( )'
	db	00
L0709:	db	', the Avatar - ( )'
	db	00
L071C:	db	'The stone pedestal should be four feet high, three feet wide'
	db	' and two feet deep. Atop each of the three pedestals shall b'
	db	'e set the three receptacles: the tetrahedron, the sphere, an'
	db	'd the cube.~~All of these items for the defense mechanism of'
	db	' the portal have already been constructed by the Trinsic bla'
	db	'cksmith.'
	db	00
L0851:	db	'Crown Jewel~~Sunrise tomorrow - sail for the Isle of the Ava'
	db	'tar!'
	db	00
L0892:	db	'To tell you the amount of explosives is quite adequate to de'
	db	'stroy the altars. To remind you of the need for silence, and'
	db	' of the punishment it will help you avoid.~~--Runeb'
	db	00
L093E:	db	'The Narwhal shall be a fine, fine vessel, measuring 100 cubi'
	db	'ts from bow to stern. She shall be constructed of the finest'
	db	' Yew wood, with a ballast of thirty-seven cubits. After the '
	db	'planks are retrograded, I shall preceriprocate the bottom de'
	db	'cks to insure their verbosity.~Each bunk shall fit exactly w'
	db	'ithin the 3 foot by four 14 cubit cabin, except for the firs'
	db	't mate and sergeant\'s quarters, which will be octagnal the '
	db	'size...~~ ~~Owen of Minoc'
	db	00
L0AFB:	db	'BRITANNIAN TAX COUNCIL'
	db	00
L0B12:	db	'TAX DECLARATION'
	db	00
L0B22:	db	'To insure the proper record-keeping of thine income and spen'
	db	'ding, first replicate in triplicate the files numbered 37-A '
	db	'through 1204-W of the forms. Following each copy, compile th'
	db	'e aggregate number of expenditures and multiply by tables 3,'
	db	' 69, 106. The next involves...'
	db	00
L0C31:	db	'First thou must needs fill a crucible with metal. Then, usin'
	db	'g the bellows, make the fire as hot as possible. When the fl'
	db	'ame no longer continues to glow, thou art ready to proceed b'
	db	'y setting the crucible on the fire to melt the metal.~~ Afte'
	db	'rwards, pour the molten metal into the blade mold and let it'
	db	' cool. Be warned! The crucible is at an extremely high tempe'
	db	'rature. Do not burn thyself.~~ With the tongs, lift the cool'
	db	'ed blade from the mold. Again heat up the fire and set the b'
	db	'lade within. Be careful not to let it lose its shape though.'
	db	' Just set it in there long enough to become malleable.~~ Whe'
	db	'n it is ready, take it to the anvil and finish shaping it wi'
	db	'th the hammer. When thou hast the desired blade, find the qu'
	db	'enching barrel and plunge the sword in the cool water. It wi'
	db	'll quickly harden.~~ All that thou must needs do now is to p'
	db	'ut the pommel over the tang. It takes some doing to make a f'
	db	'ine, sturdy sword, but the finished weapon is well worth it!'
	db	00
