	db	00
L2685:	db	'Dearest Iolo,~     In Buccaneer\'s Den I came across an old '
	db	'pirate who told me he had sailed across the waters of Britan'
	db	'nia more times than I was summers old. On a gamble, I asked '
	db	'if he had ever heard of the legendary Serpent Isle. He had! '
	db	'And he even had a map that would tell how to locate the isla'
	db	'nd. I bought the map and have already begun my search. Howev'
	db	'er, I made a copy so that thou mayest follow me after thy cu'
	db	'rrent adventures have ended. I have left the copy with Lord '
	db	'British, but he promised he wouldst not give it to thee unti'
	db	'l thou hast completed thy explorations with '
	db	00
L28CD:	db	'.~~     \'Til I see thee again, my love!~     Gwenno'
	db	00
L2901:	db	'~~All is not as it seems...'
	db	00
L291D:	db	'~     Ownership of Horse and Carriage~~This writ entitles th'
	db	'e bearer to ownership and use of the wagon and its accompany'
	db	'ing horse, ____________. Misuse of this writ by those not in'
	db	' full ownership of aforementioned wagon and horse is punisha'
	db	'ble under section 7890.3D5 of the Private Ownership of Goods'
	db	' and Livestock Act, as enforced by the Britannian Tax Counci'
	db	'l.'
	db	00
L2A88:	db	'~Very well. It is agreed that we attack Lord British\'s cast'
	db	'le at the dawning of the seventh day.~~Fransisa~Corwin~ Brax'
	db	'~Athelas'
	db	00
L2B08:	db	'~     Selwyn\'s Last Will:~~'
	db	00
L2B24:	db	'     I do hearby bequeath my firedoom staff to anyone who is'
	db	' mighty and cunning enough to penetrate the defenses of my f'
	db	'ortress and slay my pet.~~'
	db	00
L2BB7:	db	'     May all who read this rot in death!~'
	db	00
L2BE1:	db	'          Selwyn'
	db	00
L2BF2:	db	'     Throne of `Change\' keeps thee at bay, but `Virtue\' sh'
	db	'all show the way!'
	db	00
L2C3E:	db	'     I have been here for more days than I am able to rememb'
	db	'er, though I have not forgotten the day I entered this forsa'
	db	'ken cave which has become my tomb. That was 2-29-0227. But m'
	db	'y food ran out long ago, and the rats are more interested in'
	db	' eating me than letting me eat them. My strength is gone, as'
	db	' is my will. If thou dost find this, please tell Mythra I lo'
	db	've her.'
	db	00
L2DAE:	db	'     --Denyel'
	db	00
L2DBC:	db	'~     Lord British\'s Last Will and Testament:~~'
	db	00
L2DEC:	db	'     Being of sound mind and body, I hereby bequeath all of '
	db	'my belongings to... Nell, my beloved chambermaid. She has ke'
	db	'pt me warm so many nights, which is more than I can say for '
	db	'most of my bloody subjects! And to our unborn child, I beque'
	db	'ath my crown. Long live the king. Or queen, whichever it sha'
	db	'll be!~~'
	db	00
L2F21:	db	'          Lord British'
	db	00
L2F38:	db	'By proclamation of Lord British this is an official document'
	db	' denoting ownership of the heretofore mentioned sailing vess'
	db	'el. Forgery of this title is prohibited under law no. 198983'
	db	'2.A5, section 809.'
	db	00
L2FFF:	db	'     DEED~~SHIP NAME: Golden Ankh~~COMPLETION DATE: 3-8-0338'
	db	'~~ INSPECTION DATE: 3-18-0338~~SHIPWRIGHT: Clint of Britain'
	db	00
L3077:	db	'Day 1: I circumvented the living statues and made it through'
	db	' the gate. Despite the long boat ride, I feel no weakness. I'
	db	' suspect the excitement of the quest gives my strength. I wi'
	db	'll rest soon.'
	db	00
L3139:	db	'Day 2: In the large room I encountered the lightening at the'
	db	' "X." Very clever that -- predicting I would not trust  the '
	db	'marking. I will not be so foolish  again.'
	db	00
L31DB:	db	'Day 3: I found a large chamber, one in which I can see fully'
	db	' its entire contents. Yet, there are invisible barriers that'
	db	' prevent me from entering.'
	db	00
L326E:	db	'Day 4: The barriers are not what I first suspected. They are'
	db	' walls. I can see the exit, and yet I cannot reach it. This '
	db	'is maddening!'
	db	00
L32F4:	db	'Day 5: I wish I had brought more rations. I did not expect t'
	db	'o be caught like this. I will starve soon if I do not find t'
	db	'he way out... and food and water!'
	db	00
L338E:	db	'Day: I am still without food and whales... I seee but cannot'
	db	'... well hilp arrive in time!? I think but am thoughtful...'
	db	00
L3406:	db	'... I have been in this wretched place for more weeks than I'
	db	' care to remember -- than I COULD remember were I to try. I '
	db	'have seen far too much in the way of deception and falsehood'
	db	'. I am forced to wonder how this maze of tunnels can demonst'
	db	'rate Truth. There is one lesson I can claim to have learned,'
	db	' thou I wonder with whom I can ever share it: I am not the A'
	db	'vatar. I wish with my last breath good luck to he... or she.'
	db	'..  who can truly claim the Avatarhood. As I lay here dying,'
	db	' I ask but one request of the finder:  remember well my stru'
	db	'g...'
	db	00
L3627:	db	'... I write this with what little hope I have left. Frenke h'
	db	'as now died -- killed by shooting balls of flame. I will att'
	db	'empt to navigate the treacherous tunnel of fire alone. Shoul'
	db	'd my quest succeed, I will emerge the Avatar. I relflect not'
	db	' upon my other destiny...'
	db	00
L3731:	db	'     This will be my last entry. My ink is all but gone, muc'
	db	'h like my will. I no longer marvel at how a man can give up,'
	db	' like the poor fool we found at the end of the invisible maz'
	db	'e. But I refuse to succumb to the call of my weary bones. I '
	db	'will trudge on.'
	db	00
L3831:	db	'       SCROLL OF INFINITY~~ artifact TalismanOfInfinity -~ i'
	db	'f Reality is Magic -~ if Locale(Artifact) is Void -~ Convex '
	db	'is FindInBritannia(ConvexLens)~ Concave is FindInBritannia(C'
	db	'oncaveLens)~ ~ if DoLightTest(Concave, Convex) -~ TalismanLi'
	db	'st is BritanniaSearch(Talisman)~ ~~ Counter is 0~ foreach Ta'
	db	'lisman in TalismanList -~ if KnowType(Talisman) is Truth -~ '
	db	'Counter is Counter and 1~ --~ if KnowType(Talisman) is Love '
	db	'-~ Counter is Counter and 1~ --~ if KnowType(Talisman) is Co'
	db	'urage -~ Counter is Counter and 1~ --~ ~ if Counter is 3 -~ '
	db	'DoVoidAccess()~ ~~ InifinityAction is Action(Instance,~ aPla'
	db	'narTravel, Britannia,~ aCallBack, TalismanOfInfinity)~ --~ i'
	db	'f Reality is PseudoScience -~ EvilEntity is EntitySearch(All'
	db	', Powerful, Evil)~ if EvilEntity -~ Check is PushReality(Evi'
	db	'lEntity)~ if not Check -~ Test("Thou shalt never see this!")'
	db	00
L3B7A:	db	'The Diary of Erethian:~~'
	db	00
L3B93:	db	'Entry #1:'
	db	00
L3B9D:	db	'     Perhaps someday I shall have the time and inclination t'
	db	'o write on this parchment, but for now it pleases me not to.'
	db	00
