L0000:	db	'Avatar'
	db	00
L0007:	db	'You see a boy who appears to be a young teen. He is dirty an'
	db	'd unkempt. He looks as if he has been crying, but he sits up'
	db	' straight and looks sharp when he sees you.'
	db	00
L00AB:	db	'"Who art thou and what dost thou want?" You realize the boy '
	db	'has a sling in hand.'
	db	00
L00FC:	db	'You face the boy and tell him who you are.'
	db	00
L0127:	db	'"So? What makes thee so special?"*'
	db	00
L014A:	db	'"The last time I heard -that- one I fell off a prehistoric c'
	db	'reature from Eodon!"'
	db	00
L019B:	db	'"Boy, this is the Avatar! '
	db	00
L01B6:	db	'Upon my word he is! He has come to help thee!"*'
	db	00
L01E6:	db	'Upon my word she is! She has come to help thee!"*'
	db	00
L0218:	db	'Then the boy narrows his eyes, studying you. He slowly lower'
	db	's his weapon, ready to act in case it\'s a trap. You admire '
	db	'the boy\'s obvious experience in dealing with strangers.'
	db	00
L02C7:	db	'You and Spark stare at each other. He is not sure what to do'
	db	'. Finally, he nods his head. "All right. I believe thee. Tho'
	db	'u dost look like paintings I have seen. I am sorry, '
	db	00
L0374:	db	'."'
	db	00
L0377:	db	'"Yes, '
	db	00
L037E:	db	'?" Spark asks. "What dost thou want?"'
	db	00
L03A4:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L03A8:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L03AF:	db	'job'
	db	00
L03B3:	db	'name'
	db	00
L03B8:	db	'key'
	db	00
L03BC:	db	'key'
	db	00
L03C0:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L03C6:	db	'join'
	db	00
L03CB:	db	'scroll'
	db	00
L03D2:	db	'medallion'
	db	00
L03DC:	db	'gold'
	db	00
L03E1:	db	'name'
	db	00
L03E6:	db	'"I have always been called Spark."'
	db	00
L0409:	db	'name'
	db	00
L040E:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0412:	db	'"I have no job. I am only fourteen, so I am just learning ho'
	db	'w to best help Father in the smithy," he says, proudly. But '
	db	'then he suddenly realizes something which terrifies him. "An'
	db	'd now that Father is dead, I am an orphan!"'
	db	00
L04F2:	db	'orphan'
	db	00
L04F9:	db	'Father'
	db	00
L0500:	db	'smithy'
	db	00
L0507:	db	'smithy'
	db	00
L050E:	db	'"Father was the best blacksmith in Britannia. People were al'
	db	'ways coming from everywhere to get him to make this and that'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L0589:	db	'smithy'
	db	00
L0590:	db	'orphan'
	db	00
L0597:	db	'"My mother died a long time ago. I can just barely remember '
	db	'her."'
	db	00
L05D9:	db	'orphan'
	db	00
L05E0:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L05E7:	db	'"I cannot believe Father is dead. And poor Inamo, too. It is'
	db	' so strange. I -dreamed- it was happening. Well, in a way.~~'
	db	'"Last night I was having a nightmare about Father. I dreamed'
	db	' that he screamed, and it woke me up. I looked around the ho'
	db	'use, but he was not in his bed. I was wide awake, so I went '
	db	'out to find him."'
	db	00
L0725:	db	'find'
	db	00
L072A:	db	'nightmare'
	db	00
L0734:	db	'Inamo'
	db	00
L073A:	db	'"I am sure thou canst find the man who killed Father!"'
	db	00
L0771:	db	'"Dost thou want me to repeat everything I know about the mur'
	db	'der?"'
	db	00
L07B3:	db	'"What dost thou want to know about?"'
	db	00
L07D8:	db	'chest'
	db	00
L07DE:	db	'key'
	db	00
L07E2:	db	'my story'
	db	00
L07EB:	db	'"All right."'
	db	00
L07F8:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L07FF:	db	'chest'
	db	00
L0805:	db	'"I am not sure if it\'s the same one, but I think I saw Fath'
	db	'er with a scroll just like the one in the chest one or two d'
	db	'ays ago. I know he was making something special for someone.'
	db	' I am fairly certain it was at his shop. As for the medallio'
	db	'n, he usually wore it. I do not know why it was in the chest'
	db	'. And the gold-- I have never seen so much gold in my life. '
	db	'I cannot imagine why father had it."'
	db	00
L0991:	db	'"Thou shouldst try opening the chest."'
	db	00
L09B8:	db	'chest'
	db	00
L09BE:	db	'my story'
	db	00
L09C7:	db	'"It is so strange. I -dreamed- it was happening. Well, in a '
	db	'way.~~"Last night I was having a nightmare about Father. I d'
	db	'reamed that he screamed, and it woke me up. I looked around '
	db	'the house, but he was not in his bed. I was wide awake, so I'
	db	' went out to find him."'
	db	00
L0ACF:	db	'my story'
	db	00
L0AD8:	db	'nightmare'
	db	00
L0AE2:	db	'find'
	db	00
L0AE7:	db	'nightmare'
	db	00
L0AF1:	db	'"I know it sounds witless, but... I dreamed that a big red-f'
	db	'aced man was watching down on everything and... He looked do'
	db	'wn... And he noticed Father... That is all I remember."'
	db	00
L0BA1:	db	'nightmare'
	db	00
L0BAB:	db	'find'
	db	00
L0BB0:	db	'"No, I did not find him. At least, not right away. But I did'
	db	' see something."'
	db	00
L0BFD:	db	'something'
	db	00
L0C07:	db	'find'
	db	00
L0C0C:	db	'something'
	db	00
L0C16:	db	'"I was in front of the stables. I saw a man and a wingless g'
	db	'argoyle running from behind the building. They ran toward th'
	db	'e dock. Then I went inside and found... Father."~~Spark\'s v'
	db	'oice falters, and he begins to sob a little.'
	db	00
L0CF6:	db	'gargoyle'
	db	00
L0CFF:	db	'man'
	db	00
L0D03:	db	'something'
	db	00
L0D0D:	db	'man'
	db	00
L0D11:	db	'"All I saw of him was that the man had a hook for a right ha'
	db	'nd."'
	db	00
L0D52:	db	'hook'
	db	00
L0D57:	db	'man'
	db	00
L0D5B:	db	'gargoyle'
	db	00
L0D64:	db	'"I cannot tell one gargoyle from another. I could not identi'
	db	'fy him, except that he had no wings."'
	db	00
L0DC6:	db	'gargoyle'
	db	00
L0DCF:	db	'hook'
	db	00
L0DD4:	db	'"Wilt thou go find the Man with the Hook? Let me help thee!"'
	db	' the boy pleads. His tears cease, and his face takes on a de'
	db	'termined, forceful look.'
	db	00
L0E65:	db	'"Take me with thee! Please! I must avenge Father\'s death! I'
	db	'f thou dost not take me with thee, I will follow thee anyway'
	db	'!"'
	db	00
L0EDF:	db	'The boy is all excited now. "I am an expert with a slingshot'
	db	'! I can strike sewer rats with almost every shot! And I am s'
	db	'mall -- I do not eat much! Please take me! Please ask me to '
	db	'join thee!"*'
	db	00
L0FA0:	db	'Iolo whispers to you. "I do not know about taking a child on'
	db	' the road with us, '
	db	00
L0FF0:	db	'."*'
	db	00
L0FF4:	db	'Suddenly, Spark lets his sling fly. His target, a small fly '
	db	'hovering above Iolo\'s head, is smacked out of the air. You '
	db	'laugh as Iolo\tyelps, jumps away, curses and runs his finger'
	db	's through his hair. '
	db	00
L10BB:	db	'Suddenly, Spark lets his sling fly. His target, a small fly '
	db	'hovering above your head, is smacked out of the air. '
	db	00
L112D:	db	'"I told thee I am good! May I join?"'
	db	00
L1152:	db	'"Hooray!" the boy leaps with delight.'
	db	00
L1178:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L117E:	db	'"Fine." The boy looks angry. "But I\'ll follow thee anyway."'
	db	00
L11BA:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L11C0:	db	'"I know thou wilt find that man."'
	db	00
L11E2:	db	'"I know thou wilt find that man."'
	db	00
L1204:	db	'hook'
	db	00
L1209:	db	'join'
	db	00
L120E:	db	'"\'Tis about time thou didst ask again!"'
	db	00
L1236:	db	'"Hooray!"'
	db	00
L1240:	db	'"Well, on second thought, it looks like too big of a crowd. '
	db	'I do not like crowds."'
	db	00
L1293:	db	'join'
	db	00
L1298:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L129E:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L12A4:	db	'"Don\'t make me go!" Spark cries. "Dost thou really want me '
	db	'to go?" He looks at you with puppy-dog eyes.'
	db	00
L130C:	db	'"Well, should I just wait here or dost thou want me to go ho'
	db	'me to Trinsic?"'
	db	00
L1358:	db	'go home'
	db	00
L1360:	db	'wait here'
	db	00
L136A:	db	'wait here'
	db	00
L1374:	db	'"All right. I shall wait here until thou dost return and ask'
	db	' me to rejoin."*'
	db	00
L13C1:	db	'Spark bows his head and murmurs, "Goodbye, then."*'
	db	00
L13F4:	db	'"Thou wilt not be sorry!"'
	db	00
L140E:	db	'Father'
	db	00
L1415:	db	'"Father was the blacksmith. I cannot believe that he has bee'
	db	'n murdered! He had no enemies that I know of. Unless it was '
	db	'The Fellowship."'
	db	00
L149E:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L14A9:	db	'Father'
	db	00
L14B0:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L14BB:	db	'"Well, at first they harassed Father and me when they came a'
	db	'round asking us to join. I suppose they do good things. Many'
	db	' people like them. Father eventually joined the group after '
	db	'he went to Britain and took one of their tests."'
	db	00
L15A0:	db	'tests'
	db	00
L15A6:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L15B1:	db	'tests'
	db	00
L15B7:	db	'"I do not know anything about them. I never took one. Maybe '
	db	'thou shouldst ask the man at the Fellowship Branch. Klog."'
	db	00
L162E:	db	'Klog'
	db	00
L1633:	db	'branch'
	db	00
L163A:	db	'tests'
	db	00
L1640:	db	'branch'
	db	00
L1647:	db	'"The Fellowship has branches all over Britannia."'
	db	00
L1679:	db	'branch'
	db	00
L1680:	db	'Klog'
	db	00
L1685:	db	'"He is the head of the Fellowship Branch here in Trinsic. He'
	db	' and Father got into an argument a week ago when Klog and tw'
	db	'o of his friends came over to talk with Father."'
	db	00
L172E:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L1736:	db	'argument'
	db	00
L173F:	db	'Klog'
	db	00
L1744:	db	'argument'
	db	00
L174D:	db	'"I don\'t know what it was about. Perhaps thou shouldst ask '
	db	'Klog."'
	db	00
L178F:	db	'argument'
	db	00
L1798:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L17A0:	db	'"I do not remember what they look like. I did not recognize '
	db	'them.\tThey were most likely some other members of The Fello'
	db	'wship."'
	db	00
L181F:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L1827:	db	'key'
	db	00
L182B:	db	'"That key opened my Father\'s chest, did it not?"'
	db	00
L185C:	db	'"That looks like the key to Father\'s chest. I wondered wher'
	db	'e it was!"'
	db	00
L18A2:	db	'"What key? Dost thou have the key to Father\'s chest? Where '
	db	'is it?"'
	db	00
L18E5:	db	'key'
	db	00
L18E9:	db	'gold'
	db	00
L18EE:	db	'The boy\'s eyes widen. "I had no idea that Father had that m'
	db	'uch money hidden away!"'
	db	00
L1941:	db	'"I suppose I could give it to thee if thou art going to look'
	db	' for those who killed my Father!"'
	db	00
L199F:	db	'gold'
	db	00
L19A4:	db	'medallion'
	db	00
L19AE:	db	'"Father was a member of The Fellowship. I don\'t know why th'
	db	'e medallion was in the chest -- he usually wore it."'
	db	00
L1A1E:	db	'medallion'
	db	00
L1A28:	db	'scroll'
	db	00
L1A2F:	db	'"I am not sure if it\'s the same one, but I think I saw Fath'
	db	'er with a scroll just like that one or two days ago. I know '
	db	'he was making something special for someone. I am fairly cer'
	db	'tain it was at his shop."'
	db	00
L1AFC:	db	'shop'
	db	00
L1B01:	db	'scroll'
	db	00
L1B08:	db	'shop'
	db	00
L1B0D:	db	'"It\'s in the southwest corner of town."'
	db	00
L1B35:	db	'shop'
	db	00
L1B3A:	db	'Inamo'
	db	00
L1B40:	db	'"He was a very nice gargoyle. He helped Father a lot and did'
	db	' tasks in the stables. I cannot think why anyone would want '
	db	'to kill him!"'
	db	00
L1BC6:	db	'Inamo'
	db	00
L1BCC:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1BD0:	db	'"All right, I will speak with thee later."*'
	db	00
