L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'"I am sorry, I do not join thieves."'
	db	00
L0032:	db	'"All right, I suppose thou hast learned thy lesson. I shall '
	db	'rejoin."'
	db	00
L0077:	db	'Amber'
	db	00
L007D:	db	'settle down'
	db	00
L0089:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L008F:	db	'join'
	db	00
L0094:	db	'Your old friend Shamino stands before you and you marvel tha'
	db	't he has finally progressed into what some might call \'midd'
	db	'le age\'.'
	db	00
L0114:	db	'"Yes, '
	db	00
L011B:	db	'?" Shamino asks.'
	db	00
L012C:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0131:	db	'Your friend looks at you like you have lost your head. "\'Ti'
	db	's Shamino. -Sha-mi-no-."'
	db	00
L0185:	db	'name'
	db	00
L018A:	db	'job'
	db	00
L018E:	db	'"I should hope \'twould be adventuring with thee! I am weary'
	db	' of loitering about Britain. There is much we could be accom'
	db	'plishing! Where hast thou been, anyway?"'
	db	00
L022E:	db	'"But please tell me what brings thee here!"'
	db	00
L025A:	db	'murder in Trinsic'
	db	00
L026C:	db	'accomplishing'
	db	00
L027A:	db	'Britain'
	db	00
L0282:	db	'accomplishing'
	db	00
L0290:	db	'"Well, I do not know if thou art aware, but we are having ma'
	db	'ny problems with magic in general, and with the Moongates."'
	db	00
L0308:	db	'accomplishing'
	db	00
L0316:	db	'Moongates'
	db	00
L0320:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L0326:	db	'Britain'
	db	00
L032E:	db	'"Yes, I have been in Britain as of late, attempting to find '
	db	'work. Thou dost know that adventuring comes around too infre'
	db	'quently. One must find -other- diversions. Which reminds me.'
	db	'.. I have thy pocketwatch."'
	db	00
L03FE:	db	'Britain'
	db	00
L0406:	db	'pocketwatch'
	db	00
L0412:	db	'diversions'
	db	00
L041D:	db	'pocketwatch'
	db	00
L0429:	db	'"Thou didst leave it when thou didst last visit Britannia. H'
	db	'ere\tit is."'
	db	00
L0471:	db	'Shamino hands you the pocketwatch.'
	db	00
L0494:	db	'"Oops. Thine hands are too full to take it. Ask me about it '
	db	'later."'
	db	00
L04D8:	db	'"I already gave thee the pocketwatch, '
	db	00
L04FF:	db	'. I hope thou didst not lose it again!"'
	db	00
L0527:	db	'pocketwatch'
	db	00
L0533:	db	'diversions'
	db	00
L053E:	db	'"The usual. I do not see our old friends often, and Lord Bri'
	db	'tish rarely finds work for me. I certainly have no time\tfor'
	db	' wenching or drinking -- I have grown up a bit."*'
	db	00
L05E7:	db	'diversions'
	db	00
L05F2:	db	'"Ahem, I have heard something about an actress, no?"*'
	db	00
L0628:	db	'"What dost thou know of it?"*'
	db	00
L0646:	db	'"'
	db	00
L0648:	db	', ask him about \'Amber\'."*'
	db	00
L0663:	db	'"Thou art a swine, Iolo."'
	db	00
L067D:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L068A:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L0692:	db	'Amber'
	db	00
L0698:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L06A5:	db	'"I suggest that thou proceed immediately to see him!"*'
	db	00
L06DC:	db	'"I am glad I do not look as aged as -he- does!"'
	db	00
L070C:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0719:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L0721:	db	'"Thou dost mean Iolo and Dupre, I presume?"'
	db	00
L074D:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L0755:	db	'Dupre'
	db	00
L075B:	db	'Iolo'
	db	00
L0760:	db	'Iolo'
	db	00
L0765:	db	'"Dost thou mean that miserable excuse for an archer?"*'
	db	00
L079C:	db	'"Watch what thou dost say, scoundrel!"*'
	db	00
L07C4:	db	'"Yes, that\'s Iolo!"'
	db	00
L07D8:	db	'"Surely he is around somewhere. Where didst thou last leave '
	db	'him?"'
	db	00
L081A:	db	'Iolo'
	db	00
L081F:	db	'Dupre'
	db	00
L0825:	db	'"Dost thou mean that incorrigible wencher and drunkard?"*'
	db	00
L085F:	db	'"Do not forget that my mere thumb can squash in thy face lik'
	db	'e a marshmallow."*'
	db	00
L08AE:	db	'"Yes, that\'s Dupre!"*'
	db	00
L08C4:	db	'"That\'s -Sir- Dupre to thee!"*'
	db	00
L08E3:	db	'"Sir Dupuke? Didst thou say Sir Dupuke?"*'
	db	00
L090D:	db	'"Du-pre-!"*'
	db	00
L0919:	db	'"Pardon -me-, Sir Dupuke!"*'
	db	00
L0935:	db	'"I\'m not going to listen to this anymore."*'
	db	00
L0961:	db	'"I believe he is in Jhelom."'
	db	00
L097E:	db	'"He must be around somewhere!"'
	db	00
L099D:	db	'Dupre'
	db	00
L09A3:	db	'join'
	db	00
L09A8:	db	'Shamino looks relieved. "I am -so- glad thou didst ask me th'
	db	'at." He gathers his gear and prepares to follow you.'
	db	00
L0A19:	db	'"Hmmm. I do not like big crowds. I shall wait until thy grou'
	db	'p is smaller before joining."'
	db	00
L0A73:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L0A79:	db	'join'
	db	00
L0A7E:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L0A84:	db	'"Hmmm. Dost thou merely want me to wait here or dost thou wa'
	db	'nt me to go home?"'
	db	00
L0AD3:	db	'go home'
	db	00
L0ADB:	db	'wait here'
	db	00
L0AE5:	db	'wait here'
	db	00
L0AEF:	db	'"Very well. I shall await thy return."*'
	db	00
L0B17:	db	'"I really hate to, but if thou dost insist." Shamino\tgrudgi'
	db	'ngly gathers his belongings.*'
	db	00
L0B70:	db	'murder in Trinsic'
	db	00
L0B82:	db	'Shamino listens as you tell him the story. "I would be honor'
	db	'ed to join and help thee in investigating this matter."'
	db	00
L0BF6:	db	'murder in Trinsic'
	db	00
L0C08:	db	'Moongates'
	db	00
L0C12:	db	'"I am confounded by their inability to function properly."'
	db	00
L0C4D:	db	'"\'Tis a pity that thou art marooned here."'
	db	00
L0C78:	db	'Moongates'
	db	00
L0C82:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L0C88:	db	'"Magic all over Britannia seems to be disturbed. Say, dost t'
	db	'hou remember Nicodemus in the great forest? He has gone mad '
	db	'and is terribly silly. Perhaps we should visit him."'
	db	00
L0D35:	db	'"It does not work well. I do not understand it."'
	db	00
L0D66:	db	'"It will probably work extremely well now, '
	db	00
L0D92:	db	'."'
	db	00
L0D95:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L0D9B:	db	'Amber'
	db	00
L0DA1:	db	'You see a light shine in Shamino\'s eyes as you mention her '
	db	'name. He is obviously smitten.~~"She is an actress I know."'
	db	00
L0E18:	db	'Amber'
	db	00
L0E1E:	db	'settle down'
	db	00
L0E2A:	db	'"That woman! She cannot understand that I must have mine adv'
	db	'enturing! I cannot settle down. -Yet-! Soon maybe."~~Shamino'
	db	' looks concerned. "I have grown up. A bit."'
	db	00
L0ECE:	db	'settle down'
	db	00
L0EDA:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0EDE:	db	'Shamino bows slightly.*'
	db	00
