L0000:	db	'Abraham'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'Elizabeth'
	db	00
	db	00
L0013:	db	's'
	db	00
L0015:	db	'valiant warrior'
	db	00
L0025:	db	'noble enchanter'
	db	00
L0035:	db	'hermits'
	db	00
L003D:	db	'slime'
	db	00
L0043:	db	'foxes'
	db	00
L0049:	db	'harpies'
	db	00
L0051:	db	'"We need not be concerned about these bees, so long as we ha'
	db	've a number of my trusty arrows."'
	db	00
L00AF:	db	'bees'
	db	00
L00B4:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L00BF:	db	'"Greetings, traveller'
	db	00
L00D5:	db	'."'
	db	00
L00D8:	db	'lowly deceiver'
	db	00
L00E7:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L00EB:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00EF:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00F4:	db	'introduce'
	db	00
	db	00
L00FF:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0104:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0109:	db	'"I am Tseramed the woodsman. Thou art a '
	db	00
L0132:	db	'."'
	db	00
L0135:	db	'"I am called Tseramed. Art thou Fellowship members? How art '
	db	'thou called?"'
	db	00
L017F:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L018A:	db	'Avatar'
	db	00
L0191:	db	'Avatar'
	db	00
L0198:	db	'Avatar'
	db	00
L019F:	db	'"The Avatar! This is a strange chance. Tell me Avatar, by wh'
	db	'at name art thou called?"'
	db	00
L01F5:	db	'"Well met, '
	db	00
L0201:	db	'"'
	db	00
L0203:	db	'Thy demeanor is noble.'
	db	00
L021A:	db	'Perhaps thou couldst introduce me to thy companions?"'
	db	00
L0250:	db	'introduce'
	db	00
L025A:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0265:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0270:	db	'"I do not trust The Fellowship, and most especially '
	db	00
L02A5:	db	'."'
	db	00
L02A8:	db	'"I have no love for The Fellowship. We shall speak of it whe'
	db	'n I know thee better."'
	db	00
L02FB:	db	'"Yes. Perhaps I am addressing the illustrious '
	db	00
L032A:	db	'?"'
	db	00
L032D:	db	'"Not long ago The Fellowship began to spread its influence t'
	db	'hroughout Britannia.'
	db	00
L037E:	db	'"In their early days they attracted many bright and enthusia'
	db	'stic young people, among them my love, Lady M.'
	db	00
L03E9:	db	'A woman so intelligent could not help but rise in their rank'
	db	's. Her direct superior was '
	db	00
L0441:	db	'.'
	db	00
L0443:	db	'One black evening she fell gravely ill. According to friends'
	db	' of mine, '
	db	00
L048A:	db	' forbade her to visit the local healer. By the time I learne'
	db	'd of this, she had already passed away.'
	db	00
L04EE:	db	'She rests now forever in the Yew graveyard, may her sleep be'
	db	' peaceful. I searched the land for '
	db	00
L054E:	db	', but never found my quarry. In fact, it seems that every ti'
	db	'me I near my prey, they have already vanished! My search sha'
	db	'll never be truly over."'
	db	00
L05DF:	db	'Lady M.'
	db	00
L05E7:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
	db	00
L05EC:	db	'thou dost tarnish the title of Avatar!'
	db	00
L0613:	db	'"Knave, '
	db	00
L061C:	db	' I have not forgotten thy wrong doing, nor the evil crime th'
	db	'at followed it.'
	db	00
L0668:	db	'Oh soul as black as pitch!"'
	db	00
L0684:	db	'Lady M.'
	db	00
L068C:	db	'Lady M.'
	db	00
L0694:	db	'"Youth is hers forever."'
	db	00
L06AD:	db	'job'
	db	00
L06B1:	db	'"I travel with thee, '
	db	00
L06C7:	db	', to aid thee with my wood craft."'
	db	00
L06EA:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L06F1:	db	'"I am but a humble woodsman. I garner my living from the for'
	db	'est and find knowledge in its depths.'
	db	00
L0753:	db	'I have explored all this region."'
	db	00
L0775:	db	'knowledge'
	db	00
L077F:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L0786:	db	'"As I said, my woodcraft encompasses all this forest, even t'
	db	'he caves in the mountain."'
	db	00
L07DD:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L07E4:	db	'caves'
	db	00
L07EA:	db	'introduce'
	db	00
L07F4:	db	'introduce'
	db	00
L07FE:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0809:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L0810:	db	'secret places'
	db	00
L081E:	db	'caves'
	db	00
L0824:	db	'knowledge'
	db	00
L082E:	db	'Perhaps introductions are in order first.'
	db	00
L0858:	db	'We may speak more after introductions...'
	db	00
L0881:	db	'"'
	db	00
L0883:	db	'"'
	db	00
L0885:	db	'introduce'
	db	00
L088F:	db	'"The forest is a wild place, but tamed somewhat in recent ye'
	db	'ars. Within, '
	db	00
L08D9:	db	', thou mayest still find creatures spoken of only in legend.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L0917:	db	'creatures'
	db	00
L0921:	db	'"North of my hut is a deep bore-hole into the mountains. Wit'
	db	'hin live bees of a size to rival sheep, or hounds. Their win'
	db	'gs stir up leaves as they fly, and they humm with a noise to'
	db	' make men flee in fear."'
	db	00
L09EE:	db	'"Some have entered, never to return. Perhaps they are there '
	db	'still... Death is greedy, and holds a fate for those of like'
	db	' intent."'
	db	00
L0A70:	db	'death'
	db	00
L0A76:	db	'bees'
	db	00
L0A7B:	db	'mountains'
	db	00
L0A85:	db	'knowledge'
	db	00
L0A8F:	db	'"Many years have I dwelt by the mountains. Many spans have v'
	db	'anished under my roaming feet. Into the depths of the dark s'
	db	'wamp I have gone, and to the heights of the mountains. I kno'
	db	'w the trees of the forest, and the secret places in the eart'
	db	'h."'
	db	00
L0B83:	db	'secret places'
	db	00
L0B91:	db	'swamp'
	db	00
L0B97:	db	'mountains'
	db	00
L0BA1:	db	'swamp'
	db	00
L0BA7:	db	'swamp'
	db	00
L0BAD:	db	'"North of the mountain spur is a dense swamp. Killing slime '
	db	'[lurk within, guarding a clear spring. All about the water i'
	db	's foul and noisome.'
	db	00
L0C39:	db	'Into thy boots the foul concoction will seep, bringing on na'
	db	'usea and dizziness. The wise traveller wears swamp boots in '
	db	'such places.'
	db	00
L0CBE:	db	'East, North, and West that mire is drained. Through Yew and '
	db	'past the Abbey the westward river flows. The others both ben'
	db	'd north into the sea."'
	db	00
L0D4D:	db	'sea'
	db	00
L0D51:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L0D57:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
L0D5B:	db	'slime'
	db	00
L0D61:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L0D67:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L0D6D:	db	'"Empath Abbey is its proper name '
	db	00
L0D8F:	db	'. They practice ancient arts there, the eldest being the fer'
	db	'mentation and distillation of spirits. Demand for their prod'
	db	'ucts is high in Yew."'
	db	00
L0E1D:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
L0E21:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
L0E25:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
L0E29:	db	'"Citizens of a reclusive nature feel at peace there. Within '
	db	'the forest lie its buildings, many so grown-over as to seem '
	db	'a part of the wood."'
	db	00
L0EB6:	db	'"East of my dwelling the wood is thick, but a woodcrafty tra'
	db	'veller may find the houses there."'
	db	00
L0F15:	db	'sea'
	db	00
L0F19:	db	'sea'
	db	00
L0F1D:	db	'"The sea!  Its waves sooth a rough mood, but its fury is unr'
	db	'ivaled. Ask those who live upon it! A gift it is, to live by'
	db	' it and reap its natural harvest. I cast in a line when I ma'
	db	'y.'
	db	00
L0FD4:	db	'Dost thou wonder what mysteries the sea must hold?"'
	db	00
L1008:	db	'"I also wonder. But the doings of those who travel upon it a'
	db	're more familiar to me. I have seen pirates land upon the no'
	db	'rthern coast."'
	db	00
L108F:	db	'pirates'
	db	00
L1097:	db	'"Perhaps thou art not as fond of the sea as I..."'
	db	00
L10C9:	db	'pirates'
	db	00
L10D1:	db	'pirates'
	db	00
L10D9:	db	'"Perhaps they land to cache their booty in the forest. I hav'
	db	'e never followed them."'
	db	00
L112D:	db	'mountains'
	db	00
L1137:	db	'"Vaulting in from the coast looms a narrow spine. Dangerous '
	db	'and sharp rear the crags of those mountains. Caves there hol'
	db	'd danger, and death for the unwary."'
	db	00
L11D4:	db	'death'
	db	00
L11DA:	db	'caves'
	db	00
L11E0:	db	'death'
	db	00
L11E6:	db	'death'
	db	00
L11EC:	db	'"Death for the greedy. Death for any who steal from the dwel'
	db	'lers in the caves."'
	db	00
L123C:	db	'caves'
	db	00
L1242:	db	'creatures'
	db	00
L124C:	db	'creatures'
	db	00
L1256:	db	'"Aye. Such as would devour the unwary and pick bones dry. In'
	db	' the forest are harpies, and slime on the margins of the swa'
	db	'mp, and bees in the caves.'
	db	00
L12E9:	db	'"Good game live also in the forest: Foxes and the like."'
	db	00
L1322:	db	'bees'
	db	00
L1327:	db	'harpies'
	db	00
L132F:	db	'foxes'
	db	00
L1335:	db	'slime'
	db	00
L133B:	db	'harpies'
	db	00
L1343:	db	'harpies'
	db	00
L134B:	db	'"Harpies! To battle! Let us slay them at once!"'
	db	00
L137B:	db	'"A malformed flying horror. Thou wouldst not want to meet on'
	db	'e."'
	db	00
L13BB:	db	'slime'
	db	00
L13C1:	db	'"A dangerous organism is the greenish slime. Acidic to touch'
	db	', it will hurl pseudopods at its prey from three paces.'
	db	00
L1435:	db	'"Never sleeping, it has no mind and is composed in the main '
	db	'of\tpoisonous substances. It engulfs and devours hapless ani'
	db	'mals voraciously."'
	db	00
L14BF:	db	'"Attack it with flame! Slime has no defense against it."'
	db	00
L14F8:	db	'foxes'
	db	00
L14FE:	db	'  See how lustrous is the coat of that fox.'
	db	00
L152A:	db	'"Cunning is the fox, and shy of humans. We shall never belon'
	db	'g to the forest as they do.'
	db	00
L1582:	db	'"'
	db	00
L1584:	db	'bees'
	db	00
L1589:	db	'"Bees such as these may be tamed with my special arrows!"'
	db	00
L15C3:	db	'arrows'
	db	00
L15CA:	db	'"Such bees as thou hast never seen! Large as a wolf they are'
	db	', with wings stretching over a span in length.'
	db	00
L1635:	db	'A creature stung by them will pass into a deep, death-like s'
	db	'leep."'
	db	00
L1678:	db	'"I have hunted them on many occasions, for I use their poiso'
	db	'n on my arrows. And I like their honey. Perhaps together we '
	db	'might journey into the cave for some?"'
	db	00
L1717:	db	'arrows'
	db	00
L171E:	db	'join'
	db	00
L1723:	db	'arrows'
	db	00
L172A:	db	'arrows'
	db	00
L1731:	db	'"I fashion my arrows from the stingers of giant bees. With t'
	db	'hem one may put a foe to sleep."'
	db	00
	db	00
L178F:	db	'Shall I fashion these stingers into arrows?'
	db	00
L17BB:	db	'If thou wouldst like, I would be happy to give thee a dozen '
	db	'of my special arrows. Art thou interested?'
	db	00
	db	00
	db	00
	db	00
L1825:	db	's'
	db	00
L1827:	db	'"Use them with care, for even a scratch may put one to sleep'
	db	'!" he says, handing you '
	db	00
L187C:	db	' arrow'
	db	00
L1883:	db	'.'
	db	00
L1885:	db	'"Perhaps when thou art carrying less I can give them to thee'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L18C4:	db	'"Very well, '
	db	00
L18D1:	db	'."'
	db	00
L18D4:	db	'join'
	db	00
L18D9:	db	'join'
	db	00
L18DE:	db	'"I would be honored, '
	db	00
L18F4:	db	'."'
	db	00
L18F7:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L1902:	db	'"\'Twould appear, '
	db	00
L1914:	db	', that thou already hast more than enough travelling compani'
	db	'ons."'
	db	00
L1956:	db	'leave'
	db	00
L195C:	db	'"Dost thou want me to wait here or should I go home?"'
	db	00
L1992:	db	'go home'
	db	00
L199A:	db	'wait here'
	db	00
L19A4:	db	'wait here'
	db	00
L19AE:	db	'"Very well! I shall wait for thee!"*'
	db	00
L19D3:	db	'"Very well, '
	db	00
L19E0:	db	'. Fare thee well."*'
	db	00
L19F4:	db	'hermits'
	db	00
L19FC:	db	'"Speaking of caves and mountains, there are some who dwell n'
	db	'ear, or perhaps in, the cave of bees. They are hermits."'
	db	00
L1A71:	db	'bees'
	db	00
L1A76:	db	'hermits'
	db	00
L1A7E:	db	'"One day I glimpsed a man and a woman deep within the cave a'
	db	's I was hunting. Since then I have seen them twice. I believ'
	db	'e they are former citizens of Yew, though I do not know how '
	db	'they live in harmony with the bees."'
	db	00
L1B57:	db	'"These are the people I saw!"'
	db	00
L1B75:	db	'bees'
	db	00
L1B7A:	db	'"These people are the hermits I spoke of before."'
	db	00
L1BAC:	db	'"Perhaps those hermits are still living in the cave."'
	db	00
L1BE2:	db	'"This puts me in mind of a story. Wouldst thou like to hear '
	db	'it?"'
	db	00
L1C23:	db	'"One day while walking along the edge of the swamp I happene'
	db	'd upon a strange sight. A fox was held at bay on a small hil'
	db	'lock in the midst of the swamp, and all about the hillock wr'
	db	'ithed green slime.'
	db	00
L1CEA:	db	'Slowly the slime crept up toward the fox, when suddenly the '
	db	'fox trotted directly across the surface of the ooze!'
	db	00
L1D5B:	db	'Unharmed, the fox dashed off into the wood, leaving the slim'
	db	'e writhing behind. By this I guess that the victims of slime'
	db	' are those caught sleeping, or unaware."'
	db	00
L1DFC:	db	'"Perhaps another time."'
	db	00
L1E14:	db	'slime'
	db	00
L1E1A:	db	'foxes'
	db	00
L1E20:	db	'bees'
	db	00
L1E25:	db	'caves'
	db	00
L1E2B:	db	'secret places'
	db	00
L1E39:	db	'death'
	db	00
L1E3F:	db	'mountains'
	db	00
L1E49:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L1E50:	db	'join'
	db	00
L1E55:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1E59:	db	'"Thy pardon, '
	db	00
L1E67:	db	', but thy visage brings to my mind a statue that I once saw.'
	db	'  \'Twas a likeness of the ancient hero known as the Avatar.'
	db	00
L1EDF:	db	'Art thou not that same honorable soul?"'
	db	00
L1F07:	db	'That sculptor did thee justice.'
	db	00
L1F27:	db	'Thou art more fair by far than any likeness in stone could p'
	db	'ortray.'
	db	00
L1F6B:	db	'"Noble hero, it is an honor to make thine aquaintance. '
	db	00
L1FA3:	db	'"'
	db	00
L1FA5:	db	'"I must be mistaken. Farewell."'
	db	00
L1FC5:	db	'"^'
	db	00
L1FC8:	db	', if it pleases thee, I would be honored to travel with thee'
	db	'. I have skill in arms, and I can offer my knowledge and woo'
	db	'd craft to thee..."'
	db	00
L2054:	db	'join'
	db	00
L2059:	db	'"\'Til next time, '
	db	00
