L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L000B:	db	'job'
	db	00
L000F:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0014:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0020:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L002B:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0030:	db	'You see a salty old sailor who reeks of tobacco.'
	db	00
L0061:	db	'"Yes, matey?" Gargan asks, coughing.'
	db	00
L0086:	db	'name'
	db	00
L008B:	db	'"My name is Gargan."~He sniffs loudly.'
	db	00
L00B2:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00B7:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00BB:	db	'"I am the Trinsic shipwright. If thou wouldst like to know a'
	db	'bout a ship or a sextant, just say so."'
	db	00
L011F:	db	'Gargan coughs.'
	db	00
L012E:	db	'sextant'
	db	00
L0136:	db	'ship'
	db	00
L013B:	db	'ship'
	db	00
L0140:	db	'"Thou dost want to buy a ship?" the old man asks, smiling. ('
	db	'Apparently not too many folks buy ships these days.)~"My shi'
	db	'ps are sturdy and well built. They may not be built by Owen,'
	db	' but they are fine vessels! But thou must first purchase a d'
	db	'eed."'
	db	00
L0236:	db	'Gargan wipes his runny nose on his sleeve.'
	db	00
L0261:	db	'ship'
	db	00
L0266:	db	'deed'
	db	00
L026B:	db	'Owen'
	db	00
L0270:	db	'sextant'
	db	00
L0278:	db	'"Well, ye\'ll have to come to the shop when it is is open."'
	db	00
L02B3:	db	'"I sell sextants for 80 gold. Want one?"~Gargan clears his t'
	db	'hroat.'
	db	00
L02F6:	db	'"Here ye are!"'
	db	00
L0305:	db	'"Thine arms are too full to carry the sextant!"~Gargan sneez'
	db	'es.'
	db	00
L0345:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough gold, sailor." ~Gargan sneezes.'
	db	00
L0380:	db	'"Suit thyself."~Gargan sneezes.'
	db	00
L03A0:	db	'sextant'
	db	00
L03A8:	db	'Owen'
	db	00
L03AD:	db	'"Thou hast not heard of Owen? Finest shipwright in the land.'
	db	' He lives in Minoc."~Gargan coughs.'
	db	00
L040D:	db	'Owen'
	db	00
L0412:	db	'deed'
	db	00
L0417:	db	'"Well, ye\'ll have to come to the shop when it is open."'
	db	00
L044F:	db	'"I already sold thee the deed to \'The Scaly Eel\'! It was t'
	db	'he only ship I had!"'
	db	00
L049E:	db	'Gargan coughs loudly.'
	db	00
L04B4:	db	'"The deed I can sell thee is for the ship \'The Scaly Eel.'
	db	'\' It goes for 600 gold. Interested?"'
	db	00
L0512:	db	'"All right, then!" the sailor replies. He hands you the deed'
	db	' and takes your gold.~Gargan sneezes.'
	db	00
L0574:	db	'"Thou\'rt already carrying enough to sink a galleon, '
	db	00
L05A9:	db	'! If thou wilt leave something behind, mayhaps thou wilt be '
	db	'able to sail, and I will be glad, indeed, to sell thee the d'
	db	'eed."~Gargan sneezes.'
	db	00
L0637:	db	'"Sorry, matey," Gargan says. "Thou dost not have enough gold'
	db	'!"~Gargan sneezes.'
	db	00
L0686:	db	'"Some other time, then," the sailor shrugs, disappointed.~Ga'
	db	'rgan sneezes.'
	db	00
L06D0:	db	'deed'
	db	00
L06D5:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L06DC:	db	'"I heard about that. Terrible thing to happen. Can\'t say I '
	db	'saw or heard anything, though."~Gargan coughs, clears his th'
	db	'roat loudly, then spits.'
	db	00
L076C:	db	'"Ooooh, yuck!"'
	db	00
L077B:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L0782:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L078E:	db	'"Yes, that ship was docked overnight." He consults his log. '
	db	'"She sailed for Britain at sunrise. I do not recall seeing a'
	db	'nyone get on or off."~Gargan snorts and coughs a couple of t'
	db	'imes.'
	db	00
L0848:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0854:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0859:	db	'"Matey, I have always seen pirates and sailors with peglegs '
	db	'and hooks. If thou hast seen one, thou hast seen another." B'
	db	'ut the man suddenly frowns. "Hmm. Now that thou dost mention'
	db	' it, I -did- see a man with a hook late last night after sun'
	db	'down. I was leaving the shop and saw him outside. There was '
	db	'a wingless gargoyle with him. They were walking east."'
	db	00
L09BC:	db	'Gargan sneezes, then coughs a couple of times.'
	db	00
L09EB:	db	'"I told thee! It was him!"'
	db	00
L0A06:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0A0B:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0A16:	db	'"I am too old to pay attention to them."~Gargan wipes his ru'
	db	'nny nose on his sleeve.'
	db	00
L0A6A:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0A75:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0A79:	db	'"May thy day have smooth sailing," the sailor starts to say,'
	db	' but a coughing spasm interrupts him.*'
	db	00
