L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see your old friend Nystul, now a decrepit old man in ma'
	db	'ge\'s robes. He seems lost in thought, far away.'
	db	00
L0079:	db	'"Do I know thee?" Nystul asks.'
	db	00
L0098:	db	'"Yes, Avatar?" Nystul asks.'
	db	00
L00B4:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00B9:	db	'The mage looks confused a moment. "My name is Nystul? Yes, t'
	db	'hat is it!"'
	db	00
L0101:	db	'"Why, \'tis Nystul!"'
	db	00
L0115:	db	'name'
	db	00
L011A:	db	'job'
	db	00
L011E:	db	'"Well, I used to perform quite a bit of magic," he says apol'
	db	'ogetically. "At least... I -think- I used to do so. There is'
	db	' a man named Lord British, I think. I work for him."'
	db	00
L01CB:	db	'"I am Lord British\'s personal mage!"'
	db	00
L01F0:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L01FD:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L0203:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L0209:	db	'"Sometimes the magic works, sometimes it doth not." He waves'
	db	' his hand, and drops his wand. "Oops!" he cries, as he bends'
	db	' to pick it up.'
	db	00
L0291:	db	'"Art thou sure this man is not really the jester?"'
	db	00
L02C4:	db	'"Anyway, as I was saying, uhm, what was I saying? Oh yes. Ma'
	db	'gic. I can still sell thee some spells or reagents if thou w'
	db	'ouldst like."'
	db	00
L034A:	db	'"The magic is much better now. My spells all work very nicel'
	db	'y. I thank thee, Avatar, for clearing the ether. Interested '
	db	'in any spells or reagents?"'
	db	00
L03DE:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L03E4:	db	'reagents'
	db	00
L03ED:	db	'spells'
	db	00
L03F4:	db	'spells'
	db	00
L03FB:	db	'"Dost thou wish to buy some spells?"'
	db	00
L0420:	db	'"Oh. Never mind, then."'
	db	00
L0438:	db	'reagents'
	db	00
L0441:	db	'"Dost thou wish to buy some reagents?"'
	db	00
L0468:	db	'"Oh. Never mind, then."'
	db	00
L0480:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L048D:	db	'"Lord who? Dost thou mean that old man who sometimes sits on'
	db	' the throne?"'
	db	00
L04D7:	db	'"He is the greatest ruler this land has ever known and I am '
	db	'proud to serve him."'
	db	00
L0528:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0535:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0539:	db	'"Are we going somewhere?"*'
	db	00
L0554:	db	'"Goodbye, Avatar. Do come see us again soon."*'
	db	00
