L0000:	db	'You are wary of conversing with that trickster Chuckles, but'
	db	' decide to anyway.'
	db	00
L004F:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0053:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0057:	db	'name'
	db	00
L005C:	db	'"I will speak if thou dost play The Game, friend," Chuckles '
	db	'says.'
	db	00
L009E:	db	'Game'
	db	00
L00A3:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L00A7:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00AB:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00B0:	db	'"I must not say my name, lest I break the rule of The Game!"'
	db	00
L00ED:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00F2:	db	'Game'
	db	00
L00F7:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00FB:	db	'"I was, am, and shall be the Court...Fool! I could give thee'
	db	' a clue if I wish, but for now my job is to play The Game."'
	db	00
L0173:	db	'Game'
	db	00
L0178:	db	'clue'
	db	00
L017D:	db	'"Art thou sure thou canst play The Game?"'
	db	00
L01A7:	db	'"Thou must play The Game to get the clue!"'
	db	00
L01D2:	db	'"Oops. I did give thee one!"'
	db	00
L01EF:	db	'clue'
	db	00
L01F4:	db	'Game'
	db	00
L01F9:	db	'"Thou must play The Game if thou dost want to speak with me.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L0237:	db	'Explain it'
	db	00
L0242:	db	'I know The Game'
	db	00
L0252:	db	'What are the rules?'
	db	00
L0266:	db	'I don\'t understand'
	db	00
L0279:	db	'Game'
	db	00
L027E:	db	'I don\'t understand'
	db	00
L0291:	db	'I don\'t understand'
	db	00
L02A4:	db	'Explain it'
	db	00
L02AF:	db	'Explain it'
	db	00
L02BA:	db	'What are the rules?'
	db	00
L02CE:	db	'"Thou must just learn The Game and then jump in and play it!'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L030C:	db	'What are the rules?'
	db	00
L0320:	db	'I know The Game'
	db	00
L0330:	db	'"Then just play it!"'
	db	00
L0345:	db	'I know the Game'
	db	00
L0355:	db	'Of what do we speak?'
	db	00
L036A:	db	'About what do we talk?'
	db	00
L0381:	db	'What do we converse about?'
	db	00
L039C:	db	'Of what do we speak?'
	db	00
L03B1:	db	'"Of what thou wouldst like."'
	db	00
L03CE:	db	'a joke'
	db	00
L03D5:	db	'thou'
	db	00
L03DA:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L03E7:	db	'the weather'
	db	00
L03F3:	db	'the weather'
	db	00
L03FF:	db	'weather'
	db	00
L0407:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0414:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0421:	db	'thou'
	db	00
L0426:	db	'"Why dost thou want to speak of me? Canst thou not think of '
	db	'a thing much more fun of which to speak?"'
	db	00
L048C:	db	'thou'
	db	00
L0491:	db	'supper'
	db	00
L0498:	db	'food'
	db	00
L049D:	db	'girls'
	db	00
L04A3:	db	'women'
	db	00
L04A9:	db	'a joke'
	db	00
L04B0:	db	'"I do not think I can tell a good joke whilst I play The Gam'
	db	'e! \'Twould be hard! Hmm. Ah! I have one! Why did the hen cr'
	db	'oss the road? To get to the side she was not on!"'
	db	00
L0559:	db	'a joke'
	db	00
L0560:	db	'women'
	db	00
L0566:	db	'women'
	db	00
L056C:	db	'girls'
	db	00
L0572:	db	'"There be a lot of fine girls in our fair town! Or is it \'f'
	db	'air girls in our fine town\'?" Chuckles shrugs his shoulders'
	db	'.'
	db	00
L05EA:	db	'girls'
	db	00
L05F0:	db	'food'
	db	00
L05F5:	db	'"There is good food at the pub! As for me, I like to eat on '
	db	'the floor of my room!"'
	db	00
L0648:	db	'Is there liquor?'
	db	00
L0659:	db	'The pub serves mutton?'
	db	00
L0670:	db	'Where is the Blue Boar?'
	db	00
L0688:	db	'Where is the tavern?'
	db	00
L069D:	db	'Where is the Blue Boar?'
	db	00
L06B5:	db	'"Thou canst get a good meal there! But I could give thee a g'
	db	'ood -clue-!"'
	db	00
L06FE:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0702:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0706:	db	'clue'
	db	00
L070B:	db	'supper'
	db	00
L0712:	db	'supper'
	db	00
L0719:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L071D:	db	'"So long, my friend! Do not forg... I mean, do not lose how '
	db	'to play The Game!"*'
	db	00
L076D:	db	'"Bye for now!"*'
	db	00
L077D:	db	'@Hi!@'
	db	00
