	; Function at file offset 0004E7AAH
	.funcnumber  0426H
	.data
	.msize       10F3H
	.dsize       0E38H
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a gleeful-looking merchant with an enthusiastic voic'
	db	'e and manner.'
	db	00
L0057:	db	'"Why, what can I do for thee, '
	db	00
L0076:	db	'?" asks Greg.'
	db	00
L0084:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0089:	db	'"Why, my name is Greg. It is good to see thee."'
	db	00
L00B9:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00BE:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00C2:	db	'"Why, I run the Provisioner\'s Shop here in Britain. A secon'
	db	'd home to the intrepid, it is."'
	db	00
L011D:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0121:	db	'Britain'
	db	00
L0129:	db	'Provisioner\'s Shop'
	db	00
L013C:	db	'Provisioner\'s Shop'
	db	00
L014F:	db	'"Why, thou dost look to be a person to whom adventure is no '
	db	'stranger. Whether thou art climbing a mountain, sailing the '
	db	'ocean, crossing a desert, exploring a dungeon or sleeping un'
	db	'der the stars I have just what thou mayest need."'
	db	00
L0235:	db	'Provisioner\'s Shop'
	db	00
L0248:	db	'need'
	db	00
L024D:	db	'Britain'
	db	00
L0255:	db	'"I have moved my store here as a service to Lord British, wh'
	db	'o uses me exclusively to outfit all of his various expeditio'
	db	'ns. It is true!"'
	db	00
L02DE:	db	'Britain'
	db	00
L02E6:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L02F3:	db	'moved'
	db	00
L02F9:	db	'moved'
	db	00
L02FF:	db	'"I used to have my shop in Paws. But no one in Paws has the '
	db	'money to buy much of anything."'
	db	00
L035B:	db	'moved'
	db	00
L0361:	db	'need'
	db	00
L0366:	db	'"What every adventurer needs is good luck! There is just som'
	db	'ething about this shop, about the items bought here, somethi'
	db	'ng about me and my shop that is simply very lucky. I can giv'
	db	'e thee an example of what I mean."'
	db	00
L043D:	db	'need'
	db	00
L0442:	db	'example'
	db	00
L044A:	db	'lucky'
	db	00
L0450:	db	'example'
	db	00
L0458:	db	'"A fighting man named Gorn once bought a shovel from me and '
	db	'he told me that it saved his life."'
	db	00
L04B8:	db	'saved his life'
	db	00
L04C7:	db	'Gorn'
	db	00
L04CC:	db	'example'
	db	00
L04D4:	db	'Gorn'
	db	00
L04D9:	db	'"Perhaps thou knowest of Gorn. He speaks with a most peculia'
	db	'r accent!"'
	db	00
L0520:	db	'Gorn'
	db	00
L0525:	db	'saved his life'
	db	00
L0534:	db	'"Gorn wanted to dig for some buried treasure somewhere, when'
	db	' he heard some noises behind him. Upon turning, he was horri'
	db	'fied to see a swarm of undead skeletons rushing toward him! '
	db	'In his haste to dig up the treasure, he had unbuckled his be'
	db	'lt and laid down his sword. The only thing in his hands was '
	db	'the shovel. He immediately began swinging it and ended up kn'
	db	'ocking all the skeletons to bits! He now considers it his '
	db	'\'lucky shovel\'!"'
	db	00
L06E7:	db	'saved his life'
	db	00
L06F6:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0703:	db	'"This is Lord British\'s favorite provisionary shop. He told'
	db	' me so himself. All sorts of famous adventurers pass through'
	db	' these doors. Why, just last week, we had the Avatar himself'
	db	' in this, my very own store!"'
	db	00
L07D4:	db	'"Why, now that I mention it, he was dressed a lot like thou '
	db	'art. Yes, he was."'
	db	00
L0823:	db	'dressed like Avatar'
	db	00
L0837:	db	'"Why, I seem to remember that Avatar was also wearing a Fell'
	db	'owship medallion like the one thou dost possess. Hmmmm. And '
	db	'he nearly robbed me blind. I shall have to keep a careful ey'
	db	'e on thee, I will."'
	db	00
L08FF:	db	'robbed you blind?'
	db	00
L0911:	db	'another Avatar?'
	db	00
L0921:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L092E:	db	'another Avatar?'
	db	00
L093E:	db	'"Well, he said he was the Avatar. But then it is not all tha'
	db	't unusual encountering some loon or fool who claims to be th'
	db	'e Avatar!" He looks at you and for a moment appears a little'
	db	' embarrassed.'
	db	00
L0A00:	db	'another Avatar?'
	db	00
L0A10:	db	'dressed like Avatar'
	db	00
L0A24:	db	'"He was dressed like the Avatar, similarly to how thou art p'
	db	'resently attired. At first I thought it was Jesse, the actor'
	db	' who is playing the Avatar in the play by that director... W'
	db	'hat is his name again?~~"Oh, well. It was not him."'
	db	00
L0B0C:	db	'dressed like Avatar'
	db	00
L0B20:	db	'robbed you blind?'
	db	00
L0B32:	db	'"Thou wouldst think that one who appears to be like the Avat'
	db	'ar would be worthy of trust. But, no. In this day and age th'
	db	'ere is no telling what to expect!"'
	db	00
L0BCD:	db	'robbed you blind?'
	db	00
L0BDF:	db	'lucky'
	db	00
L0BE5:	db	'"My customers are all people who go out and perform dangerou'
	db	's feats of bravery and derring-do. But most keep returning t'
	db	'o buy more provisions time and again. With all the dangerous'
	db	' things my customers do, it is a wonder I have not lost them'
	db	' all and gone out of business!"'
	db	00
L0CF5:	db	'lucky'
	db	00
L0CFB:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0CFF:	db	'"I am dreadfully sorry but the Provisioner\'s Shop is curren'
	db	'tly closed. Do return at noon when it shall be open once aga'
	db	'in."'
	db	00
L0D7B:	db	'"As I say, we have everything thou dost need to have a jolly'
	db	' splendid adventure!"'
	db	00
L0DCD:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0DD1:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0DD5:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
	db	00
L0DE9:	db	'."*'
	db	00
L0DED:	db	'@Provisions here!@'
	db	00
L0E00:	db	'@Step right in!@'
	db	00
L0E11:	db	'@Thou art welcome!@'
	db	00
L0E25:	db	'@Fine goods here!@'
	db	00
