L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'exchange'
	db	00
L0016:	db	'James'
	db	00
L001C:	db	'You see a helpful and efficient-looking woman.'
	db	00
L004B:	db	'"How may I help thee?" asks Cynthia.'
	db	00
L0070:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0075:	db	'"My name is Cynthia."'
	db	00
L008B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0090:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0094:	db	'"I am the teller at the Mint. I am also a member of the Brit'
	db	'annian Tax Council."'
	db	00
L00E5:	db	'Britannian Tax Council'
	db	00
L00FC:	db	'Mint'
	db	00
L0101:	db	'Mint'
	db	00
L0106:	db	'"Here at the Mint we store gold, oversee production of coins'
	db	' and keep an accurate count of how much money the kingdom ha'
	db	's available for such things as farming, building the roads, '
	db	'developing sources of fresh water, seeing to the health of t'
	db	'he citizenry, maintaining the estates of nobles, raising the'
	db	' guard militia and carrying out the decrees of Lord British.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L0270:	db	'Mint'
	db	00
L0275:	db	'guards'
	db	00
L027C:	db	'estates'
	db	00
L0284:	db	'health'
	db	00
L028B:	db	'water'
	db	00
L0291:	db	'roads'
	db	00
L0297:	db	'farms'
	db	00
L029D:	db	'money'
	db	00
L02A3:	db	'Britannian Tax Council'
	db	00
L02BA:	db	'"The Britannian Tax Council is in charge of the accounting, '
	db	'assessment and collection of the taxes. If thou wilt be earn'
	db	'ing any money here in Britannia thou wilt need to take this '
	db	'paper."'
	db	00
L0376:	db	'"Fill it out and return it here at the end of the year when '
	db	'thou dost come back to pay thy taxes."'
	db	00
L03D9:	db	'"Thou art carrying too much. Come back and I will give thee '
	db	'thy paper when thou art not so greatly encumbered."'
	db	00
L0449:	db	'Britannian Tax Council'
	db	00
L0460:	db	'money'
	db	00
L0466:	db	'"In order to keep the standard of money constant, we also op'
	db	'erate as an exchange for those who possess quantities of gol'
	db	'd.~~We supply the equivalent value of their gold in spendabl'
	db	'e coin of the realm and then transform the gold we receive i'
	db	'nto more money. So, as thou canst see, it is a very efficien'
	db	't system."'
	db	00
L059D:	db	'money'
	db	00
L05A3:	db	'system'
	db	00
L05AA:	db	'exchange'
	db	00
L05B3:	db	'farms'
	db	00
L05B9:	db	'"As I am certain thou dost know, the seven year drought, whi'
	db	'ch thankfully ended several years ago, has left much of the '
	db	'farming in the Kingdom in disarray. That is why the cost of '
	db	'food is so expensive. But without the support of the Royal T'
	db	'reasury, the prices would be even higher."'
	db	00
L06D4:	db	'farms'
	db	00
L06DA:	db	'roads'
	db	00
L06E0:	db	'"The increased use of wagons has caused many of the roads th'
	db	'roughout Britannia to rapidly deteriorate. It costs a lot of'
	db	' money to build new roads and keep them all repaired."'
	db	00
L078F:	db	'roads'
	db	00
L0795:	db	'water'
	db	00
L079B:	db	'"It is of the utmost importance to the Kingdom to insure its'
	db	' populous a clean water supply, and that requires a regular '
	db	'supply of new and fresh wells."'
	db	00
L0833:	db	'water'
	db	00
L0839:	db	'health'
	db	00
L0840:	db	'"As Britannia\'s population has greatly increased in the las'
	db	't two hundred years, so has the risk of infectious diseases,'
	db	' such as the mysterious skin deterioration that afflicts tho'
	db	'se who partake in the venom of the silver serpent. The numbe'
	db	'r of healers that the Kingdom needs has risen dramatically."'
	db	00
L096C:	db	'health'
	db	00
L0973:	db	'estates'
	db	00
L097B:	db	'"The local Lords and Mayors all have residences that are mai'
	db	'ntained through the auspices of the Kingdom."'
	db	00
L09E5:	db	'estates'
	db	00
L09ED:	db	'guards'
	db	00
L09F4:	db	'"The military training is conducted at Serpent\'s Hold, wher'
	db	'e the guards that protect all of the towns and cities of Bri'
	db	'tannia are instructed. \'Tis funded by the Royal Treasury."'
	db	00
L0AA6:	db	'guards'
	db	00
L0AAD:	db	'system'
	db	00
L0AB4:	db	'"It not only applies to gold but it also applies to all mine'
	db	'rals. We oversee the sale and rate of exchange for precious '
	db	'ores extracted by the Britannian Mining Company. But we do n'
	db	'ot handle the sale of gems. There is a jeweler in town who h'
	db	'andles that."'
	db	00
L0BB2:	db	'system'
	db	00
L0BB9:	db	'exchange'
	db	00
L0BC2:	db	'"Dost thou have some gold that thou wouldst like to exchange'
	db	'?"'
	db	00
L0C01:	db	'"I can see thou hast no nuggets or bars of gold. Whatever go'
	db	'ld thou mayest possess is already the coin of the realm. I c'
	db	'annot help thee anymore than that."'
	db	00
L0C9D:	db	'"We can exchange thy gold nuggets and bars into spendable co'
	db	'in for thee. I will give thee ten gold coins for each gold n'
	db	'ugget and one-hundred gold coins for each gold bar."'
	db	00
L0D4A:	db	'"Oh, my. Thou canst not possibly carry that many gold coins.'
	db	' Thou must return when thou dost have more space in thy pack'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L0DC5:	db	'"And here are '
	db	00
L0DD4:	db	' gold coins for thee in return, '
	db	00
L0DF5:	db	'. I thank thee for thy business."'
	db	00
L0E17:	db	'"Very well. Mayhaps another time."'
	db	00
L0E3A:	db	'"Please come to The Mint during regular daytime hours."'
	db	00
L0E72:	db	'exchange'
	db	00
L0E7B:	db	'James'
	db	00
L0E81:	db	'"James is mine husband and I am very worried about him. I kn'
	db	'ow he is feeling very unhappy lately and he dislikes his job'
	db	'. If thou dost speak to him please tell him that even though'
	db	' we have not been speaking very much lately, that I am still'
	db	' thinking of him and that I still care about him."'
	db	00
L0FA4:	db	'James'
	db	00
L0FAA:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0FAE:	db	'"Good day, '
	db	00
L0FBA:	db	'."*'
	db	00
