	; Function at file offset 00055E2BH
	.funcnumber  042DH
	.data
	.msize       138DH
	.dsize       1084H
L0000:	db	'Figg is too intent on listening to the Fellowship meeting to'
	db	' acknowledge your attempts to converse with him.*'
	db	00
L006E:	db	'"Hast thou seen Batlin? Where is he? He needs to lead our me'
	db	'eting!"'
	db	00
L00B2:	db	'"My goodness! It is nine o\'clock! Excuse me, I must get to '
	db	'tonight\'s Fellowship meeting."*'
	db	00
L010D:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0111:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0115:	db	'name'
	db	00
L011A:	db	'Weston'
	db	00
L0121:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L012C:	db	'You see a man whose wrinkled face forms a caricature of grum'
	db	'piness.'
	db	00
L0170:	db	'"Thou dost wish words with me, '
	db	00
L0190:	db	'?" asks Figg.'
	db	00
L019E:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01A3:	db	'"I am Figg."'
	db	00
L01B0:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01B5:	db	'job'
	db	00
L01B9:	db	'"I am the caretaker of the Royal Orchards here in Britain."'
	db	00
L01F5:	db	'Royal Orchards'
	db	00
L0204:	db	'caretaker'
	db	00
L020E:	db	'caretaker'
	db	00
L0218:	db	'"My responsibilities include caring for the trees, watching '
	db	'over the pickers at harvest time and protecting the Royal Or'
	db	'chard from thieves."'
	db	00
L02A5:	db	'thieves'
	db	00
L02AD:	db	'pickers'
	db	00
L02B5:	db	'trees'
	db	00
L02BB:	db	'caretaker'
	db	00
L02C5:	db	'trees'
	db	00
L02CB:	db	'"Apple trees require constant care. I must make sure the tre'
	db	'es all have enough water but not too much. I must keep all t'
	db	'rees properly trimmed and be watchful so that the crop does '
	db	'not get infested by bugs or worms. I am also required to pic'
	db	'k up all of the fallen apples, which is a job in itself."'
	db	00
L03F5:	db	'trees'
	db	00
L03FB:	db	'pickers'
	db	00
L0403:	db	'"Most of them are migrant farmers from Paws. Because they we'
	db	're once farmers, they are convinced they know more about the'
	db	' upkeep of the orchard than I! Of course that is preposterou'
	db	's. Also the pickers do not take orders very well."'
	db	00
L04EA:	db	'pickers'
	db	00
L04F2:	db	'thieves'
	db	00
L04FA:	db	'"They would rob us down to the last twig if I gave them the '
	db	'chance! I should be awarded a medal from Lord British himsel'
	db	'f the way I risk my very life and limb protecting this orcha'
	db	'rd. Why, I just caught another thief recently. His name was '
	db	'Weston."'
	db	00
L05F3:	db	'thieves'
	db	00
L05FB:	db	'Weston'
	db	00
L0602:	db	'Royal Orchards'
	db	00
L0611:	db	'"Here are grown the finest apples in all of Britannia. I wou'
	db	'ld let thee sample one but it would be against the law as th'
	db	'ou art obviously not of noble stock."'
	db	00
L06AF:	db	'Royal Orchards'
	db	00
L06BE:	db	'Weston'
	db	00
L06C5:	db	'"He now resides in the prison, thanks to me! I knew what he '
	db	'was up to from the moment I saw him! He had the look of a ha'
	db	'rdened apple thief so I had him nicked by the town guard."'
	db	00
L0778:	db	'apple thief'
	db	00
L0784:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L078B:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0796:	db	'Weston'
	db	00
L079D:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L07A4:	db	'"Yes, Weston is now living in our local prison. If thou dost'
	db	' not believe me, thou canst go there and see for thyself!"'
	db	00
L081B:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L0822:	db	'apple thief'
	db	00
L082E:	db	'"Oh, he came here with some sob story. But when one is as as'
	db	'tute an observer of human behavior as I am, one can tell the'
	db	' true intent of people, which is often contrary to what they'
	db	' will say to thee!"'
	db	00
L08F6:	db	'apple thief'
	db	00
L0902:	db	'observer'
	db	00
L090B:	db	'sob story'
	db	00
L0915:	db	'sob story'
	db	00
L091F:	db	'"I do not recall, exactly. Something about his impoverished '
	db	'wife and family starving to death in Paws or some load of ru'
	db	'bbish."'
	db	00
L099F:	db	'sob story'
	db	00
L09A9:	db	'observer'
	db	00
L09B2:	db	'"Yes, I do consider myself to be a more than passable judge '
	db	'of character. And dost thou know how I became so?"'
	db	00
L0A21:	db	'"Oh, then art thou not the clever one!"'
	db	00
L0A49:	db	'"Then I shall tell thee! I am a member of The Fellowship!"'
	db	00
L0A84:	db	'observer'
	db	00
L0A8D:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L0A98:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L0AA3:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0AAE:	db	'"I am a member of the Fellowship, yes. But it would be a cri'
	db	'me for me to give apples from the Royal Orchard to The Fello'
	db	'wship, and it would be a violation of my sacred duty. While '
	db	'selling apples is also a violation, I was only trying to do '
	db	'this man Weston a favor. And I suppose these accusations are'
	db	' the thanks I get? Hmph!"'
	db	00
L0BF4:	db	'He leans in close to you and speaks lower. "Thou art also a '
	db	'member of The Fellowship, after all. Am I not thy brother? S'
	db	'houldst thou not trust me?" He gives you a crooked wink.'
	db	00
L0CA5:	db	'"Thou seest? I am thy brother!" He hands you an apple.'
	db	00
L0CDC:	db	'"I would give thee an apple to show thee my sincerity, but i'
	db	't seems thou art too encumbered."'
	db	00
L0D3A:	db	'"But enough of these desperate accusations from a known crim'
	db	'inal."'
	db	00
L0D7D:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0D81:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0D8C:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0D90:	db	'"I can do thee a favor as well. Wouldst thou like to buy one'
	db	' of these beautiful apples for the merest pittance of five g'
	db	'old coins?"'
	db	00
L0E14:	db	'Figg takes an apple from a nearby basket. After polishing it'
	db	' slightly on his shirt, he hands it to you.'
	db	00
L0E7C:	db	'"Thou cannot take thine apple! Thou art carrying too much!"'
	db	00
L0EB8:	db	'"Thou dost not even have enough gold to buy one apple! Thou '
	db	'hast wasted the time of the King\'s Caretaker of the Royal O'
	db	'rchard. Away, peasant! Away before I call the guard!"'
	db	00
L0F65:	db	'"Very well. But thou art passing up an opportunity that few '
	db	'are offered. In fact, eh, I would appreciate it if thou woul'
	db	'dst not mention our little chat to anyone. Agreed?"'
	db	00
L1011:	db	'"Ah, I knew thou wert a good \'un."'
	db	00
L1034:	db	'"No! Well, fine, then."*'
	db	00
L104D:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L1051:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1055:	db	'"I can see that thou shouldst be on thy way."*'
	db	00
