	; Function at file offset 00058E19H
	.funcnumber  0430H
	.data
	.msize       0E8AH
	.dsize       0C5FH
L0000:	db	'You see an attractive woman dressed in armour and carrying a'
	db	' small arsenal of weapons with her.'
	db	00
L0060:	db	'"How may I help thee?" asks Amanda.'
	db	00
L0084:	db	'Stay thine hand!'
	db	00
L0095:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0099:	db	'job'
	db	00
L009D:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00A2:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00A7:	db	'"My name is Amanda."'
	db	00
L00BC:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00C1:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00C5:	db	'"Mine half-sister and I have no job at this time. We are jou'
	db	'rneying to seek inner peace, now that our quest has been abo'
	db	'rted."'
	db	00
L0144:	db	'inner peace'
	db	00
L0150:	db	'"Mine half-sister and I have no job but to serve our quest."'
	db	00
L018D:	db	'quest'
	db	00
L0193:	db	'half-sister'
	db	00
L019F:	db	'half-sister'
	db	00
L01AB:	db	'would have been'
	db	00
L01BB:	db	'will be'
	db	00
L01C3:	db	'"Mine half-sister is Eiko. She, like myself, is a warrior tr'
	db	'ained by Karenna in the ways of combat. We studied long and '
	db	'hard together to master the skills that '
	db	00
L0264:	db	' required to achieve our vengeance."'
	db	00
L0289:	db	'"The two of us had not even met before our father\'s death. '
	db	'But we bonded like sisters in the rigorous disciplines we le'
	db	'arned from our trainer, Karenna of Minoc."*'
	db	00
L032C:	db	'half-sister'
	db	00
L0338:	db	'inner peace'
	db	00
L0344:	db	'"Yes. Our lives have been dedicated to vengeance for so long'
	db	' that we feel adrift, aimless without it. We must find a new'
	db	' reason for living.~~"We are considering joining The Fellows'
	db	'hip, as they offer guidance for lost souls. But we must cons'
	db	'ider this longer. We are still unsure."'
	db	00
L045C:	db	'quest'
	db	00
L0462:	db	'"We are on the trail of our father\'s murderer."'
	db	00
L0492:	db	'quest'
	db	00
L0498:	db	'killer'
	db	00
L049F:	db	'killer'
	db	00
L04A6:	db	'"Our father was slain in a most violent manner by a vicious '
	db	'and terrible cyclops. He was impaled on a spear. It took sev'
	db	'eral hours for him to die."~~She looks up, eyes glittering. '
	db	'"Hast thou ever watched anyone die from a belly wound, '
	db	00
L0592:	db	'? The agony cannot be imagined."'
	db	00
L05B3:	db	'killer'
	db	00
L05BA:	db	'impaled'
	db	00
L05C2:	db	'cyclops'
	db	00
L05CA:	db	'cyclops'
	db	00
L05D2:	db	'"We have been tracking this creature for years, ever since w'
	db	'e completed our training. We have followed him from one end '
	db	'of Britannia to another. Sometimes he was just one step ahea'
	db	'd of us. But now we know that we are nearer to him than we h'
	db	'ave ever been before."'
	db	00
L06D9:	db	'"When we find him there shall be no escape. We want vengeanc'
	db	'e and we mean to have it!"*'
	db	00
L0731:	db	'cyclops'
	db	00
L0739:	db	'impaled'
	db	00
L0741:	db	'"Our father fought bravely for his life. He did not die easi'
	db	'ly. He died a hero\'s death. Although we may both die in the'
	db	' effort, we intend to give his murderer a death fit for a tr'
	db	'ue villain."'
	db	00
L0801:	db	'Eiko smiles wickedly.*'
	db	00
L0818:	db	'impaled'
	db	00
L0820:	db	'Stay thine hand!'
	db	00
L0831:	db	'You explain to Amanda what you have learned. Kalideth had go'
	db	'ne mad when he fought with Iskander and the source of what i'
	db	's causing the problems with magic and the mage\'s minds - th'
	db	'e thing that really killed Kalideth - has been destroyed.~~"'
	db	'Thou hast robbed me of my rightful vengeance! How dare thee!'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L095E:	db	'Eiko sighs, and her shoulders slump. "Come now, sister. With'
	db	' the matter of our father\'s untimely death now settled we c'
	db	'an at last let it go. Now we can devote our lives to ourselv'
	db	'es rather than remain trapped in the past. It is for the bes'
	db	't, thou must trust me."*'
	db	00
L0A66:	db	'Amanda shakes her head, dazed and confused. "Perhaps thou ar'
	db	't correct, Eiko. I must think."*'
	db	00
L0AC3:	db	'Amanda turns and slams her fist into the wall, then collapse'
	db	's onto it with a sob. After a moment, she straightens, but d'
	db	'oes not turn to face you.~~"Have no fear that I will continu'
	db	'e my vengeance against the cyclops. I am not so far gone tha'
	db	't I would kill a creature for acting in self-defense.~"But I'
	db	' must have some time to myself now. Please, go. I must think'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L0C2E:	db	'Stay thine hand!'
	db	00
L0C3F:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0C43:	db	'"Good journey to thee, '
	db	00
L0C5B:	db	'."*'
	db	00
