	; Function at file offset 00060BC4H
	.funcnumber  043AH
	.data
	.msize       0EAAH
	.dsize       0BB6H
L0000:	db	'Gordon is too involved in listening to the Fellowship meetin'
	db	'g to hear you.*'
	db	00
L004C:	db	'"Where oh where is Batlin? He is late for the meeting!"'
	db	00
L0084:	db	'"Oh, my! I must leave immediately! I am late for the Fellows'
	db	'hip meeting!"*'
	db	00
L00CF:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L00D3:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00D7:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00DC:	db	'You see a friendly face looking back at you.'
	db	00
L0109:	db	'"How art thou this fine day, '
	db	00
L0127:	db	'?" asks Gordon.'
	db	00
L0137:	db	'name'
	db	00
L013C:	db	'"My name is Gordon."'
	db	00
L0151:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0156:	db	'job'
	db	00
L015A:	db	'"I sell fish and chips from my wagon."'
	db	00
L0181:	db	'wagon'
	db	00
L0187:	db	'fish and chips'
	db	00
L0196:	db	'fish and chips'
	db	00
L01A5:	db	'"Come back later when I am open for business."*'
	db	00
L01D5:	db	'"I have the best fish and chips thou shalt taste in all of B'
	db	'ritannia. My price is only 8 gold coins per serving. Wouldst'
	db	' thou like to have some?"'
	db	00
L0267:	db	'He hands you a plate.'
	db	00
L027D:	db	'"They are indeed the best fish and chips in all of Britannia'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L02BC:	db	'"Thou art carrying too many things to take thy fish and chip'
	db	's from me!"'
	db	00
L0304:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough gold to get any fish and chips. S'
	db	'orry!"'
	db	00
L0347:	db	'"Come back again when thou art hungry and I am sure thou sha'
	db	'lt change thy mind."'
	db	00
L0398:	db	'fish and chips'
	db	00
L03A7:	db	'wagon'
	db	00
L03AD:	db	'"I just painted my wagon recently. It receives more attentio'
	db	'n. Business is much better now. I am saving my money to trav'
	db	'el to Buccaneer\'s Den."'
	db	00
L043D:	db	'wagon'
	db	00
L0443:	db	'Buccaneer\'s Den'
	db	00
L0453:	db	'business'
	db	00
L045C:	db	'business'
	db	00
L0465:	db	'"Ever since I became a member of The Fellowship, business ha'
	db	's been increasing steadily. I have refined and improved the '
	db	'recipe for my fish batter and it has since become a favorite'
	db	' meal of nearly everyone in Britain. I have even served my f'
	db	'ish and chips to Lord British himself."'
	db	00
L057D:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L058A:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0595:	db	'business'
	db	00
L059E:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L05AB:	db	'"Thou dost know-- the bloke who wears a crown and acts like '
	db	'a king."'
	db	00
L05F0:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L05FD:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0608:	db	'"I am glad to see that thou art a member. Will I see thee at'
	db	' the next meeting?"'
	db	00
L0658:	db	'"Then I shall see thee at nine o\'clock sharp!"'
	db	00
L0687:	db	'"Thou shouldst apply thyself more stringently to the ways of'
	db	' The Fellowship! Our meeting is at nine o\'clock. I can see '
	db	'thou dost certainly need to attend."'
	db	00
L0723:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L072E:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L0739:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L0744:	db	'Buccaneer\'s Den'
	db	00
L0754:	db	'"I wish to win some money at Buccaneer\'s Den. It is a pirat'
	db	'e resort and they have a fabulous House of Games there."'
	db	00
L07C8:	db	'House of Games'
	db	00
L07D7:	db	'pirate resort'
	db	00
L07E5:	db	'Buccaneer\'s Den'
	db	00
L07F5:	db	'pirate resort'
	db	00
L0803:	db	'"As I am certain thou knowest, Buccaneer\'s Den was once a d'
	db	'en of thieves and villains. As such, it held a romantic appe'
	db	'al for those who longed for a taste of such an adventurous e'
	db	'xistence. I confess, I am one of those people. When thou dos'
	db	't spend thy life selling fish from a wagon, thou art in need'
	db	' of excitement. The pirates eventually realized just how muc'
	db	'h they are secretly envied, and so they have turned their is'
	db	'land into a place of thrilling amusements."'
	db	00
L09D2:	db	'pirate resort'
	db	00
L09E0:	db	'House of Games'
	db	00
L09EF:	db	'"It is said they have several games of chance there! Gold ca'
	db	'n be won wagering on the outcome of a race of fine stallions'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L0A6A:	db	'House of Games'
	db	00
L0A79:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0A84:	db	'"I saw thee receive thy medallion. I can certainly say the F'
	db	'ellowship has done wonders for my life and I know it will be'
	db	' the same for thee as well." He gives thee a knowing grin.'
	db	00
L0B37:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0B42:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0B46:	db	'"Have a pleasant day, '
	db	00
L0B5D:	db	'." *'
	db	00
L0B62:	db	'@Fish \'n\' chips!@'
	db	00
L0B74:	db	'@Hot fish \'n\' chips!@'
	db	00
L0B8A:	db	'@Fish \'n\' chippies!@'
	db	00
L0B9F:	db	'@Fish \'n\' chips here!@'
	db	00
