L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'mutton'
	db	00
L0014:	db	'This is an elderly woman who epitomizes \'grandmotherly\'.'
	db	00
L004D:	db	'"Hello, again!" Boots says.'
	db	00
L0069:	db	'name'
	db	00
L006E:	db	'"All my brothers and sisters called me \'Boots\' when I was '
	db	'a baby, and it hath remained my name ever since."'
	db	00
L00DA:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00DF:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00E3:	db	'"Why, I am Lord British\'s personal cook! I prepare meals fo'
	db	'r the entire castle."'
	db	00
L0134:	db	'meals'
	db	00
L013A:	db	'meals'
	db	00
L0140:	db	'"Just go to the dining room at breakfast or supper time and '
	db	'mine husband Bennie will serve thee!"'
	db	00
L01A2:	db	'Bennie'
	db	00
L01A9:	db	'supper'
	db	00
L01B0:	db	'breakfast'
	db	00
L01BA:	db	'meals'
	db	00
L01C0:	db	'breakfast'
	db	00
L01CA:	db	'"For breakfast I usually prepare a dish that my Liege brough'
	db	't with him from his homeland. Here we call it Eggs British. '
	db	'It is served with assorted fruits and tea, of course. It is '
	db	'the King\'s favorite."'
	db	00
L0294:	db	'breakfast'
	db	00
L029E:	db	'supper'
	db	00
L02A5:	db	'"This meal is usually whatever meat or game or fish Lord Bri'
	db	'tish requests, accompanied by several additional courses and'
	db	' a fine dessert."'
	db	00
L032F:	db	'supper'
	db	00
L0336:	db	'Bennie'
	db	00
L033D:	db	'"He\'s a dear, but he has become a little absent-minded in h'
	db	'is later years. He never remembers to bring enough meat from'
	db	' the slaughterhouse in Paws. In fact, we are short this week'
	db	'!"'
	db	00
L03F3:	db	'short'
	db	00
L03F9:	db	'absent-minded'
	db	00
L0407:	db	'Bennie'
	db	00
L040E:	db	'absent-minded'
	db	00
L041C:	db	'"Last week I asked him to put a little garlic into some soup'
	db	'. He put in the garlic and then forgot about it. So he went '
	db	'and put some more in. Then he forgot he did that. So he put '
	db	'in more. Well, thou canst imagine the look on Lord British'
	db	'\'s face when he finally did taste that soup! It is a good t'
	db	'hing we live and work in the castle of such a just ruler."'
	db	00
L0580:	db	'absent-minded'
	db	00
L058E:	db	'short'
	db	00
L0594:	db	'"That is right, we do not have enough. If thou couldst bring'
	db	' me mutton from the slaughterhouse, I will pay thee 5 gold f'
	db	'or every portion thou canst bring. All right?"'
	db	00
L063B:	db	'"Good, I will be awaiting thy return!"'
	db	00
L0662:	db	'"Oh dear. Well, I know thou art busy. Some other time, then.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L06A0:	db	'short'
	db	00
L06A6:	db	'mutton'
	db	00
L06AD:	db	'"Splendid! Let\'s see, we agreed on 5 gold per portion, if I'
	db	' remember correctly."'
	db	00
L06FE:	db	'mutton'
	db	00
L0705:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0709:	db	'"Bye now!"*'
	db	00
