L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a thoroughly disheartened young man who is miserably'
	db	' languishing behind bars.'
	db	00
L0063:	db	'"Hello again, '
	db	00
L0072:	db	'," says Weston.'
	db	00
L0082:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0087:	db	'"I am Weston."'
	db	00
L0096:	db	'name'
	db	00
L009B:	db	'job'
	db	00
L009F:	db	'"I have none so long as I am left to rot here in this prison'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L00DE:	db	'"Thy job is to pay for the crime thou hast committed."*'
	db	00
L0116:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L011D:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L0124:	db	'"My crime was stealing apples from the Royal Orchards. This '
	db	'I did and I admit it freely. If given the same set of circum'
	db	'stances I would do it again."'
	db	00
L01BA:	db	'"A-ha! Not only an unrepentant criminal but also a potential'
	db	' professional thief! Looks like this one has ended in the ri'
	db	'ght place and just in the nick o\' time."*'
	db	00
L025C:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L0263:	db	'circumstances'
	db	00
L0271:	db	'stealing apples'
	db	00
L0281:	db	'stealing apples'
	db	00
L0291:	db	'"I had offered to buy them first, but Figg, the caretaker of'
	db	' the orchard, set an exorbitant price which I am certain he '
	db	'would have pocketed for himself. So, yes, I admit to stealin'
	db	'g them."'
	db	00
L034E:	db	'"See how the common criminal blames his type of immoral beha'
	db	'vior on others, all the while denying it in himself! This on'
	db	'e is irredeemable, he is."*'
	db	00
L03E2:	db	'stealing apples'
	db	00
L03F2:	db	'admit'
	db	00
L03F8:	db	'Figg'
	db	00
L03FD:	db	'Figg'
	db	00
L0402:	db	'"He gives baskets of fruit free to The Fellowship without Lo'
	db	'rd British\'s consent, I am quite certain."'
	db	00
L0469:	db	'"Thou shouldst not listen to this obvious slander, '
	db	00
L049D:	db	'! It is hearsay!"*'
	db	00
L04B0:	db	'Figg'
	db	00
L04B5:	db	'admit'
	db	00
L04BB:	db	'"Mine only regrets are that I did not try to steal something'
	db	' bigger and that\tI did not get away with it."'
	db	00
L0525:	db	'admit'
	db	00
L052B:	db	'circumstances'
	db	00
L0539:	db	'"I am not from Britain, '
	db	00
L0552:	db	'. I am from Paws and it is another reason why they believe I'
	db	' can be trifled with."'
	db	00
L05A5:	db	'"This prisoner is from Paws! I bloody knew it! To his credit'
	db	' he was in town nearly an entire day before he stole somethi'
	db	'ng. For a citizen of Paws that is as honest as they come!"*'
	db	00
L0659:	db	'circumstances'
	db	00
L0667:	db	'Paws'
	db	00
L066C:	db	'Paws'
	db	00
L0671:	db	'"Paws is a town where thou mayest feel the icy grip of pover'
	db	'ty about thine heart."'
	db	00
L06C4:	db	'Paws'
	db	00
L06C9:	db	'poverty'
	db	00
L06D1:	db	'town'
	db	00
L06D6:	db	'"Oh bloody \'ell! Now I suppose he is going to go and tell u'
	db	's his whole pathetic life\'s story! Couldst thou wait until '
	db	'I get out mine handkerchief so I do not interrupt thee with '
	db	'all my wailing!"*'
	db	00
L079A:	db	'town'
	db	00
L079F:	db	'"Not so long ago Paws was a thriving rustic coastal village.'
	db	' But as Britain grew larger most of our local businesses mov'
	db	'ed there. We became a farming town and the seven year drough'
	db	't gave us a lashing that we have yet to recover from."'
	db	00
L088A:	db	'town'
	db	00
L088F:	db	'poverty'
	db	00
L0897:	db	'"I do not wish to bemoan my fate, but my family lives in Paw'
	db	's -- my wife Alina and my child Cassie. They were starving a'
	db	'nd I came to Britain to get food for them."'
	db	00
L093B:	db	'"Oh, now! Do not go and bring up poverty as an excuse as to '
	db	'why thou hast turned to crime! My father was so poor he and '
	db	'his family had to eat dirt. But he still raised me proper. B'
	db	'eat the stuffings out of me if he ever so much as imagined I'
	db	' did anything wrong, I can tell thee that!"*'
	db	00
L0A58:	db	'poverty'
	db	00
L0A60:	db	'starving'
	db	00
L0A69:	db	'family'
	db	00
L0A70:	db	'family'
	db	00
L0A77:	db	'"I do not want any mercy for myself. I have admitted my guil'
	db	't. But my life does not only belong to myself. It belongs to'
	db	' my wife and family as well. Without me they will suffer unb'
	db	'earable hardships, such as they might not survive."'
	db	00
L0B5F:	db	'family'
	db	00
L0B66:	db	'starving'
	db	00
L0B6F:	db	'"Although there are fools who will speak otherwise, the peop'
	db	'le of Britannia are being crushed by the vicious tyranny of '
	db	'the class system. While a few have more than they could ever'
	db	' enjoy, there are many who go to sleep hungry every night. M'
	db	'y wife and daughter to name two of them."'
	db	00
L0C89:	db	'"Oh, that reminds me it is nearly time for my meal break! Th'
	db	'e trout is supposed to be delicious today at the Farmer\'s M'
	db	'arket."'
	db	00
L0D08:	db	'starving'
	db	00
L0D11:	db	'class system'
	db	00
L0D1E:	db	'fools'
	db	00
L0D24:	db	'fools'
	db	00
L0D2A:	db	'"Fools like our good friend the guard would have us believe '
	db	'that nothing has changed in Britannia for over two hundred y'
	db	'ears. That we can live our lives as if all of our problems d'
	db	'o not exist. I say to thee that it is people like that who c'
	db	'ause our problems in the first place."'
	db	00
L0E41:	db	'fools'
	db	00
L0E47:	db	'class system'
	db	00
L0E54:	db	'"While I am certain Lord British is a just and fair ruler, h'
	db	'e must be quite unaware of all that goes on in his kingdom. '
	db	'Surely he would not tolerate such inequity."'
	db	00
L0EF9:	db	'"All right! That is enough noise out of thee! All day long y'
	db	'akkata-yakkata about the awful terrible class system! Why, t'
	db	'he next thing thou knowest thou shalt be sayin\' society is '
	db	'to blame for thy crimes. Not a word from anybody about any a'
	db	'ppreciation for keeping the laws and order. No, of course no'
	db	't! But all the pity in the world for the dangerous lawbreake'
	db	'rs who are the real threat to society."*'
	db	00
L1089:	db	'"Wouldst thou speak with Lord British about me? I would bet '
	db	'that he is completely unaware of my case! Please! Wilt thou '
	db	'speak with him?"'
	db	00
L1112:	db	'"Oh, I thank thee, Avatar! My fate and the fates of my wife '
	db	'and daughter are in thine hands!"'
	db	00
L1170:	db	'Weston lowers his head. "Then why art thou speaking with me?'
	db	' Go away and leave me to my misery."*'
	db	00
L11D2:	db	'class system'
	db	00
L11DF:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L11E3:	db	'"I thank thee for visiting me." *'
	db	00
