	.dsize       0563H
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a young gypsy lad. He is wearing a Fellowship medall'
	db	'ion. His eyes look down and his expression is one of extreme'
	db	' sorrow.'
	db	00
L008E:	db	'Sasha looks up. "Good day to thee, '
	db	00
L00B2:	db	'."'
	db	00
L00B5:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00BA:	db	'"My name is Sasha."'
	db	00
L00CE:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00D3:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00D7:	db	'"I am too young to have a job. I am a gypsy as my parents ve'
	db	're gypsies. I am also a member of The Fellowship."'
	db	00
L0146:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0151:	db	'gypsies'
	db	00
L0159:	db	'parents'
	db	00
L0161:	db	'parents'
	db	00
L0169:	db	'"My parents - Frederico and Tania - vere murdered. I do not '
	db	'know vhy anyone vould vant to harm them." The words choke ou'
	db	't of the boy. Suddenly he is overwhelmed by grief and is una'
	db	'ble to speak further.'
	db	00
L0233:	db	'parents'
	db	00
L023B:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0243:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L024B:	db	'"It happened at the sawmill in Minoc."'
	db	00
L0272:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L027A:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0285:	db	'"For the past veek I have been avay from home doing vork for'
	db	' The Fellowship."'
	db	00
L02D3:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L02DE:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L02E9:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L02F4:	db	'gypsies'
	db	00
L02FC:	db	'"I have returned to be vith Margareta and Jergi to grieve fo'
	db	'r my parents. They did not approve of my joining The Fellows'
	db	'hip but I know that they vere concerned out of their love fo'
	db	'r me, just as I loved them."'
	db	00
L03CD:	db	'gypsies'
	db	00
L03D5:	db	'Jergi'
	db	00
L03DB:	db	'Margareta'
	db	00
L03E5:	db	'Margareta'
	db	00
L03EF:	db	'"She is very vise and knows many things but vhen I asked her'
	db	' if I should go back to The Fellowship or stay with them she'
	db	' did not answer me."'
	db	00
L047C:	db	'Margareta'
	db	00
L0486:	db	'Jergi'
	db	00
L048C:	db	'"He vas my father\'s brother. He is a good man and vise. Now'
	db	' he is the leader of our people. He vill do what is right fo'
	db	'r us."'
	db	00
L050A:	db	'"Perhaps thou shouldst talk vith him."'
	db	00
L0531:	db	'Jergi'
	db	00
L0537:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L053B:	db	'The lad stoically nods and turns away.*'
	db	00
