	; Function at file offset 0007663EH
	.funcnumber  0455H
	.data
	.msize       12A4H
	.dsize       10AEH
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a handsome craftsman with an intense, piercing gaze.'
	db	00
L004A:	db	'Gladstone shakes your hand and you can feel just a trace of '
	db	'sculptor\'s clay clinging to his palm. Although he hardly kn'
	db	'ows you, he treats you like an old friend.'
	db	00
L00EC:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00F1:	db	'"My name is Gladstone, '
	db	00
L0109:	db	'. At thy service."'
	db	00
L011C:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0121:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0125:	db	'"I am a glassblower and a sculptor. I make mostly bottles an'
	db	'd bowls. But in my time I have constructed all manners of st'
	db	'atuary out of glass as well."'
	db	00
L01BB:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L01C1:	db	'Artist\'s Guild'
	db	00
L01D0:	db	'glass'
	db	00
L01D6:	db	'The man\'s eyes study you for a moment. "Thou dost not know '
	db	'what has happened? William, our local Sawyer found two gypsi'
	db	'es murdered in his sawmill."'
	db	00
L026A:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0272:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L0278:	db	'"There is active commerce here in Minoc sufficient to keep t'
	db	'he Artist\'s Guild financially solvent. But in recent weeks '
	db	'I have come to fear we may not keep it going for very much l'
	db	'onger. Unlike The Fellowship or Owen\'s monument, we do not '
	db	'have much political power. Now other events make our trouble'
	db	's seem less important."'
	db	00
L03BA:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L03C0:	db	'events'
	db	00
L03C7:	db	'power'
	db	00
L03CD:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L03D6:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L03E1:	db	'power'
	db	00
L03E7:	db	'"The Artist\'s Guild is taxed mercilessly by the Britannian '
	db	'Tax Council. Even in our best year it is a struggle to make '
	db	'ends meet. It seems that we are not considered important eno'
	db	'ugh to be given an even chance."'
	db	00
L04BB:	db	'power'
	db	00
L04C1:	db	'events'
	db	00
L04C8:	db	'"Surely thou hast heard about the murders of Frederico and T'
	db	'ania?!"'
	db	00
L050C:	db	'events'
	db	00
L0513:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L051B:	db	'Artist\'s Guild'
	db	00
L052A:	db	'"The Artist\'s Guild is a group of local craftsmen. We sell '
	db	'our wares here in Minoc. While we are organized as a guild o'
	db	'f equal members, I am tentatively the Guild head."'
	db	00
L05D4:	db	'Artist\'s Guild'
	db	00
L05E3:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L05EB:	db	'"I shudder to think such foul deeds are so freely committed '
	db	'in our fair town. Art thou investigating it? I wish thee all'
	db	' success in tracking the culprit. I barely knew Frederico or'
	db	' Tania, but I did meet their son Sasha once."'
	db	00
L06CD:	db	'Sasha'
	db	00
L06D3:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L06DB:	db	'Sasha'
	db	00
L06E1:	db	'"He befriended Seara and stayed the night with us once. He s'
	db	'eemed like a nice young man, but misguided."'
	db	00
L074A:	db	'Sasha'
	db	00
L0750:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L075B:	db	'"We do not get along very well with those people. I believe '
	db	'we have been unofficially marked as enemies of The Fellowshi'
	db	'p ever since all of the members of the Artist\'s Guild refus'
	db	'ed Elynor\'s invitation to join. They dislike us because the'
	db	'y consider us to be indisposed toward Unity."'
	db	00
L0877:	db	'"Dost thou think of us as thine enemy?"'
	db	00
L089F:	db	'"Then get out of my sight! I do not wish to speak with thee!'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L08DD:	db	'"Then I shall give thee the benefit of the doubt for now. Bu'
	db	't know that I do what I must to protect our Guild."'
	db	00
L094D:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0958:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L0961:	db	'"Owen the shipwright is commissioning a statue of himself to'
	db	' be built in the center of town. The Artist\'s Guild decided'
	db	' to have nothing to do with this foolishness, of course. But'
	db	' just the word of this statue has spread and now orders are '
	db	'coming in from all over Britannia. Merchants want to have a '
	db	'ship built by the \'famous\' Owen, master shipwright of Mino'
	db	'c."'
	db	00
L0ACA:	db	'statue'
	db	00
L0AD1:	db	'"Oh, yes, that reminds me! I cannot speak for long, I\'m afr'
	db	'aid. There is, after all, that barren slab in the center of '
	db	'town with nothing for it now. The Mayor has commissioned us '
	db	'to create something to fill the empty space. I don\'t want t'
	db	'o say anything about it other than it\'s going to be wonderf'
	db	'ul. It will not be ready for quite a while but once it is, I'
	db	' hope thou wilt be able to return to Minoc then and see it. '
	db	'In better times perhaps. Farewell, then."*'
	db	00
L0C9D:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L0CA6:	db	'statue'
	db	00
L0CAD:	db	'"I fear we have grievously miscalculated by thinking that if'
	db	' we boycotted the statue, it would not be built. It seems al'
	db	'l the talk of it has made Owen into some sort of bizarre leg'
	db	'end around this area, and the bloody statue hasn\'t even gon'
	db	'e up yet! But that, I fear, is not the worst of the situatio'
	db	'n."'
	db	00
L0DDC:	db	'statue'
	db	00
L0DE3:	db	'worst'
	db	00
L0DE9:	db	'worst'
	db	00
L0DEF:	db	'"Once the statue is built, orders for ship-building are boun'
	db	'd to increase even more! It won\'t take long before all loca'
	db	'l commerce will become affected by it. Owen will be purchasi'
	db	'ng more of the local resources, which will cause prices to r'
	db	'ise, especially at the sawmill, and that will surely force t'
	db	'he Artist\'s Guild into bankruptcy."'
	db	00
L0F3E:	db	'worst'
	db	00
L0F44:	db	'glass'
	db	00
L0F4A:	db	'"I regret that I do not have any of my work for sale at pres'
	db	'ent. Like our other artists I have a backlog of orders that '
	db	'will keep me busy for the foreseeable future. But there are '
	db	'several examples of my work, of which I am most proud, in th'
	db	'e Guild Hall on display. If thou art interested, please have'
	db	' a look at them."'
	db	00
L1088:	db	'glass'
	db	00
L108E:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1092:	db	'"Good journey, my friend."*'
	db	00
