	; Function at file offset 0007A4B3H
	.funcnumber  0459H
	.data
	.msize       111DH
	.dsize       0EF4H
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'brother'
	db	00
L0015:	db	'You see a mountain man who appears to have been in the wilde'
	db	'rness a long time. He gives you a long look, then he snorts '
	db	'and looks away.'
	db	00
L009D:	db	'"What dost thou want? Leave me alone!"'
	db	00
L00C4:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00C9:	db	'"I am not in the habit of speakin\' to strangers but seein'
	db	'\' as how thou dost not appear to be very intelligent, I sha'
	db	'll humor thee for now. My name is Karl, formerly of Minoc."'
	db	00
L0179:	db	'brother'
	db	00
L0181:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0186:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L018C:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0190:	db	'"Job?! Art thou mad, '
	db	00
L01A6:	db	'?! Firstly, if thou dost wish to offer me employment I have '
	db	'no interest in it. Secondly, if thou dost wish to hire my se'
	db	'rvices for anything for any reason, then I reject thine offe'
	db	'r most enthusiastically. Thirdly, if thou dost wonder what m'
	db	'y job is, then wonder no more for I have not one.\tFourth an'
	db	'd lastly, if thou dost wonder why I have no job then stop it'
	db	' right now because it is none of thy business!"*'
	db	00
L033E:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L0344:	db	'"Do not ask me of Minoc, the filthy little town of Fellowshi'
	db	'p fools, casual murders and monuments to incompetence. I do '
	db	'not even live here and I would not if thou didst pay me!"'
	db	00
L03F6:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L03FC:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0407:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L0410:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0418:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0420:	db	'"Hmmph. Why should that be any concern of mine? People kill '
	db	'each other every day. Oh, thou art investigating the crime! '
	db	'Well, do not let me keep thee from it. After thou dost catch'
	db	' the murderer thou canst build a statue of him."'
	db	00
L0505:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L050D:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0518:	db	'"Gads! Thou dost want me to join! Away from me, thou dolt!"*'
	db	00
L0555:	db	'"Do I look like a member of The Fellowship to thee? I do not'
	db	' even know what The Fellowship is! And I do not care!"*'
	db	00
L05C9:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L05D2:	db	'"Owen, the shipwright, dost deserve to have a monument built'
	db	' to him. It should be in the shape of a gallows and it shoul'
	db	'd have him hanging from it."*'
	db	00
L0668:	db	'brother'
	db	00
L0670:	db	'"My brother - mine only family in the world - served aboard '
	db	'a ship built by Owen. The ship was one of several that sank '
	db	'three years ago during the first storm it ever encountered. '
	db	'My brother went down with it and was never seen again."'
	db	00
L075C:	db	'brother'
	db	00
L0764:	db	'several ships'
	db	00
L0772:	db	'Owen'
	db	00
L0777:	db	'Owen'
	db	00
L077C:	db	'"I confronted Owen with this and he denied that it had anyth'
	db	'ing to do with his workmanship. I returned that night and st'
	db	'ole the plans he had drafted, so at least no other ships wou'
	db	'ld ever be built like them again. But it left me so angry at'
	db	' the world that I knew I could not live among people ever ag'
	db	'ain. I went away to live up in the mountains. The only times'
	db	' I ever come back are to fetch a few supplies and maybe have'
	db	' a drink of Rutherford\'s fine ale once in a while."'
	db	00
L0954:	db	'Owen'
	db	00
L0959:	db	'fine ale'
	db	00
L0962:	db	'plans'
	db	00
L0968:	db	'several ships'
	db	00
L0976:	db	'"Three other ships that were built from Owen\'s basic design'
	db	's all sunk within the first year of their launch. Over a doz'
	db	'en lives were lost due to that vainglorious bastard!"'
	db	00
L0A23:	db	'several ships'
	db	00
L0A31:	db	'fine ale'
	db	00
L0A3A:	db	'"If not for Rutherford\'s fine ale, there would no purpose t'
	db	'o the existence of civilization."'
	db	00
L0A97:	db	'fine ale'
	db	00
L0AA0:	db	'plans'
	db	00
L0AA6:	db	'"I still have those plans up in my cabin. Every once in a wh'
	db	'ile I try to figure them out. I suspect no one in town, save'
	db	' for Owen himself, could understand them. Maybe Julia, the t'
	db	'inker, would be able to shed some light on them. But she wou'
	db	'ld never listen to an old mountain man like me."'
	db	00
L0BC7:	db	'"Yes I would, Karl! Thou dost have too low opinion of thysel'
	db	'f! Raise thy spirits, please!"'
	db	00
L0C22:	db	'plans'
	db	00
L0C28:	db	'mountain man'
	db	00
L0C35:	db	'Julia'
	db	00
L0C3B:	db	'mountain man'
	db	00
L0C48:	db	'"Far away from the mire of present day society is where I be'
	db	'long. In the wilderness thou canst know what is what."'
	db	00
L0CBB:	db	'mountain man'
	db	00
L0CC8:	db	'Julia'
	db	00
L0CCE:	db	'"If thou dost want to show Julia the plans, I will give them'
	db	' to thee. They are in my cabin southeast of the BMC office."'
	db	00
L0D47:	db	'Julia'
	db	00
L0D4D:	db	'follow'
	db	00
L0D54:	db	'"Make up thy mind! Art thou following me or not?! If thou ar'
	db	't following me then close thy mouth, move thy feet and let u'
	db	's get on."'
	db	00
L0DD7:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0DDB:	db	'"I know I can be a bear to get along with sometimes. I recko'
	db	'n it is just my nature to be an ornery bastard. But I do app'
	db	'reciate what few friends I have and I know that thou hast be'
	db	'en one to me. Take good care of thyself, Avatar."*'
	db	00
L0EC2:	db	'"Cease thy racket then before I lose my temper!"*'
	db	00
