L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0015:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0021:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0026:	db	'You see a weary-looking man who is missing his right arm. Wi'
	db	'th his one hand he scratches his head and squints in your ge'
	db	'neral direction.'
	db	00
L00AF:	db	'"Oy, how ye been, '
	db	00
L00C2:	db	'?" Rutherford calls out to you.'
	db	00
L00E2:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00E7:	db	'He lets out a sharp cough to clear his throat. "Rutherford'
	db	'\'s me name. Pleased ta meet \'chur."~~ He extends his greas'
	db	'y hand for you to shake and does not retract it until it is '
	db	'clasped.'
	db	00
L01A0:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01A5:	db	'job'
	db	00
L01A9:	db	'"Why I be the barkeep of The Checquered Cork. No better plac'
	db	'e in Minoc to discuss the events of the day."'
	db	00
L0213:	db	'He coughs into the rag he had just been using to polish the '
	db	'bar.'
	db	00
L0254:	db	'"Hello again, Sir Dupre! Didst thou enjoy mine establishment'
	db	' so much that thou hast returned?"*'
	db	00
L02B4:	db	'"My dear Rutherford, this is not a reflection on The Checque'
	db	'red Cork, but I simply like a good drink!"*'
	db	00
L031C:	db	'room'
	db	00
L0321:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0325:	db	'events'
	db	00
L032C:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L0332:	db	'"\'Tis no time for idle chatter! There have been two people '
	db	'murdered over at William\'s sawmill!"'
	db	00
L0392:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0396:	db	'"We have a cornucopian variety of elixirs to quench thy tong'
	db	'ue and gourmet dishes to appease thy palate."'
	db	00
L0400:	db	'"As I have finished my workday, I ask thee to come back anot'
	db	'her time. Thou dost have my thanks."'
	db	00
L0461:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0465:	db	'room'
	db	00
L046A:	db	'"A room for the night is quite reasonable. Only 8 gold per p'
	db	'erson. Want one?"'
	db	00
L04B8:	db	'"Thou art carrying too much to take the room key, '
	db	00
L04EB:	db	'!"'
	db	00
L04EE:	db	'"Here is thy room key. It is good only until thou dost leave'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L052D:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough gold, eh? That be right bad."'
	db	00
L0566:	db	'"Mayhaps another night, then."'
	db	00
L0585:	db	'"If thou wouldst please make thy request at a time that was '
	db	'during my normal business hours, I would be most grateful."'
	db	00
L05FD:	db	'room'
	db	00
L0602:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L0608:	db	'"Yep, this town\'s usually bloody quiet. That was until rece'
	db	'ntly!" His squinting eye suddenly opens wide and stares stra'
	db	'ight at you.'
	db	00
L068C:	db	'"Say, when exackly again didst thou say thou didst arrive in'
	db	' town, stranger?"~~After a moment of carefully observing you'
	db	', he shrugs his shoulders and goes back to wiping off the ba'
	db	'r.'
	db	00
L0743:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L0749:	db	'events'
	db	00
L0750:	db	'"Before all this evil at the sawmill, the buzz were all abou'
	db	't the monument."'
	db	00
L079D:	db	'events'
	db	00
L07A4:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L07AC:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L07B5:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L07BD:	db	'"Well, I suppose that clears thee from the list o\' possible'
	db	' murderers. If\'n thou wert the murderer, thou wouldst not h'
	db	'ave to be askin\' questions o\'people about wha\' \'appened '
	db	'regardin\' the murders. Thou wouldst already know, havin\' b'
	db	'een there."'
	db	00
L08B1:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L08B9:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L08C1:	db	'"Say, thou be not from around here?" He looks at you skeptic'
	db	'ally. "Thou art not from the Fellowship by any chance, art t'
	db	'hou?"'
	db	00
L093F:	db	'"I thought so!"'
	db	00
L094F:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L095A:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0962:	db	'"Just askin\'! Thou dost not have to take any offense!"'
	db	00
L0999:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L09A4:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L09AC:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L09B4:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L09B9:	db	'"I know him! He be a pirate who lives in Buccaneer\'s Den. T'
	db	'hey say Hook is so mean he\'d kill his own mudder for the ri'
	db	'ght price, an\' I would wager they\'s right.~~"Why, I got in'
	db	'to a fight with this Hook once. I was lucky and I escaped lo'
	db	'sin\' only my right arm and still with one good eye left. It'
	db	' was somewhere around that time that I started having second'
	db	' thoughts about my career as a pirate and now here I be.'
	db	00
L0B55:	db	'"I have not seen him recently, but the description of the mu'
	db	'rder scene certainly sounds like his handiwork!"'
	db	00
L0BC2:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0BC7:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0BD3:	db	'"That ship was, indeed, here of late. In fact, \'twas the ni'
	db	'ght of the murders! Could there be a connection? Hmmm..."'
	db	00
L0C48:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0C54:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0C5F:	db	'"Thank goodness that with all the town at each others\' thro'
	db	'ats in recent weeks we have the Fellowship tryin\' to hold t'
	db	'he town together. I be no member or nothin\', but I just a'
	db	'\'heared of all the good things they done. Feedin\' the poor'
	db	' an\' such."'
	db	00
L0D54:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0D5F:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L0D68:	db	'"Oh, thou must mean thet statuer they are goin\' ta build of'
	db	' our shipwright. His name is Owen, a local boy. I understan'
	db	'\' it is to be as tall as a man on horseback and shows Owen '
	db	'gazin\' through a telerscope or some such thing like that."'
	db	00
L0E54:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L0E5D:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0E61:	db	'"I shall see thee later... At least I will if thou dost stay'
	db	' in the front o\' me good eye."*'
	db	00
