	; Function at file offset 000803E2H
	.funcnumber  045DH
	.data
	.msize       0B07H
	.dsize       0934H
L0000:	db	'William does not want to avert his attention from the Fellow'
	db	'ship meeting.*'
	db	00
L004B:	db	'"I must not stop to speak with thee now! I am late for the F'
	db	'ellowship meeting at the hall!"*'
	db	00
L00A8:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L00AC:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00B0:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00B5:	db	'You see a man with a very worried look on his face.'
	db	00
L00E9:	db	'"Avatar! What is it? Why dost thou want to talk to me again?'
	db	' What is wrong now?!" says William.'
	db	00
L0149:	db	'name'
	db	00
L014E:	db	'"I am called William, '
	db	00
L0165:	db	'."'
	db	00
L0168:	db	'name'
	db	00
L016D:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0171:	db	'"I work in the sawmill here in Minoc."'
	db	00
L0198:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L019E:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L01A6:	db	'"What a ludicrous question at a time like this! Why, I have '
	db	'just been given the fright of my life when I entered my sawm'
	db	'ill and saw those two who have not only been killed quite de'
	db	'ad, but torn apart nearly beyond recognition!"'
	db	00
L0289:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0291:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L0299:	db	'"I take the logs that are made from all the trees that are c'
	db	'ut down by the logger in Yew, and cut them into planks in th'
	db	'e local sawmill. Then I sell the planks - mostly to Owen the'
	db	' shipwright, and some to the Artist\'s Guild as well."'
	db	00
L0383:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L038B:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L0391:	db	'"It was such a quiet town until these murders happened. I ca'
	db	'nnot believe it."'
	db	00
L03DF:	db	'Minoc'
	db	00
L03E5:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L03ED:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L03F5:	db	'"I found the bodies first thing this morning when I went to '
	db	'open the sawmill. It took all of the discipline I have gaine'
	db	'd from the Triad of Inner Strength and the teachings of The '
	db	'Fellowship to keep from going mad at the sight of it. It mus'
	db	't have happened sometime last night but I swear to thee I ne'
	db	'ver heard a thing!"'
	db	00
L0535:	db	'"I swear by The Fellowship I have already told thee all I kn'
	db	'ow concerning the murders!"'
	db	00
L058D:	db	'murders'
	db	00
L0595:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L05A0:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L05AB:	db	'"I have been a member of The Fellowship for only a short tim'
	db	'e. I have only of late begun attending Elynor\'s meetings. O'
	db	'nly since they announced the monument was to be built."'
	db	00
L065A:	db	'"I am so glad thou art my brother in The Fellowship; I know '
	db	'I may trust thee. It is all of the others in this town that '
	db	'I worry about."'
	db	00
L06E2:	db	'"Wouldst thou like to know more of The Fellowship?"'
	db	00
L0716:	db	'"Trust me, thou canst not possibly understand how cruel and '
	db	'terrible life can be! Thou dost need The Fellowship! I am lu'
	db	'cky to have found it in time to face mine own moment of trut'
	db	'h! I hope thou dost realize that thou dost need The Fellowsh'
	db	'ip before it is too late!"'
	db	00
L0821:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L082C:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L0835:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L0840:	db	'philosophy'
	db	00
L084B:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L0854:	db	'"Thou dost know! The monument of Owen the shipwright standin'
	db	'g on the bow of a tall ship. Everyone in town doth know of i'
	db	't!"'
	db	00
L08D0:	db	'monument'
	db	00
L08D9:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L08DD:	db	'As soon as he has dismissed you, the overwrought William hid'
	db	'es his face in his hands.*'
	db	00
