	; Function at file offset 0008BA47H
	.funcnumber  046CH
	.data
	.msize       1385H
	.dsize       0F19H
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'The woman greets you with shining eyes.'
	db	00
L0035:	db	'"Hello, '
	db	00
L003E:	db	'," says Reyna.'
	db	00
L004D:	db	'cemetery'
	db	00
L0056:	db	'brought flowers'
	db	00
L0066:	db	'heal'
	db	00
L006B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0070:	db	'"I am Reyna," she says, brushing the hair out of her face.'
	db	00
L00AB:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00B0:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00B4:	db	'"I am a healer. I have chosen to set up shop here near the f'
	db	'orest."'
	db	00
L00F8:	db	'heal'
	db	00
L00FD:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L0104:	db	'animals'
	db	00
L010C:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L0113:	db	'"I wanted to live and work here because the land is very bea'
	db	'utiful. I have found many things to do and see. Unfortunatel'
	db	'y, the forest is so spread out that I have yet to meet many '
	db	'of the others who live in this area. I do know that the Abbe'
	db	'y is just across the way from mine house.~~"And somewhere ne'
	db	'arby is a scholar." She appears thoughtful for a moment. "Al'
	db	'so, I believe there is a prison just east of the Abbey.'
	db	00
L02B3:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L02BA:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L02C1:	db	'scholar'
	db	00
L02C9:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L02CF:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L02D6:	db	'"I\'ve never actually seen it," she laughs, "but rumor has i'
	db	't that the cells are located right next to the court, for qu'
	db	'ick, easy imprisonment after the trial."'
	db	00
L0376:	db	'prison'
	db	00
L037D:	db	'scholar'
	db	00
L0385:	db	'"From Aimi I have heard that he is brilliant, and... also a '
	db	'bit overzealous to instruct those interested in increasing t'
	db	'heir knowledge."'
	db	00
L040E:	db	'Aimi'
	db	00
L0413:	db	'scholar'
	db	00
L041B:	db	'Aimi'
	db	00
L0420:	db	'"She is the monk who tends the garden at the Abbey."'
	db	00
L0455:	db	'"She is one of the monks who lives at the Abbey. At this tim'
	db	'e, she is the only other person I have actually met here in '
	db	'the forest."'
	db	00
L04DA:	db	'Aimi'
	db	00
L04DF:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L04E5:	db	'"That is how this area -- Empath Abbey -- got its name, from'
	db	' the monks who live at the abbey of the Brotherhood of the R'
	db	'ose. They are said to make delicious wine. One of the monks '
	db	'cares for a beautiful garden in her spare time. In fact, I o'
	db	'ften buy flowers from her.~~ But," she grins, "as for the ot'
	db	'her monks, all that I\tever see them do is make wine and wan'
	db	'der the countryside."'
	db	00
L0662:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L0668:	db	'others'
	db	00
L066F:	db	'flowers'
	db	00
L0677:	db	'others'
	db	00
L067E:	db	'"Aimi is the only one I have met, but I know there are one o'
	db	'r two others who make wine there."'
	db	00
L06DD:	db	'Aimi'
	db	00
L06E2:	db	'others'
	db	00
L06E9:	db	'flowers'
	db	00
L06F1:	db	'"Yes, I get them for my mother."'
	db	00
L0712:	db	'mother'
	db	00
L0719:	db	'flowers'
	db	00
L0721:	db	'cemetery'
	db	00
L072A:	db	'mother'
	db	00
	db	00
L0732:	db	'I realize there are already \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tvery beautiful f'
	db	'lowers here, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tbut there can never be enough '
	db	'\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tto demonstrate how much she is \r\n\t\t\t\t'
	db	'\t\tmissed. '
	db	00
L07D1:	db	'She looks down at her feet, and then back up at you. It is o'
	db	'bvious she is fighting an urge to cry.~~ "Several months ago'
	db	', my mother passed away in her home town. She was born here '
	db	'in the forests, and had asked to be buried here, near me. Ev'
	db	'ery morning I come out here to visit her and set flowers by '
	db	'her grave.~~ "But," a lone tear escapes and trickles down he'
	db	'r cheek, "I am the only member of our family who lives nearb'
	db	'y. No one else is able to visit or leave flowers very often.'
	db	'~~"Her grave looks so bare sometimes." She looks off into th'
	db	'e horizon and sighs. "'
	db	00
L0A04:	db	'It would be nice\tif there were some way to have more flower'
	db	's brought to her."~~She quickly turns and looks at you.~~"I '
	db	'am terribly sorry for rambling on like that. Please excuse m'
	db	'e, '
	db	00
L0ABB:	db	'."'
	db	00
L0ABE:	db	'cemetery'
	db	00
L0AC7:	db	'mother'
	db	00
L0ACE:	db	'have flowers'
	db	00
L0ADB:	db	'have flowers'
	db	00
L0AE8:	db	'brought flowers'
	db	00
L0AF8:	db	'Her eyes light up as she sees the bouquet of flowers.~~ "The'
	db	'y are lovely! Thou art too kind, '
	db	00
L0B56:	db	', to bring flowers for my mother! I cannot wait to set them '
	db	'by her grave."'
	db	00
L0BA1:	db	'brought flowers'
	db	00
L0BB1:	db	'have flowers'
	db	00
L0BBE:	db	'heal'
	db	00
L0BC3:	db	'"For thy kindly gift of flowers, I will aid thee for half pr'
	db	'ice." She smiles at you.'
	db	00
L0C18:	db	'"I am sorry, '
	db	00
L0C26:	db	', but, unless this is an emergency, I would prefer to wait u'
	db	'ntil my shop is open."'
	db	00
L0C79:	db	'emergency'
	db	00
L0C83:	db	'emergency'
	db	00
L0C8D:	db	' and your companions'
	db	00
	db	00
L0CA3:	db	'She quickly examines you'
	db	00
L0CBC:	db	'.'
	db	00
L0CBE:	db	'"Thou art correct, '
	db	00
L0CD2:	db	'. This is a true emergency!"'
	db	00
L0CEF:	db	'heal'
	db	00
L0CF4:	db	'"I am sorry, but thy wounds are not mortal. Perhaps thou can'
	db	'st visit me when my shop is open."'
	db	00
L0D53:	db	'emergency'
	db	00
L0D5D:	db	'animals'
	db	00
L0D65:	db	'She smiles shyly.~~"I very much love animals. When I was ver'
	db	'y young, I found an ailing dove that I was unable to nurse b'
	db	'ack to health. Since that time, I began to study the healing'
	db	' arts, so that I would be able to help other animals who mig'
	db	'ht need healing.~~ "Of course," she laughs, "now that I have'
	db	' the skills, I use them to help people, too."'
	db	00
L0EBF:	db	'animals'
	db	00
L0EC7:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0ECB:	db	'"Goodbye, '
	db	00
L0ED6:	db	'.'
	db	00
L0ED8:	db	'"I thank thee for the bouquet!'
	db	00
L0EF7:	db	'"May health always follow thee!"*'
	db	00
