L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a monk wandering around apparently without direction'
	db	'.'
	db	00
L004B:	db	'"Greetings, '
	db	00
L0058:	db	'. May I help thee?" asks Wayne.'
	db	00
L0078:	db	'name'
	db	00
L007D:	db	'"Thou mayest call me Brother Wayne, '
	db	00
L00A2:	db	'."'
	db	00
L00A5:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00AA:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00AE:	db	'"My job? Well, I, er, do not truly have one at the moment." '
	db	'He looks down at his feet.'
	db	00
L0105:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0109:	db	'at the moment'
	db	00
L0117:	db	'at the moment'
	db	00
L0125:	db	'"Yes, I am... Well, I am lost, '
	db	00
L0145:	db	'. I am from the Abbey to the south of here... or to the nort'
	db	'h.... Mayhaps the northwest." He cradles his chin and looks '
	db	'up.~~"Southeast?"'
	db	00
L01CF:	db	'at the moment'
	db	00
L01DD:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L01E3:	db	'lost'
	db	00
L01E8:	db	'lost'
	db	00
L01ED:	db	'"Well... I am sure it is not permanent." He blushes. "I just'
	db	' need to get my bearings, that\'s all," he says unconvincing'
	db	'ly.'
	db	00
L0268:	db	'lost'
	db	00
L026D:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L0273:	db	'"I am a monk of the Brotherhood of the Rose. I study geograp'
	db	'hy and nature with a brother named Taylor."'
	db	00
L02DB:	db	'Abbey'
	db	00
L02E1:	db	'Taylor'
	db	00
L02E8:	db	'nature'
	db	00
L02EF:	db	'geography'
	db	00
L02F9:	db	'geography'
	db	00
L0303:	db	'"Well," he shrugs, "I suppose I should have studied a little'
	db	' bit better." He smiles sheepishly.'
	db	00
L0363:	db	'geography'
	db	00
L036D:	db	'nature'
	db	00
L0374:	db	'"There are so many beautiful things to see in Britannia. Bot'
	db	'h animals and plants alike offer excitement to the observer.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L03EE:	db	'nature'
	db	00
L03F5:	db	'plants'
	db	00
L03FC:	db	'animals'
	db	00
L0404:	db	'Taylor'
	db	00
L040B:	db	'"Well, I haven\'t actually seen him for some time. I assume '
	db	'he is still continuing his studies."'
	db	00
L046B:	db	'Taylor'
	db	00
L0472:	db	'plants'
	db	00
L0479:	db	'"Ah, yes, '
	db	00
L0484:	db	', they are quite wondrous to see. I highly recommend to thee'
	db	' to always observe thy surroundings. Otherwise, '
	db	00
L04F1:	db	', thou wilt miss much in life: flowers, trees, birds... land'
	db	'marks!"'
	db	00
L0535:	db	'plants'
	db	00
L053C:	db	'birds'
	db	00
L0542:	db	'trees'
	db	00
L0548:	db	'flowers'
	db	00
L0550:	db	'trees'
	db	00
L0556:	db	'"Ah, my least favorite subject. I find the trees much less i'
	db	'nteresting than the birds."'
	db	00
L05AE:	db	'trees'
	db	00
L05B4:	db	'birds'
	db	00
L05BA:	db	'"My favorite type of animal! The birds are so free, able to '
	db	'fly vast distances. How I wish I could roam about the open s'
	db	'kies... most especially considering my current situation. Th'
	db	'ou canst see so much more from the air, I am certain of it!"'
	db	00
L06AB:	db	'birds'
	db	00
L06B1:	db	'flowers'
	db	00
L06B9:	db	'"Very, very lovely plants. All the colors of the rainbow, an'
	db	'd then some. One of the monks at the Abbey had a lovely flow'
	db	'er garden. She may still tend it for all that I know, '
	db	00
L0768:	db	'."'
	db	00
L076B:	db	'flowers'
	db	00
L0773:	db	'She still does.'
	db	00
L0783:	db	'She still does.'
	db	00
L0793:	db	'"Excellent, '
	db	00
L07A0:	db	'. I am glad to hear it. \'Twould be a shame were Aimi to giv'
	db	'e that up for her other... pastime."'
	db	00
L0800:	db	'She still does.'
	db	00
L0810:	db	'other pastime'
	db	00
L081E:	db	'other pastime'
	db	00
L082C:	db	'"Aimi also paints. Or rather, makes a bold attempt. I must, '
	db	'of course, commend her for her efforts."'
	db	00
L0891:	db	'other pastime'
	db	00
L089F:	db	'animals'
	db	00
L08A7:	db	'"My favorite ones are the birds, especially the Golden-Cheek'
	db	'ed Warbler. I love to follow and watch them. They do not see'
	db	'm to have a very good sense of direction, however." He sighs'
	db	'. "But there is a great variety of species in this land."'
	db	00
L0995:	db	'animals'
	db	00
L099D:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L09A1:	db	'"May thy good fortune guide thee down the trail of life."*'
	db	00
