L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'Brother Wayne'
	db	00
L001B:	db	'You see a mage with a wild look in his eyes.'
	db	00
L0048:	db	'You see a mage with a peaceful look in his eyes.'
	db	00
L0079:	db	'"Thou art talking to me?" Garok asks, suspiciously.'
	db	00
L00AD:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00B2:	db	'The mage stares at you a moment. "Art thou from the Britanni'
	db	'an Tax Council?"'
	db	00
L00FF:	db	'"Then I am nobody!"*'
	db	00
L0114:	db	'"Good for thee. I would have had to kill thee. I am Garok Al'
	db	'-Mat. At least, the last time I looked in the mirror, that w'
	db	'as who I was!"'
	db	00
L019B:	db	'"I like thee already! I am Garok Al-Mat."'
	db	00
L01C5:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01CA:	db	'Tax Council'
	db	00
L01D6:	db	'job'
	db	00
L01DA:	db	'Garok looks as if he might suddenly tear out his hair, but h'
	db	'e restrains himself.~~"I am... -was-... a mage. Until it all'
	db	' went wrong. I am attempting to correct things."'
	db	00
L0283:	db	'correct'
	db	00
L028B:	db	'mage'
	db	00
L0290:	db	'"I am, and always have been, a mage. I was down here trying '
	db	'to locate what was amiss with the ethereal waves, but they s'
	db	'eem to be all right now."'
	db	00
L0322:	db	'ethereal waves'
	db	00
L0331:	db	'mage'
	db	00
L0336:	db	'mage'
	db	00
L033B:	db	'Garok suddenly hits himself on the side of the head.~~ "Get '
	db	'out! Damn thee! Out of there! No one invited thee into mine '
	db	'head! Away with thee!"~~Garok hits himself again, shakes his'
	db	' head like a wet dog and makes a blubbering sound with his l'
	db	'ips.~~Garok looks at you and smiles. "That\'s better. Now, w'
	db	'hat was it... oh yes, I remember. Thou dost not believe I am'
	db	' a mage? Well, I am. I live in the mountains. But now I am l'
	db	'ost in this wretched dungeon."'
	db	00
L04FD:	db	'lost'
	db	00
L0502:	db	'thine head'
	db	00
L050D:	db	'"I usually live in the mountains, but I am lost in this dung'
	db	'eon."'
	db	00
L054F:	db	'lost'
	db	00
L0554:	db	'mage'
	db	00
L0559:	db	'ethereal waves'
	db	00
L0568:	db	'correct'
	db	00
L0570:	db	'"My magic is not working!'
	db	00
L058A:	db	'"My magic was not working!'
	db	00
L05A5:	db	'"I attributed it to a disturbance in the ethereal waves! I h'
	db	'ad to find out what was happening. So here I am!"'
	db	00
L0613:	db	'ethereal waves'
	db	00
L0622:	db	'correct'
	db	00
L062A:	db	'thine head'
	db	00
L0635:	db	'"There is a voice in mine head. Some demon of some sort. It '
	db	'is always congratulating me on things. And then other times '
	db	'it scolds me for things. I -know- it is not my conscience. I'
	db	' -know- what -he- sounds like! This is... someone else."'
	db	00
L0722:	db	'thine head'
	db	00
L072D:	db	'voice'
	db	00
L0733:	db	'voice'
	db	00
L0739:	db	'"I started hearing it around the time my magic began to fail'
	db	'. I do not find it amusing."'
	db	00
L0792:	db	'voice'
	db	00
L0798:	db	'lost'
	db	00
L079D:	db	'"My crystal ball told me that the source of my problems was '
	db	'in a dungeon, but it did not say which one. This was the fir'
	db	'st dungeon I had ever explored. I have not found anything th'
	db	'at might help me, and I cannot find my way out!"'
	db	00
L0882:	db	'"I came down here to find the source of my problems. My crys'
	db	'tal ball told me that it was in a dungeon, but did not say w'
	db	'hich one. This is my first dungeon expedition, and now I am '
	db	'lost."'
	db	00
L093D:	db	'lost'
	db	00
L0942:	db	'wrong dungeon'
	db	00
L0950:	db	'way out'
	db	00
L0958:	db	'wrong dungeon'
	db	00
L0966:	db	'You explain to Garok that the Tetrahedron Generator is locat'
	db	'ed in Dungeon Deceit.~~"Hmmmm. Correct idea. Wrong dungeon."'
	db	00
L09DF:	db	'wrong dungeon'
	db	00
L09ED:	db	'way out'
	db	00
L09F5:	db	'"Dost thou know the way out?"'
	db	00
L0A13:	db	'You tell Garok how to get out of the dungeon.~~"Why, it soun'
	db	'ds so simple! My marbles must be losing me!~~ "I thank thee!'
	db	' Now I must be on my way. In fact, now that I know the way, '
	db	'I can use what little magic I have going for me to teleport.'
	db	' One must know the direction thou art travelling if one wish'
	db	'es to teleport!~~"Say, for helping me, wouldst thou like to '
	db	'have some useless reagents? By useless, I mean they are usel'
	db	'ess to me. They are probably perfectly good reagents. Thou a'
	db	'rt welcome to have them. Dost thou want them?"'
	db	00
L0C22:	db	'"Good. One less thing I have to carry."'
	db	00
L0C4A:	db	'"Oh. Thou dost not have the room. Too bad."'
	db	00
L0C76:	db	'Garok shrugs. "Suit thyself. Thanks anyway."'
	db	00
L0CA3:	db	'You watch as Garok turns, intones a spell, and vanishes.*'
	db	00
L0CDD:	db	'"Oh. Thou art as lost as I, eh? Then we shall surely die in '
	db	'here."'
	db	00
L0D20:	db	'way out'
	db	00
L0D28:	db	'Tax Council'
	db	00
L0D34:	db	'"Grrrr! They are a thorn in my side! They have been seeking '
	db	'me for the past three years! I neglected to report a certain'
	db	' amount of income for reagent distribution, and somehow they'
	db	' found me out. By the way, if thou shouldst ever care to vis'
	db	'it me in the mountains, I can sell thee reagents at reduced '
	db	'prices!"'
	db	00
L0E69:	db	'Tax Council'
	db	00
L0E75:	db	'Brother Wayne'
	db	00
L0E83:	db	'"Yes, I remember him! He is lost, too! Dost thou know if he '
	db	'found his way out? Give him my best when thou dost speak to '
	db	'him."'
	db	00
L0F01:	db	'Brother Wayne'
	db	00
L0F0F:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0F13:	db	'"Goodbye."*'
