L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a horse. "What else did you expect to see?"'
	db	00
L0041:	db	'"What now, '
	db	00
L004D:	db	'?" asks Smith.'
	db	00
L005C:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0061:	db	'"Yes, I have a name."'
	db	00
L0077:	db	'name'
	db	00
L007C:	db	'"Scoundrel! When thou art asked thy name, thou shouldst resp'
	db	'ond politely and accurately! The Avatar has just asked thee '
	db	'for -thy- name."'
	db	00
L0105:	db	'"My name? You can call\tme what you want, but I will only re'
	db	'spond to Smith."'
	db	00
L0151:	db	'Smith'
	db	00
L0157:	db	'-thy- name'
	db	00
L0162:	db	'-thy- name'
	db	00
L016D:	db	'"My name? You can call\tme what you want, but I will only re'
	db	'spond to Smith."'
	db	00
L01B9:	db	'Smith'
	db	00
L01BF:	db	'-thy- name'
	db	00
L01CA:	db	'job'
	db	00
L01CE:	db	'"Job? -Job-? I\'m a horse, what kind of job could I have?" H'
	db	'e looks off in the distance. "I can see it now: Smith -- Bak'
	db	'er extraordinaire.~~"Actually, I have gotten quite good at i'
	db	'nterior decorating. See how I arranged my abode? You like it'
	db	', don\'t you?"'
	db	00
L02CB:	db	'"Good. I will let you continue talking to me then! Which do '
	db	'you prefer, my living room or my bedroom?"'
	db	00
L0332:	db	'bedroom'
	db	00
L033A:	db	'living room'
	db	00
L0346:	db	'"That\'s funny, I feel the same way about you!"*'
	db	00
L0376:	db	'bedroom'
	db	00
L037E:	db	'living room'
	db	00
L038A:	db	'"You always did have bad taste!"'
	db	00
L03AB:	db	'bedroom'
	db	00
L03B3:	db	'living room'
	db	00
L03BF:	db	'Smith'
	db	00
L03C5:	db	'still want'
	db	00
L03D0:	db	'want'
	db	00
L03D5:	db	'"Yep, that\'s what I told you to call me. Oh, I get it! You '
	db	00
L0411:	db	' something from me, don\'t you?'
	db	00
L0430:	db	'"I thought as much. You\'ve always been a selfish one. What '
	db	'do you want? Now, let\'s see... Money? Advice?\tHappiness? N'
	db	'o, you usually want a clue of some sort, don\'t you. Of cour'
	db	'se, you may have become altruistic over the past 200 years..'
	db	'..~~"I know! You want to save Britannia!"'
	db	00
L0546:	db	'to save Britannia'
	db	00
L0558:	db	'happiness'
	db	00
L0562:	db	'a clue'
	db	00
L0569:	db	'advice'
	db	00
L0570:	db	'money'
	db	00
L0576:	db	'"Then what are you talking to me for?"*'
	db	00
L059E:	db	'money'
	db	00
L05A4:	db	'"From a horse? Right! Like I\'ve got some to give you."'
	db	00
L05DB:	db	'to save Britannia'
	db	00
L05ED:	db	'happiness'
	db	00
L05F7:	db	'a clue'
	db	00
L05FE:	db	'advice'
	db	00
L0605:	db	'money'
	db	00
L060B:	db	'advice'
	db	00
L0612:	db	'"Don\'t talk to horses!"*'
	db	00
L062B:	db	'happiness'
	db	00
L0635:	db	'"Who doesn\'t?"'
	db	00
L0644:	db	'to save Britannia'
	db	00
L0656:	db	'happiness'
	db	00
L0660:	db	'a clue'
	db	00
L0667:	db	'advice'
	db	00
L066E:	db	'money'
	db	00
L0674:	db	'to save Britannia'
	db	00
L0686:	db	'"You really expect me to believe that? You\'re just in this '
	db	'for the money."'
	db	00
L06D1:	db	'to save Britannia'
	db	00
L06E3:	db	'happiness'
	db	00
L06ED:	db	'a clue'
	db	00
L06F4:	db	'advice'
	db	00
L06FB:	db	'money'
	db	00
L0701:	db	'a clue'
	db	00
L0708:	db	'"Now we\'re getting to the nitty-gritty. O.K., I\'ll give yo'
	db	'u a clue, but what\'s in it for me? Let me guess. Money? Lov'
	db	'e? No, knowing you it\'s probably nothing. With any luck, yo'
	db	'u\'ll go away and leave me alone."'
	db	00
L07DA:	db	'to save Britannia'
	db	00
L07EC:	db	'happiness'
	db	00
L07F6:	db	'a clue'
	db	00
L07FD:	db	'advice'
	db	00
L0804:	db	'money'
	db	00
L080A:	db	'will not make you glue'
	db	00
L0821:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
L0829:	db	'love'
	db	00
L082E:	db	'money'
	db	00
L0834:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
L083C:	db	'"I\'ve already got that!"*'
	db	00
L0856:	db	'money'
	db	00
L085C:	db	'"Sure! Like I have a use for that!"*'
	db	00
L0881:	db	'love'
	db	00
L0886:	db	'"Sorry, I don\'t get into that."*'
	db	00
L08A7:	db	'will not make you glue'
	db	00
L08BE:	db	'"Threats, huh? And how do you expect me to respond to that? '
	db	'With courtesy and open hooves?~~ "Tell you what: you go away'
	db	' and leave me alone, and I\'ll tell you a clue. Fair?"'
	db	00
L096C:	db	'"Now we\'re talking! Done deal. Here we go." He checks aroun'
	db	'd to make sure no else is within earshot. "The gargoyles," h'
	db	'e pauses, "are not evil.~~"And Rasputin is a mean Martian. T'
	db	'here, that\'s it! Now get!"*'
	db	00
L0A3B:	db	'"Fine. I\'m not going to talk to you anyway!"*'
	db	00
L0A69:	db	'will not make you glue'
	db	00
L0A80:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0A84:	db	'"That\'s just fine. I was getting tired of you anyway."'
	db	00
L0ABB:	db	'"Why, how dare thou speakest to the Avatar in that manner, S'
	db	'mith!"'
	db	00
L0AFE:	db	'"And who are you? My master?"'
	db	00
L0B1C:	db	'"Why, as a matter of fact..."'
	db	00
L0B3A:	db	'"Sure, whatever."'
	db	00
L0B4C:	db	'*'
	db	00
