L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'Resting an axe on his shoulder, a tall, broad-chested man sm'
	db	'iles and nods at you.'
	db	00
L005F:	db	'"\'ello, '
	db	00
L0068:	db	'. Good day, ay?"'
	db	00
L0079:	db	'name'
	db	00
L007E:	db	'"Thou kin call me Ben, '
	db	00
L0096:	db	'. I live \'ere in the forest of Yew."'
	db	00
L00BB:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00C0:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L00C7:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
L00CB:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00CF:	db	'"I be a logger, '
	db	00
L00E0:	db	'. \'Tis what I have done all my life. In fact, '
	db	00
L010F:	db	', \'tis what my father did. And \'is father before \'im. And'
	db	' so on. We have been doin\' this for more than ten generatio'
	db	'ns."'
	db	00
L0188:	db	'Silverleaf'
	db	00
L0193:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
L0197:	db	'"It was once a large town, but now, \'tis but a smattering o'
	db	'f cottages livin\' throughout the woods."'
	db	00
L01FB:	db	'Yew'
	db	00
L01FF:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L0206:	db	'"I am afraid, '
	db	00
L0215:	db	', that I know no one in this area. But," he adds proudly, "I'
	db	' do know \'oo runs the sawmill in Minoc. I also know that mo'
	db	'nks reside in the abbey, next to the high court."'
	db	00
L02BE:	db	'high court'
	db	00
L02C9:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L02D1:	db	'forest'
	db	00
L02D8:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L02E0:	db	'"The sawyer there is named William."'
	db	00
L0305:	db	'sawmill'
	db	00
L030D:	db	'high court'
	db	00
L0318:	db	'"\'Tis in the building just northeast of the Brotherhood. I '
	db	'know they keep prisoners there."'
	db	00
L0374:	db	'high court'
	db	00
L037F:	db	'Silverleaf'
	db	00
L038A:	db	'"Why, yes, '
	db	00
L0396:	db	', I cut down Silverleaf trees. They only grow in one area, s'
	db	'o I \'afta travel quite a distance when I needs some of thei'
	db	'r wood. Why dost thou ask, '
	db	00
L0429:	db	'?~~"Oh, I see," he grins, "Thou wants some for thyself, ay?"'
	db	00
L0466:	db	'"I am sorry, '
	db	00
L0474:	db	', I do not know \'ow to prepare it. Perhaps thou shouldst tr'
	db	'y a pub."'
	db	00
L04B9:	db	'"Thou\'st got another reason for askin\'?"'
	db	00
L04E2:	db	'Emps'
	db	00
L04E7:	db	'"All right, '
	db	00
L04F4:	db	'," he shrugs.'
	db	00
L0502:	db	'one area'
	db	00
L050B:	db	'Silverleaf'
	db	00
L0516:	db	'one area'
	db	00
L051F:	db	'"They mainly populate the east part o\' the Great Forest, wa'
	db	'y on the other side."'
	db	00
L0570:	db	'one area'
	db	00
L0579:	db	'Emps'
	db	00
L057E:	db	'"What in the bloody \'ell are emps?"~~After you quickly expl'
	db	'ain the Silverleaf Tree situation to him, he exclaims, "Oh, '
	db	'well, that\'s \'orrible. I did not realize anyone -- er -- a'
	db	'ny other creature used the Silverleaf trees. What\tkin I do '
	db	'about it?"'
	db	00
L0675:	db	'sign contract'
	db	00
L0683:	db	'Emps'
	db	00
L0688:	db	'sign contract'
	db	00
L0696:	db	'"Why, o\' course I\'ll sign. No more Silverleaf trees for me'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L06D3:	db	'He takes the contract from you and signs it.'
	db	00
L0700:	db	'He turns to Trellek. "Please apologize to thy kindred for me'
	db	'. I never meant to destroy thine \'omes. Friends, ay?"~~ Tre'
	db	'llek smiles and nods.'
	db	00
L078D:	db	'"And please apologize to the Emps for me, '
	db	00
L07B8:	db	'. I never meant to destroy their \'omes."'
	db	00
L07E1:	db	'"Well, I would sign it, but it seems thou hast lost it. If t'
	db	'hou dost find it again I will be more than happy to help the'
	db	'e and the Emps."'
	db	00
L086A:	db	'sign contract'
	db	00
L0878:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L087C:	db	'"G\'bye, '
	db	00
L0885:	db	'. Pleasant journeys, ay."*'
	db	00
