L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'The beady-eyed man sneers at you.'
	db	00
L002F:	db	'"What dost thou want now?" Goth spits.'
	db	00
L0056:	db	'buy keys'
	db	00
L005F:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0064:	db	'"Goth. Not that it is any of thy business!"'
	db	00
L0090:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0095:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0099:	db	'"What does it look like I do?" he says, holding up a ring of'
	db	' keys. "Gardening?"'
	db	00
L00E9:	db	'gardening'
	db	00
L00F3:	db	'keys'
	db	00
L00F8:	db	'gardening'
	db	00
L0102:	db	'"What? Art thou daft?" He shakes his head. "Well, at least t'
	db	'hou art in the right area for gardening."'
	db	00
L0168:	db	'area'
	db	00
L016D:	db	'gardening'
	db	00
L0177:	db	'area'
	db	00
L017C:	db	'"Empath Abbey, dolt!"'
	db	00
L0192:	db	'Empath Abbey'
	db	00
L019F:	db	'area'
	db	00
L01A4:	db	'Empath Abbey'
	db	00
L01B1:	db	'"As a matter of fact,  know quite a bit about the people who'
	db	' live here. And I just might even tell thee. What is it wort'
	db	'h to thee in gold?"'
	db	00
L023D:	db	'5'
	db	00
L023F:	db	'4'
	db	00
L0241:	db	'3'
	db	00
L0243:	db	'2'
	db	00
L0245:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
L024D:	db	'Empath Abbey'
	db	00
L025A:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
L0262:	db	'"Fine by me!"'
	db	00
L0270:	db	'4'
	db	00
L0272:	db	'3'
	db	00
L0274:	db	'2'
	db	00
L0276:	db	'He glowers at you. "Thou must do better than that, fool!"'
	db	00
L02B0:	db	'5'
	db	00
L02B2:	db	'"I will tell thee what I know: Sir Jeff is in charge of the '
	db	'High Court. \'E\'s a real mean bastard, so I would stay away'
	db	' from \'im. The monks nearby make excellent wine, and Aimi d'
	db	'oth warm a man\'s... heart. And whatever thou dost, do not w'
	db	'aste time talking to the undertaker -- \'e\'s daft in the he'
	db	'ad."'
	db	00
L03DD:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough gold, toad."'
	db	00
L0405:	db	'5'
	db	00
L0407:	db	'4'
	db	00
L0409:	db	'3'
	db	00
L040B:	db	'2'
	db	00
L040D:	db	'keys'
	db	00
L0412:	db	'"These? They are for the prisoner\'s cells, witless knave!"'
	db	00
L044D:	db	'buy keys'
	db	00
L0456:	db	'prisoners'
	db	00
L0460:	db	'keys'
	db	00
L0465:	db	'prisoners'
	db	00
L046F:	db	'"I will tell thee for 5 gold. Interested?"'
	db	00
L049A:	db	'"One of them is named D\'Rel. E\'s a pirate, from Buccaneer'
	db	'\'s Den."'
	db	00
L04DC:	db	'another prisoner'
	db	00
L04ED:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough money, stonehead."'
	db	00
L051B:	db	'"Pinchpenny!"*'
	db	00
L052A:	db	'prisoners'
	db	00
L0534:	db	'another prisoner'
	db	00
L0545:	db	'"Another, eh. Hast thou 5 more gold for me?"'
	db	00
L0572:	db	'"The other one is a troll. \'E don\'t talk much, but\t\'e\'s'
	db	' the first troll prisoner I have ever seen."'
	db	00
L05D6:	db	'another prisoner'
	db	00
L05E7:	db	'"Thou canst not fool me, brainless dolt. Thou dost not have '
	db	'enough gold!"'
	db	00
L0631:	db	'"Fine, slug!"*'
	db	00
L0640:	db	'another prisoner'
	db	00
L0651:	db	'buy keys'
	db	00
L065A:	db	'"Thou dost want these, eh?" he asks, holding up keys. "\'Twi'
	db	'll cost thee... 20 gold. Still want them?"'
	db	00
L06C0:	db	'"Done!"'
	db	00
L06C8:	db	'buy keys'
	db	00
L06D1:	db	'He smiles cruelly. "I am afraid thou dost not have enough go'
	db	'ld."'
	db	00
L0712:	db	'"Fine. Rot for all I care!*'
	db	00
L072E:	db	'buy keys'
	db	00
L0737:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L073B:	db	'"Indeed, knave. Get thee gone!"*'
	db	00
