L000D:	db	'winnings'
	db	00
L0016:	db	'You see a disgruntled, obviously overworked barmaid. She giv'
	db	'es you a perfunctory grunt of a hello.'
	db	00
L0079:	db	'"Art thou still here?" she asks Dupre.'
	db	00
L00A0:	db	'"I have not finished making mine assessment of thy fine drin'
	db	'king establishment!"*'
	db	00
L00F2:	db	'"What? Art thou working for Brommer\'s Britannia travel guid'
	db	'es?"*'
	db	00
L0133:	db	'"No, my dear. This research is strictly for mine own digesti'
	db	'on!"*'
	db	00
L0175:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
	db	00
L0189:	db	'. Rest and take a load off."'
	db	00
L01A6:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01AB:	db	'"I am Daphne."'
	db	00
L01BA:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01BF:	db	'job'
	db	00
L01C3:	db	'"That is an easy one. I am the workhorse in residence of the'
	db	' Bunk and Stool. While our resident princess flirts with the'
	db	' customers I do all the cooking, cleaning and serving."'
	db	00
L0273:	db	'room'
	db	00
L0278:	db	'Bunk and Stool'
	db	00
L0287:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L028B:	db	'princess'
	db	00
L0294:	db	'workhorse'
	db	00
L029E:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L02A2:	db	'"Sorry, '
	db	00
L02AB:	db	', I do not sell food and drink at this time."'
	db	00
L02D9:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L02DD:	db	'workhorse'
	db	00
L02E7:	db	'"Ever since the owner, Sprellic, got himself into trouble wi'
	db	'th the Library of Scars, there hath been no one else to run '
	db	'the place. Ohh, mine aching back!"'
	db	00
L0382:	db	'workhorse'
	db	00
L038C:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L039D:	db	'Sprellic'
	db	00
L03A6:	db	'princess'
	db	00
L03AF:	db	'"Hmmph! That would be Ophelia."'
	db	00
L03CF:	db	'princess'
	db	00
L03D8:	db	'Ophelia'
	db	00
L03E0:	db	'room'
	db	00
L03E5:	db	'"Thou shalt have to ask Ophelia about that. My domain is the'
	db	' kitchen!"'
	db	00
L042C:	db	'room'
	db	00
L0431:	db	'Ophelia'
	db	00
L0439:	db	'"Ophelia this! Ophelia that! That is all I ever hear all blo'
	db	'ody day! If all thou dost want to talk about is her, talk to'
	db	' someone else!"'
	db	00
L04C1:	db	'"Do not hate me just because I am beautiful, Daphne."*'
	db	00
L04F8:	db	'"That is not the reason I hate thee, Ophelia!"*'
	db	00
L0528:	db	'"Oh, yes, I remember now. Thou dost hate me because I am bea'
	db	'utiful, and thou art not!"*'
	db	00
L0580:	db	'"Thank thee so much, '
	db	00
L0596:	db	', for bringing up my favorite subject."*'
	db	00
L05BF:	db	'Ophelia'
	db	00
L05C7:	db	'Bunk and Stool'
	db	00
L05D6:	db	'"The Bunk and Stool is where the fighters and ruffians come '
	db	'to drink in Jhelom. \'Tis not an easy job keeping such a lot'
	db	' happy with all their drinking and duelling and gambling."'
	db	00
L0688:	db	'Bunk and Stool'
	db	00
L0697:	db	'gambling'
	db	00
L06A0:	db	'Sprellic'
	db	00
L06A9:	db	'"The fool was caught stealing the honor flag from the wall o'
	db	'f the Library of Scars! Now the three students who challenge'
	db	'd him will kill him on the duelling field. \'Tis a tragedy."'
	db	00
L075D:	db	'Sprellic'
	db	00
L0766:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L0777:	db	'"That is the fighting club in Jhelom which produces perhaps '
	db	'the toughest fighters in all Britannia. Sprellic has never f'
	db	'ought before in his entire life."'
	db	00
L0811:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L0822:	db	'gambling'
	db	00
L082B:	db	'"I am sorry. All bets are off since the matter has been reso'
	db	'lved."'
	db	00
L086E:	db	'"In fact, I am taking bets on the upcoming duels. Dost thou '
	db	'wish to bet that Sprellic will lose to any of the three othe'
	db	'r duellists?"'
	db	00
L08F4:	db	'"How much wouldst thou like to bet?"'
	db	00
L0919:	db	'"Perhaps thou art not truly serious about thy convictions. M'
	db	'ayhaps the princess will take thy line of bets."'
	db	00
L0986:	db	'"Thou wouldst bet '
	db	00
L0999:	db	' gold that Sprellic will lose?"'
	db	00
L09B9:	db	'"Very well. How much wouldst thou like to bet?"'
	db	00
L09E9:	db	'"Very well. Let me give thee markers for thy gold. Each one '
	db	'is worth 10 gold coins. If Sprellic loses, thou mayest come '
	db	'collect twice that amount of gold from me.~~"Should he win, '
	db	00
L0A9E:	db	', thy markers are, of course, worthless."'
	db	00
L0AC8:	db	'"Thou mayest come see me after the duels and exchange this m'
	db	'arker for thy winnings if thou hast won."'
	db	00
L0B2E:	db	'"Oh! Thou must return later when thou hast enough room in th'
	db	'y pack for these markers."'
	db	00
L0B85:	db	'"Thou hast not the amount of gold thou dost want to bet! Art'
	db	' thou trying to swindle me?"'
	db	00
L0BDE:	db	'"Then if thou wouldst like to bet in favor of Sprellic, thou'
	db	' mayest see Ophelia, but I warn thee thou wilt be throwing t'
	db	'hy money away!"'
	db	00
L0C66:	db	'gambling'
	db	00
L0C6F:	db	'winnings'
	db	00
L0C78:	db	'"Here are thy winnings, '
	db	00
L0C91:	db	'. But I have reason to believe that thou wert the one who ki'
	db	'lled poor Sprellic! If this is the way that thou makest thy '
	db	'money, then thou shouldst be ashamed!"'
	db	00
L0D30:	db	'"Thou cannot possibly carry all that gold. Thou must come ba'
	db	'ck when I can give thee the proper amount of gold!"'
	db	00
L0DA0:	db	'winnings'
	db	00
L0DA9:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0DAD:	db	'"Enjoy thyself."*'
	db	00
