	; Function at file offset 0009C693H
	.funcnumber  047DH
	.data
	.msize       0F1DH
	.dsize       0CB8H
L0000:	db	'You see a fighting man. His voice booms like thunder as he g'
	db	'reets you. "Hail to thee, '
	db	00
L0057:	db	'!"'
	db	00
L005A:	db	'"So, once again, I am at thy service," bellows Vokes.'
	db	00
L0090:	db	'"If thou wouldst return the honor flag of the Library of Sca'
	db	'rs, then it is only proper that is turned back over to Syria'
	db	', who was guarding it when it was stolen. Please do so."*'
	db	00
L0142:	db	'"So, thou wishest to fight for the cowardly Sprellic! Then I'
	db	' have no choice but to finish thee myself!"*'
	db	00
L01AB:	db	'"So, thou wishes to fight for the cowardly Sprellic! Meet us'
	db	' at the duelling area at next noon!"'
	db	00
L020C:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0210:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0214:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0219:	db	'name'
	db	00
L021E:	db	'"My name is Vokes, '
	db	00
L0232:	db	'. As big as a mountain, as strong as an ox, as fierce as... '
	db	'well, more fierce than anything thou hast ever fought!"'
	db	00
L02A6:	db	'name'
	db	00
L02AB:	db	'job'
	db	00
L02AF:	db	'"Job! I am not in the habit of plowing fields or peddling ve'
	db	'getables, '
	db	00
L02F6:	db	'! I earn my gold with this sword arm," he says as he flexes '
	db	'a mighty bicep. "Right now I am in Jhelom continuing my stud'
	db	'ies in my trade with De Snel, and when I am finished my pric'
	db	'e is going to go up!"'
	db	00
L03C0:	db	'Jhelom'
	db	00
L03C7:	db	'Jhelom'
	db	00
L03CE:	db	'"I was born here! Is it not magnificent?! Why, in any hour o'
	db	'f any day thou canst get into a duel with anyone for no reas'
	db	'on at all! Now that is what I call the benefits of civilizat'
	db	'ion!"'
	db	00
L0488:	db	'duel'
	db	00
L048D:	db	'Jhelom'
	db	00
L0494:	db	'duel'
	db	00
L0499:	db	'"A responsibility, yes, even a necessity. The cost of being '
	db	'honorable is that one must defend one\'s honor. There is no '
	db	'telling just where or when the next stain on one\'s honor ma'
	db	'y appear. Like this Sprellic fool, for instance. The perfect'
	db	' example!"*'
	db	00
L0593:	db	'"I\'ll make a stain on his honor, that\'s for sure. A blood '
	db	'red one!"*'
	db	00
L05D8:	db	'Sprellic'
	db	00
L05E1:	db	'duel'
	db	00
L05E6:	db	'Sprellic'
	db	00
L05EF:	db	'"The bloody idiot had no idea that when he took our honor fl'
	db	'ag he would be seen doing it. Hence, he never considered the'
	db	' fact that he would have to fight a duel over our sullied ho'
	db	'nor. But now that the whole town is talking of the incident '
	db	'there is no way that we could refrain from standing up for o'
	db	'urselves. Especially since he has refused to return what he '
	db	'has taken from us."*'
	db	00
L076C:	db	'"Were he not such a cad, he would see the foolishness of his'
	db	' actions. \'Tis now up to us to show him!"*'
	db	00
L07D3:	db	'honor flag'
	db	00
L07DE:	db	'misunderstanding'
	db	00
L07EF:	db	'"If he had not returned the honor flag to us we would have h'
	db	'ad to kill him dead as sure as I am standing here."'
	db	00
L085F:	db	'Sprellic'
	db	00
L0868:	db	'honor flag'
	db	00
L0873:	db	'"There is a widely known and long-standing tradition concern'
	db	'ing the honor flag of the Library of Scars. It is said that '
	db	'taking the flag from the wall is a signal meaning that the p'
	db	'erson who takes the flag can beat anyone who studies at the '
	db	'school in a fight. It is also a grossly insulting way of say'
	db	'ing that thou dost think the method of fighting a school tea'
	db	'ches is inferior, which the Library of Scars most certainly '
	db	'is not!"'
	db	00
L0A20:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L0A31:	db	'honor flag'
	db	00
L0A3C:	db	'misunderstanding'
	db	00
L0A4D:	db	'"I have heard that rot about it all being a misunderstanding'
	db	'. The only thing misunderstood is how bad Sprellic will look'
	db	' when we finish with him!"'
	db	00
L0AE0:	db	'misunderstanding'
	db	00
L0AF1:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L0B02:	db	'"The Library of Scars teaches the supreme fighting style! On'
	db	'e that enables thee to get the advantage against thine oppon'
	db	'ents and soundly defeat them through the brilliantly conceiv'
	db	'ed subterfuge of Master De Snel!"'
	db	00
L0BD8:	db	'De Snel'
	db	00
L0BE0:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L0BF1:	db	'De Snel'
	db	00
L0BF9:	db	'"He is a genius. Perhaps the greatest military mind that eve'
	db	'r lived. He told us so!"'
	db	00
L0C4E:	db	'De Snel'
	db	00
L0C56:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0C5A:	db	'"If I am not killed and thou art not killed perhaps we may r'
	db	'aise a\tglass together some day!"*'
	db	00
