L0000:	db	'You see a very serious young man. He carries himself like a '
	db	'learned and mannered gentleman.'
	db	00
L005C:	db	'"Dost thou wish to speak with me?" asks Timmons.'
	db	00
L008D:	db	'"I see thou hast the honor flag. As little more than an inte'
	db	'rested third party in this affair, I ask thee to return the '
	db	'flag to Syria. Please do so."*'
	db	00
L0124:	db	'"Well, '
	db	00
L012C:	db	', I must prove myself to De Snel. If thou art the one who su'
	db	'ffers, I will apologize, but I will not back down!"'
	db	00
L019C:	db	'"Prepare to die!"*'
	db	00
L01AF:	db	'"Well, '
	db	00
L01B7:	db	', I must prove myself to De Snel. If thou art the one who su'
	db	'ffers, so be it! Meet us at the dueling area at next noon!"*'
	db	00
L0230:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0234:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0238:	db	'name'
	db	00
L023D:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0242:	db	'"Timmons is my name, '
	db	00
L0258:	db	'."'
	db	00
L025B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0260:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0264:	db	'"At the moment I have no job. I left all that behind in New '
	db	'Magincia. I have come to Jhelom to study under Master De Sne'
	db	'l in the Library of Scars."'
	db	00
L02F8:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L0309:	db	'Jhelom'
	db	00
L0310:	db	'Jhelom'
	db	00
L0317:	db	'"I am afraid I would not be able to help thee. I know little'
	db	' of this town, except for the duels. I am newly arrived here'
	db	' myself. Perhaps thou shouldst ask someone else."'
	db	00
L03C1:	db	'duels'
	db	00
L03C7:	db	'Jhelom'
	db	00
L03CE:	db	'duels'
	db	00
L03D4:	db	'"I had heard of this man Sprellic who claims he is a greater'
	db	' fighter than any in the Library of Scars and how he had sto'
	db	'len the honor flag from their wall. So I sought this man out'
	db	' and challenged him to a duel myself."'
	db	00
L04AF:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L04C0:	db	'"Unfortunately, the duels with Sprellic were called off befo'
	db	're I had the opportunity to impress Master De Snel."'
	db	00
L0531:	db	'duels'
	db	00
L0537:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L0548:	db	'"A sailor on a ship at port in New Magincia first told me of'
	db	' the Library of Scars, of how it was the greatest fighting g'
	db	'uild in Britannia and how its trainer, Master De Snel, had c'
	db	'reated the perfect fighting style. I immediately spent every'
	db	' coin I had to come here. But De Snel now refuses to accept '
	db	'me as a student. I know if I can defeat a fighter who claims'
	db	' to be better than anyone in the guild, and help restore its'
	db	' honor in the process, De Snel will have to finally accept m'
	db	'e."'
	db	00
L072C:	db	'"Master De Snel, the trainer at the Library of Scars, has re'
	db	'fused me entry until I have proven myself in combat. The onl'
	db	'y way to prove oneself in combat in the town of Jhelom is by'
	db	' duelling. But my mother raised me to be a perfect gentleman'
	db	'. So far I have not succeeded in offending anyone sufficient'
	db	'ly to have them challenge me to a duel. Hmmm. Perhaps I am j'
	db	'ust not suited to be a member of the Library of Scars."'
	db	00
L08CC:	db	'Library of Scars'
	db	00
L08DD:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L08E1:	db	'"It was a pleasure speaking to thee, '
	db	00
L0907:	db	'."*'
	db	00
