L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'locket'
	db	00
L0014:	db	'medallion'
	db	00
L001E:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L002A:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L002F:	db	'strangers'
	db	00
L0039:	db	'Before you is a shrewd-looking craftsman, obviously filled w'
	db	'ith the contentment of a peaceful life.'
	db	00
L009D:	db	'"What may I do for thee?" says Russell.'
	db	00
L00C5:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00CA:	db	'"I am Russell, a shipwright."'
	db	00
L00E8:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00ED:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00F1:	db	'"I build ships in New Magincia. It is a profession I enjoy v'
	db	'ery much. I also sell deeds for my ships, and sextants by wh'
	db	'ich one can navigate the open seas."'
	db	00
L018E:	db	'sextants'
	db	00
L0197:	db	'deeds'
	db	00
L019D:	db	'New Magincia'
	db	00
L01AA:	db	'deeds'
	db	00
L01B0:	db	'"But I have already sold thee the deed to \'The Nymphet\'! I'
	db	' am afraid that was the only ship I had at this time."'
	db	00
L0221:	db	'"Thou wishest to purchase my ship \'The Nymphet\'? The deed '
	db	'will cost thee 600 gold."'
	db	00
L0275:	db	'"\'The Nymphet\' is thine, '
	db	00
L028F:	db	'. Enjoy the waters."'
	db	00
L02A4:	db	'"Thou art carrying too much to take thy deed. Come back afte'
	db	'r putting some things down."'
	db	00
L02FD:	db	'"Mine apologies, '
	db	00
L030F:	db	', thou dost not have enough gold."'
	db	00
L0332:	db	'"I understand, '
	db	00
L0342:	db	', the seas aren\'t for everyone."'
	db	00
L0363:	db	'"When my shop is again open I shall be more than happy to he'
	db	'lp thee."'
	db	00
L03A9:	db	'deeds'
	db	00
L03AF:	db	'sextants'
	db	00
L03B8:	db	'"Thou wishest to purchase one of my fine sextants? \'Twill c'
	db	'ost thee 40 gold."'
	db	00
L0406:	db	'"\'Tis thine, '
	db	00
L0414:	db	'. Enjoy the waters."'
	db	00
L0429:	db	'"I would gladly give thee thy sextant but thou shalt have to'
	db	' put something down! Thou art carrying\ttoo much to take it.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L04A2:	db	'"Mine apologies, '
	db	00
L04B4:	db	', thou dost not have enough gold."'
	db	00
L04D7:	db	'"I understand, '
	db	00
L04E7:	db	', some of us can navigate with just the naked stars!"'
	db	00
L051D:	db	'"At present my shop is closed. If thou wilt come back during'
	db	' business hours I shall be more than happy to help thee."'
	db	00
L0593:	db	'sextants'
	db	00
L059C:	db	'New Magincia'
	db	00
L05A9:	db	'"Things have been very peaceful in New Magincia. There has b'
	db	'een little trouble from outsiders lately."'
	db	00
L0610:	db	'outsiders'
	db	00
L061A:	db	'New Magincia'
	db	00
L0627:	db	'outsiders'
	db	00
L0631:	db	'"Before thine arrival there had not been a stranger in New M'
	db	'agincia for years, save for the survivors of the shipwreck."'
	db	00
L06AA:	db	'shipwreck'
	db	00
L06B4:	db	'outsiders'
	db	00
L06BE:	db	'shipwreck'
	db	00
L06C8:	db	'"I found the wreckage. Three men were clinging to it for the'
	db	'ir lives."'
	db	00
L070F:	db	'three men'
	db	00
L0719:	db	'wreckage'
	db	00
L0722:	db	'shipwreck'
	db	00
L072C:	db	'wreckage'
	db	00
L0735:	db	'"I had never seen a ship like it before. The markings show i'
	db	't was constructed by a Minoc shipwright named Owen. It was n'
	db	'ot very well constructed."'
	db	00
L07C8:	db	'wreckage'
	db	00
L07D1:	db	'strangers'
	db	00
L07DB:	db	'three men'
	db	00
L07E5:	db	'"They were from Buccaneer\'s Den. Most people that come here'
	db	' come because they are lost on their way to or from Buccanee'
	db	'r\'s Den."'
	db	00
L0866:	db	'Buccaneer\'s Den'
	db	00
L0876:	db	'three men'
	db	00
L0880:	db	'strangers'
	db	00
L088A:	db	'Buccaneer\'s Den'
	db	00
L089A:	db	'"The three men wish to go back. They say there is a house of'
	db	' games in Buccaneer\'s Den." Russell shrugs. "As if that wou'
	db	'ld be a reason to go there.'
	db	00
L092D:	db	'"I offered to sell them a ship, but they had no money. They '
	db	'actually seemed offended when I would not give it to them fo'
	db	'r free!"'
	db	00
L09AE:	db	'Buccaneer\'s Den'
	db	00
L09BE:	db	'locket'
	db	00
L09C5:	db	'"The three strangers tried to offer me some kind of trinket '
	db	'to build or sell them a ship. It sounds like the locket thou'
	db	' art describing."'
	db	00
L0A4F:	db	'trinket'
	db	00
L0A57:	db	'locket'
	db	00
L0A5E:	db	'trinket'
	db	00
L0A66:	db	'"I would not have accepted their offer, but I was curious. L'
	db	'ater they said nothing when I wanted to see the trinket agai'
	db	'n. I doubt they have it."'
	db	00
L0AF8:	db	'trinket'
	db	00
L0B00:	db	'medallion'
	db	00
L0B0A:	db	'"I could not help noticing your medallion. It does look some'
	db	'what sinister. I cannot recall ever having seen one like it '
	db	'before."'
	db	00
L0B8B:	db	'medallion'
	db	00
L0B95:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0BA1:	db	'"The Crown Jewel just left here a short while ago. I do not '
	db	'know where it was headed."'
	db	00
L0BF8:	db	'"I have heard nothing more of the Crown Jewel since we last '
	db	'spoke of it."'
	db	00
L0C42:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0C4E:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0C53:	db	'"Just as the Crown Jewel left I saw a man with a hook jump o'
	db	'n board. There was a gargoyle accompanying him."'
	db	00
L0CC0:	db	'"I have heard nothing more of this man Hook since we last sp'
	db	'oke of him."'
	db	00
L0D09:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0D0E:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0D12:	db	'"Fare thee well, '
	db	00
L0D24:	db	'."*'
	db	00
