	; Function at file offset 000ACFB2H
	.funcnumber  048DH
	.data
	.msize       154DH
	.dsize       11F6H
L0000:	db	'You attempt to speak to the undead creature, but it does not'
	db	', or cannot, respond.*'
	db	00
L0053:	db	'The Liche practically glows, power coursing visibly through '
	db	'its undead veins.'
	db	00
L00A1:	db	'You step forward to confront this vile-looking creature and '
	db	'he slowly turns to face you. As his intense gaze locks onto '
	db	'your form, you almost wish you hadn\'t been so bold.~~ "'
	db	00
L0151:	db	'." A sardonic expression comes to his undead features. "How '
	db	'may I help thee?" You get the distinct impression that help '
	db	'is the last thing you\'ll get from the Liche.'
	db	00
L01F6:	db	'Shamino steps near you and speaks in a whispered tone.~~"Do '
	db	'not trust this one, '
	db	00
L0247:	db	'. Methinks he\'ll cause naught but evil."'
	db	00
L0270:	db	'Iolo steps near you and speaks in a whispered tone.~~"Do not'
	db	' trust this one, '
	db	00
L02BE:	db	'. Methinks he\'ll cause naught but evil."'
	db	00
L02E7:	db	'"Uh, '
	db	00
L02ED:	db	'? I am ready to go now," he says to you, cowering from the u'
	db	'ndead creature.*'
	db	00
L033A:	db	'The Liche performs something akin to a smile and speaks with'
	db	' a sarcastic flair.~~"Ah, the wondrous Avatar has returned. '
	db	'What have I done to deserve such an honor?" The word "honor"'
	db	' sours on this creature\'s tongue.'
	db	00
L0410:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0414:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0418:	db	'name'
	db	00
L041D:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0422:	db	'The Liche\'s dry features take on a haughty appearance. "Tho'
	db	'u mayest call me Lord Horance. It would only be prudent, as '
	db	'I shall one day rule all of Britannia.~~ "Surprised, Avatar?'
	db	' Come now. Surely thou dost not think that Lord British will'
	db	' stand in my way. I know how to deal with his ilk."'
	db	00
L0545:	db	'name'
	db	00
L054A:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0557:	db	'Lord Horance'
	db	00
L0564:	db	'Lord Horance'
	db	00
L0571:	db	'"Ah, it is good to hear such an obeisance from the Avatar. P'
	db	'erhaps thou wilt have a place in my New Order." The Liche lo'
	db	'oks at you with an expression somewhere between malice and h'
	db	'umor.'
	db	00
L062B:	db	'Lord Horance'
	db	00
L0638:	db	'New Order'
	db	00
L0642:	db	'obeisance'
	db	00
L064C:	db	'obeisance'
	db	00
L0656:	db	'"Why, what else wouldst thou call it? Surely thou art truly '
	db	'humbled by my `majestic\' presence."'
	db	00
L06B6:	db	'obeisance'
	db	00
L06C0:	db	'New Order'
	db	00
L06CA:	db	'An expression of zeal lights the dead face of the Liche.~~"Y'
	db	'es, '
	db	00
L070B:	db	'. The dead will rule! I will be their leader and thou canst '
	db	'become an Avatar... to ME!"'
	db	00
L0763:	db	'New Order'
	db	00
L076D:	db	'Fine!'
	db	00
L0773:	db	'Over my dead body!'
	db	00
L0786:	db	'Over my dead body!'
	db	00
L0799:	db	'"Why, '
	db	00
L07A0:	db	'. I thought that was understood. It will be my pleasure to h'
	db	'elp thee enter the realm of the dead."'
	db	00
L0803:	db	'Fine!'
	db	00
L0809:	db	'"Yes, I thought thou wouldst see the wisdom of my vision." H'
	db	'e looks at you like a cat toying with a mouse.'
	db	00
L0874:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0881:	db	'`Evil\' is a mild word for the sneer that appears on the Lic'
	db	'he\'s cracked lips. "It has recently come to my attention th'
	db	'at a certain ore found in the Britannian surface can, if fas'
	db	'hioned properly, become the bane of the vaunted Lord British'
	db	'.~~"I know this ore and have used it\tbefore for other purpo'
	db	'ses. I will use it once again to destroy that so-called Lord'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L09E9:	db	'other purposes'
	db	00
L09F8:	db	'ore'
	db	00
L09FC:	db	'Lord British'
	db	00
L0A09:	db	'other purposes'
	db	00
L0A18:	db	'He gestures at the walls of the tower. "How else didst thou '
	db	'expect my tower to withstand the ravaging effect the ether i'
	db	's having\ton my magic?"'
	db	00
L0AA7:	db	'He gestures at the walls of the tower. "It served as an effe'
	db	'ctive barrier against the ravaging effects of the disrupted '
	db	'ether."'
	db	00
L0B27:	db	'other purposes'
	db	00
L0B36:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0B3A:	db	'A harsh cackle escapes his dry throat. "I am the illustrious'
	db	' Lord of the Dead, soon to be Lord of all Britannia. Dost th'
	db	'ou have any idea of the number of dead people and creatures '
	db	'there are? I thought not.~~"The dead of the ages are mine to'
	db	' summon and control. The graves of beloved ancestors will sp'
	db	'ew forth their contents into an army. A special treat for th'
	db	'e living, mine undead monsters will be. Imagine a skeletal d'
	db	'ragon that cannot be killed. Consider a cabal of everliving '
	db	'mages eternally enthralled to me.~~"And the most beautiful p'
	db	'art of my plot is that, as the living die in these battles, '
	db	'and they will die, they will swell the ranks of the undead h'
	db	'ost. I will rule supreme -- a world of the dead!" A terrifyi'
	db	'ng glimpse of his sick and twisted future causes you to shiv'
	db	'er\tever so slightly.~~"And I will have a queen, the lovely '
	db	'Rowena."'
	db	00
L0E8A:	db	'Rowena'
	db	00
L0E91:	db	'"Yes, my Lord. I must be the happiest Lady in all the land."'
	db	' Her gaze never wanders from the horrid face of the Liche.'
	db	00
L0F08:	db	'Rowena'
	db	00
L0F0F:	db	'"Is she not the most beautiful lady thou hast seen? ~~"She s'
	db	'hall have eternal beauty at my side, and we shall rule toget'
	db	'her."'
	db	00
L0F8D:	db	'"She is the most beautiful lady I have been witness to. She '
	db	'shall have eternal beauty at my side, and we shall rule toge'
	db	'ther." After hearing him speak of his plans for the future, '
	db	'you find this a very unlikely statement.'
	db	00
L106A:	db	'Rowena'
	db	00
L1071:	db	'ore'
	db	00
L1075:	db	'"Now, now, Avatar, that would be revealing. Then I would hav'
	db	'e no secret from thee, would I?"'
	db	00
L10D2:	db	'ore'
	db	00
L10D6:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L10DA:	db	'"It is truly sad to see thee go." He says with a sardonic sm'
	db	'ile.*'
	db	00
L111C:	db	'"Yeah, right."*'
	db	00
L112C:	db	'"Yeah, right."*'
	db	00
L113C:	db	'"Feel free to explore mine humble abode. Though, have a care'
	db	'. My guardians are none too intelligent and will most likely'
	db	' assault anything living." He smiles with his death\'s head '
	db	'grin.*'
	db	00
