	; Function at file offset 000AE503H
	.funcnumber  048EH
	.data
	.msize       14BEH
	.dsize       1248H
L0000:	db	'Trent glares, giving his eyes an intensity that leaves no do'
	db	'ubt in your mind about his attitude. "If I thought that thou'
	db	' wert going to run off at a moment\'s notice I\'d not have a'
	db	'sked thee to help me free my love.~~"Now please, take the ca'
	db	'ge and go to\tMordra. She will instruct thee in its use." Hi'
	db	's manner smoothes, "I have placed mine only chance at reunio'
	db	'n with Rowena in thy capable hands."*'
	db	00
L018B:	db	'"Please, do not disturb me whilst I build this cage, for my '
	db	'thoughts are on nothing but the destruction of that foul Hor'
	db	'ance!" He continues the construction of the Soul Cage.*'
	db	00
L023B:	db	'The large, angry-looking ghost ignores your presence and con'
	db	'tinues to hammer on a strange iron cage.*'
	db	00
L02A1:	db	'The large, angry-looking ghost ignores your presence, while '
	db	'obviously searching for some item.*'
	db	00
L0301:	db	'ring'
	db	00
L0306:	db	'sacrifice'
	db	00
L0310:	db	'You see in the fire of the ghostly forge a large, heavily-mu'
	db	'scled ghost with a full beard and mustache. He does not noti'
	db	'ce your approach.'
	db	00
L039A:	db	'Trent continues his work on the strangely-shaped iron cage.'
	db	00
L03D6:	db	'iron cage'
	db	00
L03E0:	db	'Trent seems to be searching for something.'
	db	00
L040B:	db	'something'
	db	00
L0415:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0419:	db	'job'
	db	00
L041D:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0422:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0427:	db	'A deep furrow, accentuated by thick eyebrows, creases the gh'
	db	'ost\'s weary brow. He doesn\'t look away from his work. "I a'
	db	'm Trent. Now, please, leave me to my work."'
	db	00
L04C9:	db	'He continues hammering on a strangely-shaped iron cage.'
	db	00
L0501:	db	'iron cage'
	db	00
L050B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0510:	db	'something'
	db	00
L051A:	db	'"I cannot find the iron cage!" he shouts. "Some fool must ha'
	db	've taken it! When I find out who did it and where it is, tha'
	db	't fool will sorely regret having removed it from my shop!"*'
	db	00
L05CE:	db	'job'
	db	00
L05D2:	db	'"Art thou blind! Canst thou not see that I am a smith?" He d'
	db	'oesn\'t seem the sort for idle conversation.'
	db	00
L063A:	db	'job'
	db	00
L063E:	db	'iron cage'
	db	00
L0648:	db	'Anger radiates from the large ghost in almost tangible waves'
	db	'. He looks up from the cage and you see that the light of fi'
	db	're isn\'t coming from the forge, it\'s coming from his eyes.'
	db	' "I build this cage to destroy that bastard, Horance, who to'
	db	'ok my wife from me."~~For a moment, you think he is going to'
	db	' strike out at you, then he unclenches his fists with a heav'
	db	'y sigh and returns to his work.'
	db	00
L07CE:	db	'iron cage'
	db	00
L07D8:	db	'wife'
	db	00
L07DD:	db	'Horance'
	db	00
L07E5:	db	'Horance'
	db	00
L07ED:	db	'His whole body tenses as you speak.~~"Horance..." The word c'
	db	'omes out like a curse. "I will see his foul spirit burn befo'
	db	're mine eyes. Then I will laugh as he cries out pitifully fo'
	db	'r mercy." For some reason you think that you\'d rather avoid'
	db	' hearing that laugh.'
	db	00
L08F1:	db	'Horance'
	db	00
L08F9:	db	'wife'
	db	00
L08FE:	db	'One hot tear slips from the ghost\'s eye and falls on a heat'
	db	'ed piece of the iron cage. It sizzles, and then is gone.~~"R'
	db	'owena was my life, mine only joy in this world." His voice i'
	db	's almost tender, but then he returns to his guttural tones. '
	db	'"He killed her and took that joy from me. Now I am only a ho'
	db	'llow shell of a man, burning with hatred."'
	db	00
L0A54:	db	'wife'
	db	00
L0A59:	db	'killed'
	db	00
L0A60:	db	'Rowena'
	db	00
L0A67:	db	'killed'
	db	00
L0A6E:	db	'"In an attempt to steal her away from my side, the evil fien'
	db	'd sent his undead minions to bring her to the dark tower. Th'
	db	'e mindless creatures slew her as she struggled." The ghost t'
	db	'urns to you in anguish, "I could do nought to save her... th'
	db	'e sheer numbers of skeletal warriors bore me to the ground a'
	db	's she was bereft of life."~~Insane determination flickers in'
	db	' the big ghost\'s eyes, "For this I will never forgive and n'
	db	'ever forget.'
	db	00
L0C1E:	db	'killed'
	db	00
L0C25:	db	'Rowena'
	db	00
L0C2C:	db	'He holds up one hand as you say the name of his late wife. "'
	db	'Please, do not say that name. It takes from me\ta little of '
	db	'mine Hatred, which is all I have now. Wouldst thou rob me of'
	db	' the one thing that keeps me alive?" It would seem that he i'
	db	's unaware of the fact that he is, indeed, no longer alive. A'
	db	'n odd expression crosses his face.~~"I gave her a music box '
	db	'for our wedding, and now it is all I have left to remember h'
	db	'er by." His tone changes.~~"Do thou see what thou hast done?'
	db	'! I cannot work when I think of her!" He returns to his work'
	db	' with renewed passion.'
	db	00
L0E5E:	db	'You notice the music box he spoke of sitting nearby.'
	db	00
L0E93:	db	'Rowena'
	db	00
L0E9A:	db	'ring'
	db	00
L0E9F:	db	'You hold out the ring to Trent. At first he ignores you. The'
	db	'n, recognizing the ring, he takes it from you and holds it b'
	db	'efore him. Something in him snaps and his huge frame slumps '
	db	'forward.~~You let the ghost cry for a while, and when he fin'
	db	'ishes, you see a remarkable change in his appearance.'
	db	00
L0FC5:	db	'The flames that once burned in his eyes are now gone, replac'
	db	'ed by a deep shade of blue. He looks like a new man, or rath'
	db	'er, ghost as it were.~ "Forgive my behavior, '
	db	00
L106B:	db	'. I know not what came over me. I remember flames, but they '
	db	'burned no hotter than mine own Hatred." He looks pained at t'
	db	'he memory.~~ "Thou hast seen her? Thou hast seen Rowena? And'
	db	' she still cares for me. Well, all the more reason to finish'
	db	' this Soul Cage. We must free her from Horance\'s vile sorce'
	db	'ry."'
	db	00
L119B:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L119F:	db	'ring'
	db	00
L11A4:	db	'killed'
	db	00
L11AB:	db	'Rowena'
	db	00
L11B2:	db	'wife'
	db	00
L11B7:	db	'Horance'
	db	00
L11BF:	db	'job'
	db	00
L11C3:	db	'name'
	db	00
L11C8:	db	'iron cage'
	db	00
L11D2:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L11D6:	db	'If he heard you, he ignores the fact as you take your leave.'
	db	' You truly feel pity for this deeply wounded spirit.*'
	db	00
