	; Function at file offset 000B16C0H
	.funcnumber  0490H
	.data
	.msize       0781H
	.dsize       05EDH
L0000:	db	'The beautiful ghost looks through you with a slack look. Not'
	db	'hing\tyou do seems to attract her attention.*'
	db	00
L0069:	db	'sacrifice'
	db	00
L0073:	db	'You see a ghostly lady wearing a long, black gown. Something'
	db	' is a bit strange about the way she looks, but you can\'t qu'
	db	'ite place it. After a pause, she says, "Greetings, '
	db	00
L011E:	db	'. I am Rowena, lady of this wondrous tower." She gestures ar'
	db	'ound the room, indicating the moldering walls and cobwebbed '
	db	'rafters.'
	db	00
L019F:	db	'Rowena smiles in an abstract manner as you approach. "Ah, th'
	db	'ou hast returned, '
	db	00
L01EE:	db	'. How may the lady of the tower be of assistance to thee?"'
	db	00
L0229:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L022D:	db	'tower'
	db	00
L0233:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0237:	db	'name'
	db	00
L023C:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0241:	db	'"I am called... Rowena"'
	db	00
L0259:	db	'name'
	db	00
L025E:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0262:	db	'She stares blankly for a second, then, as if on cue, "I am t'
	db	'he Mistress of the Tower. I tend to my Lord Horance\'s needs'
	db	' and keep our place looking respectable." It would appear th'
	db	'at she\'s been falling behind in the latter duty.'
	db	00
L0346:	db	'Horance'
	db	00
L034E:	db	'tower'
	db	00
L0354:	db	'After a moment, "This is a lovely tower, dost thou not agree'
	db	'?" Before you can answer, she continues.~~ "Dost thou see th'
	db	'e lovely rays of light playing across the flagstones of the '
	db	'floor? Water sparkles in the fountain. This is truly a beaut'
	db	'iful place in which to live." Her eyes fix upon the floor.'
	db	00
L047F:	db	'tower'
	db	00
L0485:	db	'Horance'
	db	00
L048D:	db	'She blinks once, then, "Horance... What a wonderful name. He'
	db	' found me lost and lonely and brought me here to be a lady. '
	db	'Is he not truly the most magnificent of Lords?"'
	db	00
L0535:	db	'Horance'
	db	00
L053D:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0541:	db	'She pauses. "Goodbye, '
	db	00
L0558:	db	'. I hope thou hast enjoyed thy visit to our glorious tower. '
	db	'Please, return whenever thou wishest." You feel as if you\'v'
	db	'e been speaking to a statue.*'
	db	00
