L0204:	db	'She shakes her head sadly. "I have not been `myself\' for so'
	db	' long that I no longer recognize this town." Her eyes widen.'
	db	'~~ "There are so many buildings around the Lycaeum now, hast'
	db	' thou seen them?"~~She pauses, looking at you.~~"By the way,'
	db	' old friend. I assume thou art responsible for returning the'
	db	' ether to its normal state. I thank thee."'
	db	00
L035A:	db	'Lycaeum'
	db	00
L0362:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0366:	db	'"Fair days ahead, friend '
	db	00
L0380:	db	'."*'
	db	00
L0384:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0389:	db	'"Surely thou dost recognize thine old companion, Mariah?"*'
	db	00
L03C4:	db	'"Yes, dost thou not recognize me?" She pauses, glaring at yo'
	db	'u. "But who art thou, and where are my pastries?"'
	db	00
L0432:	db	'"Yes, thou mayest tell me thy name," she says, glancing arou'
	db	'nd the building. "Are not the many books beautiful?"'
	db	00
L04A3:	db	'name'
	db	00
L04A8:	db	'job'
	db	00
L04AC:	db	'She smiles. "I have a very important job, I do. My, are not '
	db	'those shelves lovely? So neat and orderly." She looks back a'
	db	't you.~~"Be careful! The ink wells are full, and the quills '
	db	'so sharp." She giggles.'
	db	00
L0578:	db	'quills'
	db	00
L057F:	db	'ink wells'
	db	00
L0589:	db	'shelves'
	db	00
L0591:	db	'shelves'
	db	00
L0599:	db	'"Are not they the neatest, most orderly, and well-kept shelv'
	db	'es thou hast seen? They do an excellent job of maintaining t'
	db	'hem!"'
	db	00
L0617:	db	'they'
	db	00
L061C:	db	'shelves'
	db	00
L0624:	db	'ink wells'
	db	00
L062E:	db	'"They are always so full and ready for use. They are so good'
	db	' about keeping them filled and clean!"'
	db	00
L0691:	db	'they'
	db	00
L0696:	db	'ink wells'
	db	00
L06A0:	db	'quills'
	db	00
L06A7:	db	'"Oh, yes, they are quite sharp! Always there when one needs '
	db	'to scribe a missive. They do an excellent job of having many'
	db	' ready at a moment\'s notice!"'
	db	00
L073D:	db	'they'
	db	00
L0742:	db	'quills'
	db	00
L0749:	db	'they'
	db	00
L074E:	db	'"Yes, they do!" Her face turns sad. "But I only sell."'
	db	00
L0785:	db	'sell'
	db	00
L078A:	db	'they'
	db	00
L078F:	db	'sell'
	db	00
L0794:	db	'"Yes," she agrees, "I do indeed sell. I even spell. In fact,'
	db	' I even sell spells! But, if thou desirest reagents, thou ar'
	db	't out of luck, for I only sell those during one of the seven'
	db	' weekdays. Wouldst thou like to know which day?~~"What a lov'
	db	'ely set of books thou must have! I have just the item for th'
	db	'ee to match thy shelves -- a potion. If thou wilt buy a spel'
	db	'l or reagent from me, I will sell thee a potion for only its'
	db	' normal price!"'
	db	00
