L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'"'
	db	00
L000F:	db	'? Thou, too, hast joined the evil organization? But how is t'
	db	'his possible? Canst thou not see their tenets vie with the v'
	db	'ery virtues themselves? Dost thou not feel more like a sheep'
	db	' than a man? I am truly sorry, for if one of Britannia\'s gr'
	db	'eatest heroes has fallen in with such filth, then there is n'
	db	'o hope for our great land!" He turns away in disgust.*'
	db	00
L0171:	db	'You see a man with an unhappy look upon his face.'
	db	00
L01A3:	db	'Cubolt looks up. "Yes, '
	db	00
L01BB:	db	'?"'
	db	00
L01BE:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01C3:	db	'"I am Cubolt of Moonglow."'
	db	00
L01DE:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L01E7:	db	'name'
	db	00
L01EC:	db	'job'
	db	00
L01F0:	db	'"I am a farmer, '
	db	00
L0201:	db	'. I manage my farm with the help of Tolemac, my brother, and'
	db	' Morz, our family friend."'
	db	00
L0258:	db	'Morz'
	db	00
L025D:	db	'Tolemac'
	db	00
L0265:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L026E:	db	'"The city occupies the entire island now, including the Lyca'
	db	'eum. Most of the residents still live south, though. We are '
	db	'due east of Britain proper."'
	db	00
L0303:	db	'residents'
	db	00
L030D:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L0316:	db	'Morz'
	db	00
L031B:	db	'"My brother and I have known Morz for most of our lives. He '
	db	'is very friendly when he is not too busy worrying about his '
	db	'stutter. Unfortunately, he listens to Tolemac too often."'
	db	00
L03CD:	db	'stutter'
	db	00
L03D5:	db	'Morz'
	db	00
L03DA:	db	'stutter'
	db	00
L03E2:	db	'Cubolt looks down at the ground, shaking his head sadly. "He'
	db	' started when he was five years old. He and my brother were '
	db	'wrestling in the back of a wagon driven by his parents. They'
	db	' hit a bump and he fell out -- and landed on his head. Ever '
	db	'since, he hath had his stutter." He looks back up at you. "T'
	db	'he odd thing is, neither he nor Tolemac remember the acciden'
	db	't. Or at least, Tolemac doth not. I cannot convince Morz to '
	db	'talk about it."'
	db	00
L0596:	db	'stutter'
	db	00
L059E:	db	'residents'
	db	00
L05A8:	db	'"Zelda, the clerk at the Lycaeum, would be the best person t'
	db	'o talk to about Moonglow\'s residents. Or the bartender, tho'
	db	'ugh I do not know his name. I know that the Observatory head'
	db	' and the Lycaeum head are twins, but I have never met either'
	db	' of them. I do know that thou dost not want to talk to Ranki'
	db	'n or Balayna at The Fellowship. They are ill news to our onc'
	db	'e-pleasant city."'
	db	00
L0721:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L072C:	db	'residents'
	db	00
L0736:	db	'Tolemac'
	db	00
L073E:	db	'"He is my younger brother. Need I say more? I am a little co'
	db	'ncerned about him though. I am used to his rebellious behavi'
	db	'or, but recently he has joined The Fellowship. That frighten'
	db	's me. They frighten me. I have tried to get him to come to h'
	db	'is senses, but he is too busy enjoying making me worry to li'
	db	'sten. Also, he is trying to get Morz to join. I wish I could'
	db	' get him to reconsider."'
	db	00
L08BF:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L08CA:	db	'reconsider'
	db	00
L08D5:	db	'Tolemac'
	db	00
L08DD:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L08E8:	db	'He spits on the ground. "A bane to Britannia is what The Fel'
	db	'lowship is. They have some odd philosophy that teaches thee '
	db	'to forget who thou art and follow them. The process is dehum'
	db	'anizing, and I think it meshes poorly with the eight virtues'
	db	'. Not only that, but their leader here in Moonglow has persu'
	db	'aded Tolemac to join."'
	db	00
L0A2B:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0A36:	db	'reconsider'
	db	00
L0A41:	db	'"Unfortunately, Tolemac will not listen to me. However," he '
	db	'begins to smile hopefully, "he just might listen to thee, '
	db	00
L0AB8:	db	'. Perhaps thou couldst talk him into reconverting. I would v'
	db	'ery much appreciate that! Perhaps," he adds, "thou couldst a'
	db	'lso ask Morz not to join."'
	db	00
L0B4B:	db	'reconsider'
	db	00
L0B56:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0B5A:	db	'"Take care, '
	db	00
L0B67:	db	'."*'
	db	00
