L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'"I think thou dost ask too many questions."'
	db	00
L0039:	db	'You see a fox standing on his hind legs, staring directly at'
	db	' you.'
	db	00
L007B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0080:	db	'"My name is Frank, devout follower of honesty." He makes a s'
	db	'light bow.'
	db	00
L00C7:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00CC:	db	'"And who wouldst thou be?"'
	db	00
L00E7:	db	'won\'t tell'
	db	00
L00F2:	db	'"It is good that thou didst tell me. One should always be ho'
	db	'nest in one\'s dealings with others. By the by, thy voice cr'
	db	'ackles too much."'
	db	00
L017B:	db	'won\'t tell'
	db	00
L0186:	db	'won\'t tell'
	db	00
L0191:	db	'"I am sorry to see that thou art not trusting enough to reve'
	db	'al thy name." He shrugs. "By the by, thy voice crackles too '
	db	'much."'
	db	00
L0210:	db	'won\'t tell'
	db	00
L021B:	db	'job'
	db	00
L021F:	db	'"I," he says, "am on a quest. A quest for honesty." He sniff'
	db	's the air, and then turns to you.~~ "By the by, thou mightes'
	db	't have more friends if thou didst bathe a little more often.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L02D5:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L02DD:	db	'bathed'
	db	00
L02E4:	db	'bathed'
	db	00
L02EB:	db	'"Yes, as in `take a bath.\' I must inform thee that thou dos'
	db	't truly stink!"'
	db	00
L0336:	db	'bathed'
	db	00
L033D:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L0345:	db	'"Speaking of thy friends, I have heard that thy companion, D'
	db	'upre, is a drunken sot."'
	db	00
L039A:	db	'"Hey, I don\'t think --"*'
	db	00
L03B3:	db	'"Yes, from what I have been told, that Dupre has no will whe'
	db	'n confronted by a tankard of, well, anything.~~"As a matter '
	db	'of fact, thou hast fairly poor taste in companions overall."'
	db	00
L0468:	db	'companions'
	db	00
L0473:	db	'friends'
	db	00
L047B:	db	'companions'
	db	00
L0486:	db	'"I am glad thou didst ask, '
	db	00
L04A2:	db	'. Thy friend, Iolo, charges far too much for his bows. Perha'
	db	'ps thou couldst have a chat with him."'
	db	00
L0505:	db	'"Too much? What dost thou mean, too --"*'
	db	00
L052E:	db	'"His bows and crossbows just aren\'t of the quality that is '
	db	'worth the kind of gold he charges."~~He takes a step back.~~'
	db	'"Gads! Thy breath could gag an ox. Thou shouldst consider ta'
	db	'king better care of thy teeth, or thy fellows will leave the'
	db	'e."'
	db	00
L0621:	db	'teeth'
	db	00
L0627:	db	'companions'
	db	00
L0632:	db	'teeth'
	db	00
L0638:	db	'"That is the reason for thine offensive mouth odor. I have n'
	db	'ot seen anything that yellow since the time thy fellow Shami'
	db	'no ran away from a battle in fear."'
	db	00
L06D4:	db	'"Thou must be mad!" Shamino turns to you. "This rogue needs '
	db	'to be taught a lesson."*'
	db	00
L0729:	db	'"And thy friend, Shamino, '
	db	00
L0744:	db	', has quite a bellicose temper."'
	db	00
L0765:	db	'bellicose'
	db	00
L076F:	db	'"And," he pauses, peering very closely at your face, "I neve'
	db	'r noticed how large thy nose is. \'Tis amazing thou canst fi'
	db	'nd enough air to breathe."'
	db	00
L0801:	db	'nose'
	db	00
L0806:	db	'teeth'
	db	00
L080C:	db	'bellicose'
	db	00
L0816:	db	'"Yes, bellicose, warlike, angry. If thou dost not know that,'
	db	' I believe thou needest to improve thy vocabulary. Thou art '
	db	'too unschooled."'
	db	00
L089F:	db	'bellicose'
	db	00
L08A9:	db	'unschooled'
	db	00
L08B4:	db	'unschooled'
	db	00
L08BF:	db	'"Trust me, '
	db	00
L08CB:	db	', thou art too ignorant to argue with me."'
	db	00
L08F6:	db	'"Oh, this is too much!"*'
	db	00
L090F:	db	'unschooled'
	db	00
L091A:	db	'nose'
	db	00
L091F:	db	'"Truly quite large, and not in the least bit attractive."'
	db	00
L0959:	db	'nose'
	db	00
L095E:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0962:	db	'"Thou hast the manners of a pig. \'Tis not polite to break c'
	db	'onversation so abruptly."*'
	db	00
