	; Function at file offset 000C720EH
	.funcnumber  04A7H
	.data
	.msize       1FCAH
	.dsize       1B31H
L0000:	db	'"Avatar! Didst thou know that the merchant Morfin had a quan'
	db	'tity of silver serpent venom stolen? This theft has caused t'
	db	'he community no small amount of distress."'
	db	00
L00A3:	db	'"Avatar! Oh Avatar! I have news!"'
	db	00
L00C5:	db	'"Garritt, my son, told me that Tobias was in possession of s'
	db	'ome silver snake venom. I went to investigate and found Tobi'
	db	'as with it!"*'
	db	00
L014B:	db	'"That is correct! I am a witness that what Feridwyn has said'
	db	' is the truth!"*'
	db	00
L0198:	db	'"I have often said that Tobias was no good. Now here is proo'
	db	'f. He is the thief that has been praying upon one of our hon'
	db	'est merchants! And to think I let him come into contact with'
	db	' my son! I hope he shall be dealt with in a manner appropria'
	db	'te to one who is leading youth astray from the way of The Fe'
	db	'llowship.'
	db	00
L02CE:	db	'"I suggest that thou go and speak with his mother at once! C'
	db	'amille should keep a tighter rein on her offspring!"*'
	db	00
L0340:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0344:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0348:	db	'name'
	db	00
L034D:	db	'Elizabeth and Abraham'
	db	00
L0363:	db	'case solved'
	db	00
L036F:	db	'found venom'
	db	00
L037B:	db	'case solved'
	db	00
L0387:	db	'Tobias'
	db	00
L038E:	db	'take action'
	db	00
L039A:	db	'Garritt caught'
	db	00
L03A9:	db	'found venom'
	db	00
L03B5:	db	'You see a small man with twisted, sloped posture. He looks y'
	db	'ou up and down before deciding he will speak to you.'
	db	00
L0426:	db	'"I had gotten word that thou wert coming to our town. I have'
	db	' been expecting thee. I must admit, though, that I find it d'
	db	'ifficult to believe that thou art truly the Avatar."'
	db	00
L04D3:	db	'"Thou dost wish to speak with me again, Avatar?" says Feridw'
	db	'yn.'
	db	00
L0513:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0518:	db	'"My name is Feridwyn."'
	db	00
L052F:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0534:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0538:	db	'"I run the Fellowship shelter with my wife Brita and my son '
	db	'Garritt here in Paws."'
	db	00
L058B:	db	'Paws'
	db	00
L0590:	db	'Garritt'
	db	00
L0598:	db	'Brita'
	db	00
L059E:	db	'shelter'
	db	00
L05A6:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L05B1:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L05BC:	db	'"Wouldst thou like to join?"'
	db	00
L05D9:	db	'"Then thou must see Batlin of Britain. He is the founder of '
	db	'The Fellowship."'
	db	00
L0626:	db	'"Thou dost not yet comprehend how much thy life could be imp'
	db	'roved through the guidance of The Fellowship."'
	db	00
L0691:	db	'"Gentle Avatar, it is good of thee to come to our humble tow'
	db	'n. Thou canst well see that The Fellowship has much work to '
	db	'do if it is to alleviate the suffering of the unfortunate of'
	db	' Britannia."'
	db	00
L0752:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L075D:	db	'shelter'
	db	00
L0765:	db	'"This is the only place in all of Britannia designed for the'
	db	' aid and care of the poor. It is hard work, but then one str'
	db	'ives to be worthy of that which we wish to receive."'
	db	00
L0812:	db	'shelter'
	db	00
L081A:	db	'Brita'
	db	00
L0820:	db	'"A wonderful woman. Thou shouldst meet her."'
	db	00
L084D:	db	'"Mine husband is such a flatterer. The truth is that our wor'
	db	'k for The Fellowship has brought us closer together."*'
	db	00
L08C0:	db	'"As thou dost already know my wife Brita, I am certain thou '
	db	'wilt agree that thou couldst not find a more dedicated pract'
	db	'itioner of The Fellowship\'s teachings."'
	db	00
L0960:	db	'Brita'
	db	00
L0966:	db	'Garritt'
	db	00
L096E:	db	'"Thankfully, we have been able to raise our son properly by '
	db	'emphasizing the teachings of The Fellowship. Garritt shall n'
	db	'ot be trapped in the poverty of his surroundings. He shall b'
	db	'e intellectually, spiritually, and morally superior. He\'s t'
	db	'alented, too!"'
	db	00
L0A6C:	db	'Garritt'
	db	00
L0A74:	db	'talented'
	db	00
L0A7D:	db	'talented'
	db	00
L0A86:	db	'"He plays the whistle panpipes extremely well for a lad his '
	db	'age! Brita and I are very proud. He could probably attend Th'
	db	'e Music Hall in Britain when he is older!"'
	db	00
L0B29:	db	'talented'
	db	00
L0B32:	db	'Paws'
	db	00
L0B37:	db	'"As this is a small town with few privileges and little priv'
	db	'acy, our family has come to know everyone in Paws quite well'
	db	'. Is there someone thou dost wish to hear about? I am well a'
	db	'cquainted with these people."'
	db	00
L0C09:	db	'Paws'
	db	00
L0C0E:	db	'beggars'
	db	00
L0C16:	db	'shelter residents'
	db	00
L0C28:	db	'farmers'
	db	00
L0C30:	db	'merchants'
	db	00
L0C3A:	db	'merchants'
	db	00
L0C44:	db	'"They would be Morfin, Andrew, Thurston, and Beverlea."'
	db	00
L0C7C:	db	'Beverlea'
	db	00
L0C85:	db	'Thurston'
	db	00
L0C8E:	db	'Andrew'
	db	00
L0C95:	db	'Morfin'
	db	00
L0C9C:	db	'merchants'
	db	00
L0CA6:	db	'Beverlea'
	db	00
L0CAF:	db	'"She is a nearly blind elderly woman who runs the antique sh'
	db	'oppe on the east side of the river."'
	db	00
L0D10:	db	'Beverlea'
	db	00
L0D19:	db	'farmers'
	db	00
L0D21:	db	'"That would be Camille and her son Tobias."'
	db	00
L0D4D:	db	'Tobias'
	db	00
L0D54:	db	'Camille'
	db	00
L0D5C:	db	'farmers'
	db	00
L0D64:	db	'beggars'
	db	00
L0D6C:	db	'"Oh. Them. Komor and Fenn." Feridwyn rolls his eyes.'
	db	00
L0DA1:	db	'Fenn'
	db	00
L0DA6:	db	'Komor'
	db	00
L0DAC:	db	'beggars'
	db	00
L0DB4:	db	'shelter residents'
	db	00
L0DC6:	db	'"Our residents include Alina and her child, and Merrick."'
	db	00
L0E00:	db	'Merrick'
	db	00
L0E08:	db	'Alina'
	db	00
L0E0E:	db	'shelter residents'
	db	00
L0E20:	db	'Alina'
	db	00
L0E26:	db	'"Her husband is currently in Britain somewhere. I do not kno'
	db	'w the details. She has a small child."'
	db	00
L0E89:	db	'Alina'
	db	00
L0E8F:	db	'Elizabeth and Abraham'
	db	00
L0EA5:	db	'"I am so sorry! Thou hast just missed them! Elizabeth and Ab'
	db	'raham were here delivering funds, but they have gone now to '
	db	'Jhelom. There is currently no Fellowship branch there, so th'
	db	'ey are taking the Triad of Inner Strength to lands west!"'
	db	00
L0F93:	db	'"I have not seen Elizabeth and Abraham for many days now."'
	db	00
L0FCE:	db	'Elizabeth and Abraham'
	db	00
L0FE4:	db	'Thurston'
	db	00
L0FED:	db	'"Thurston owns the mill. He could do better if he ran his bu'
	db	'siness with more of an eye toward profit."'
	db	00
L1054:	db	'Thurston'
	db	00
L105D:	db	'Camille'
	db	00
L1065:	db	'"She\'s a sad woman -- a widow -- who is living in the past.'
	db	' \'Tis a pity, really. Fortunately her husband left her the '
	db	'farm which does happen to turn a profit."'
	db	00
L1105:	db	'Camille'
	db	00
L110D:	db	'Merrick'
	db	00
L1115:	db	'"A splendid example of The Fellowship turning someone\'s lif'
	db	'e around. Presently he resides in our shelter."'
	db	00
L1180:	db	'Merrick'
	db	00
L1188:	db	'Morfin'
	db	00
L118F:	db	'"Morfin is a clever and industrious member of The Fellowship'
	db	'. He runs the local slaughterhouse and is also a snake venom'
	db	' merchant."'
	db	00
L1213:	db	'snake venom'
	db	00
L121F:	db	'Morfin'
	db	00
L1226:	db	'Andrew'
	db	00
L122D:	db	'"Andrew is such a happy young man. He doth not notice the my'
	db	'riad of personal problems that he is afflicted with."'
	db	00
L129F:	db	'Andrew'
	db	00
L12A6:	db	'Tobias'
	db	00
L12AD:	db	'"A local rascal. I normally would not allow Garritt to assoc'
	db	'iate with such a troublemaker, but The Fellowship has taught'
	db	' me to be a tolerant parent. Besides, associating with my so'
	db	'n might do the lad some good. Who knows?"'
	db	00
L138B:	db	'"No matter that Tobias did not personally steal the venom hi'
	db	'mself. He caused the theft by means of his corrupting influe'
	db	'nce on my son. While his actions are just short of criminal,'
	db	' I still blame Tobias."'
	db	00
L1457:	db	'Tobias'
	db	00
L145E:	db	'Fenn'
	db	00
L1463:	db	'"Fenn is a beggar who refuses all aid from The Fellowship. A'
	db	' pathetic case. Not even his former friend Merrick can reach'
	db	' him any more."'
	db	00
L14EB:	db	'Fenn'
	db	00
L14F0:	db	'Komor'
	db	00
L14F6:	db	'"Komor is the most hateful man I have ever met. He is a bund'
	db	'le of bitterness. In all the time I have known him, Komor ha'
	db	's never spoken a word to me that was not at best a thinly ve'
	db	'iled insult."'
	db	00
L15B8:	db	'Komor'
	db	00
L15BE:	db	'case solved'
	db	00
L15CA:	db	'"Thankfully we can now put this business of snake venom thef'
	db	'ts behind us, thanks to thy thorough efforts. I shall deal w'
	db	'ith my son. Let us speak of this no more."'
	db	00
L166D:	db	'"Thank goodness Garritt, my sharp eyed boy, got to the botto'
	db	'm of this business of the snake venom thefts. Frankly, I had'
	db	' my suspicions about Tobias myself."'
	db	00
L170A:	db	'case solved'
	db	00
L1716:	db	'snake venom'
	db	00
L1722:	db	'"Morfin, the local merchant, informs me that a quantity of s'
	db	'ilver serpent venom was stolen from him. The thief is still '
	db	'at large, so be wary! Of course, I do not know why anyone wo'
	db	'uld want the vile substance. It is surely not good for one'
	db	'\'s health."'
	db	00
L181C:	db	'snake venom'
	db	00
L1828:	db	'take action'
	db	00
L1834:	db	'"I promise thee, I shall apply the necessary discipline to m'
	db	'y son to insure that this bad habit he has picked up from th'
	db	'e local riffraff will not trouble this community again."'
	db	00
L18E5:	db	'take action'
	db	00
L18F1:	db	'found venom'
	db	00
L18FD:	db	'"Thou didst find the venom vial in Garritt\'s belongings? I '
	db	'am amazed! I am astonished! I am-- sorry."'
	db	00
L1963:	db	'"Thou art a resourceful person. Unfortunately, thy discovery'
	db	' has upset me a great deal."'
	db	00
L19BC:	db	'found venom'
	db	00
L19C8:	db	'Garritt caught'
	db	00
L19D7:	db	'"Thou dost say my son has admitted to stealing the venom?! I'
	db	' do not know what to say. My thanks, Avatar, for uncovering '
	db	'the truth."'
	db	00
L1A5B:	db	'Garritt caught'
	db	00
L1A6A:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1A6E:	db	'"Mayest thou walk with the Fellowship."*'
	db	00
L1A97:	db	'You realize that the Cube did not bring out anything that Fe'
	db	'ridwyn did not actually believe himself. He is one of the in'
	db	'nocent followers of The Guardian.'
	db	00
