L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'Ethereal Ring'
	db	00
L001B:	db	'You see a nobleman, all alone, with a demented gleam in his '
	db	'eye.~~"Who in blazes art thou?" the man asks. His attitude i'
	db	's that of someone who was just interrupted from something te'
	db	'rribly important.'
	db	00
L00E1:	db	'I am the Avatar'
	db	00
L00F1:	db	'Martingo shakes your hand but acts thoroughly disinterested.'
	db	' "I\'m thrilled."'
	db	00
L013E:	db	'He turns to his right and speaks to no one.'
	db	00
L016A:	db	'"What? Oh, really! I do not think '
	db	00
L018D:	db	' looks particularly brainless. We shall have to see, shall w'
	db	'e not?"'
	db	00
L01D1:	db	'He turns back to you and grins.'
	db	00
L01F1:	db	'"Of course thou art! And I am the evil spirit of Mondain, co'
	db	'me back to wreak havoc over all Britannia. Funny, thou dost '
	db	'not look like an Avatar -- thou dost look like a fool.'
	db	00
L02A0:	db	'"What can I do for thee, Miss Fool?"'
	db	00
L02C5:	db	'"What can I do for thee, Mr. Fool?"'
	db	00
L02E9:	db	'He turns to his right and speaks to no one.'
	db	00
L0315:	db	'"What? Oh, really! Thou dost think this Avatar looks like th'
	db	'e real thing? I doubt it, Lucinda. I doubt it very much."'
	db	00
L038B:	db	'He turns back to you and grins.'
	db	00
L03AB:	db	'"What\'chu want?" Martingo asks, belligerently.'
	db	00
L03DA:	db	'name'
	db	00
L03DF:	db	'The nobleman looks at you with impatience. "I am Martingo, t'
	db	'he Sultan of Spektran. Is that all right with thee?" He roll'
	db	's his eyes. He turns to his right side and whispers again to'
	db	' an imaginary person, "I believe we have an ignoramus on our'
	db	' hands."'
	db	00
L04D8:	db	'name'
	db	00
L04DD:	db	'job'
	db	00
L04E1:	db	'"I am the Sultan of Spektran! What, is thy brain the size of'
	db	' a pea? Do not answer, \'twas a rhetorical question."'
	db	00
L0552:	db	'He turns to his left side and whispers to no one, "Dost thou'
	db	' not think her brain is the size of a pea? I do!" He giggles'
	db	' conspiratorially with his invisible friend.'
	db	00
L05F7:	db	'He turns to his left side and whispers again to an imaginary'
	db	' person, "Dost thou not think his brain is the\tsize of a pe'
	db	'a? I do!" He giggles conspiratorially with his invisible fri'
	db	'end.'
	db	00
L06AF:	db	'Martingo then pulls out a banana and begins to peel it.'
	db	00
L06E7:	db	'banana'
	db	00
L06EE:	db	'Spektran'
	db	00
L06F7:	db	'Sultan'
	db	00
L06FE:	db	'Sultan'
	db	00
L0705:	db	'"Come on, do not insult mine intelligence. Surely thou dost '
	db	'know what a Sultan is! Canst not thou see mine harem?"'
	db	00
L0778:	db	'"Lovely, are they not?'
	db	00
L078F:	db	'Martingo looks bewildered. "Then thou must have thine eyes e'
	db	'xamined! I am surrounded by ten..." He looks around quickly.'
	db	' "No, -eleven- beautiful women!'
	db	00
L0827:	db	'"Each day I enjoy a different one. Thou canst not imagine ho'
	db	'w much fun being a Sultan really is!" He leans over and kiss'
	db	'es an invisible cheek. "Today, I am enjoying Lucinda." He gr'
	db	'ins broadly.'
	db	00
L08E8:	db	'Lucinda'
	db	00
L08F0:	db	'Martingo looks you up and down lecherously. "Hmmm. Wouldst t'
	db	'hou like to join mine harem?"'
	db	00
L094A:	db	'Your answer takes Martingo by surprise. "Thou wouldst?" He l'
	db	'ooks around nervously. "Oh, uhm, I had better consult mine a'
	db	'strologer about this matter. I shall get back to thee, all r'
	db	'ight?"'
	db	00
L0A05:	db	'"Pity."'
	db	00
L0A0D:	db	'Sultan'
	db	00
L0A14:	db	'Spektran'
	db	00
L0A1D:	db	'"\'Tis the island thou dost stand upon!" He turns to the inv'
	db	'isible person on his left and whispers, "Thou art correct --'
	db	' this person really is a fool!" ~~Martingo turns back to you'
	db	'. "As I said, I am the Sultan here. I am the master of all o'
	db	'f these subjects." He gestures\taround the room.'
	db	00
L0B3C:	db	'Iolo whispers to you. "This fellow is quite daft. Be careful'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L0B7B:	db	'Spektran'
	db	00
L0B84:	db	'Lucinda'
	db	00
L0B8C:	db	'"She is beautiful, is she not?" Martingo leans over and stic'
	db	'ks his tongue in an ear that isn\'t there.'
	db	00
L0BF2:	db	'Lucinda'
	db	00
L0BFA:	db	'banana'
	db	00
L0C01:	db	'"Oh, forgive my manners! Wouldst thou like a banana?"'
	db	00
L0C37:	db	'"Well, it shall cost thee 3 gold coins. Still want one?"'
	db	00
L0C70:	db	'"Here thou art." Martingo hands you a banana and takes your '
	db	'gold. He turns to \'Lucinda\' and whispers, "That rotter too'
	db	'k my last banana!"'
	db	00
L0CF9:	db	'"Thou dost have wheat for brains! Thou hast not room for a s'
	db	'ingle banana!"'
	db	00
L0D44:	db	'"Broke, art thou? Too bad." Martingo sniffs. "Well, I am ver'
	db	'y rich, I must say."'
	db	00
L0D95:	db	'"That\'s a relief. I only had one left."'
	db	00
L0DBD:	db	'"That\'s a relief. I only had one left."'
	db	00
L0DE5:	db	'"I already sold thee my last banana!"'
	db	00
L0E0B:	db	'banana'
	db	00
L0E12:	db	'Ethereal Ring'
	db	00
L0E20:	db	'Martingo looks suspicious. "Art thou wanting to steal mine E'
	db	'thereal Ring?" He turns to his imaginary friend and whispers'
	db	', "Thou wert right. Our guest looks like a thief." He turns '
	db	'back to you and smiles. "Yes, I do have an Ethereal Ring. I '
	db	'purchased it from the King of the Gargoyles. What was his na'
	db	'me?" He leans toward the invisible companion on his right. "'
	db	'What? Oh yes, Draxinusom. I knew it all the time." He turns '
	db	'back to you. "It is in my vault."'
	db	00
L0FE6:	db	'Ethereal Ring'
	db	00
L0FF4:	db	'vault'
	db	00
L0FFA:	db	'vault'
	db	00
L1000:	db	'Martingo\'s eyes light up. "My vault is the most protected v'
	db	'ault in all Britannia. No one, and I repeat, -no one- can st'
	db	'eal anything from my vault. I have many fine treasures there'
	db	'." He turns to \'Lucinda\' and bites an nonexistent ear lobe'
	db	'.'
	db	00
L10EF:	db	'vault'
	db	00
L10F5:	db	'protected'
	db	00
L10FF:	db	'treasures'
	db	00
L1109:	db	'treasures'
	db	00
L1113:	db	'"I collect magical items. The vault is full of them. Includi'
	db	'ng this ring thou dost mention."'
	db	00
L1170:	db	'treasures'
	db	00
L117A:	db	'protected'
	db	00
L1184:	db	'"The vault\'s security is my secret. Feel free to try and en'
	db	'ter it. In fact, I dare thee! If thou canst succeed in getti'
	db	'ng inside, thou art welcome to take anything!" Martingo laug'
	db	'hs. "All thou dost need is the key!" He laughs with his imag'
	db	'inary harem, as if they were all laughing with him. "I\'m su'
	db	're thou wilt find it!" He breaks up, laughing so hard that t'
	db	'ears begin to fall down his cheeks.'
	db	00
L130E:	db	'protected'
	db	00
L1318:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L131C:	db	'"Fine. Go away. It shall do thee good!"*'
	db	00
