L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'The large, muscle-bound man smiles pleasantly at you.'
	db	00
L0043:	db	'"Greetings, '
	db	00
L0050:	db	'," says Menion.'
	db	00
L0060:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0065:	db	'"I am Menion, '
	db	00
L0074:	db	'." He shakes your hand.'
	db	00
L008C:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0091:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0095:	db	'"I am a trainer. I help warriors become bigger and stronger '
	db	'and better fighters. I also forge swords to match the streng'
	db	'th in my students\' arms."'
	db	00
L0127:	db	'students'
	db	00
L0130:	db	'forge'
	db	00
L0136:	db	'train'
	db	00
L013C:	db	'students'
	db	00
L0145:	db	'"I have taught many a warrior how to use his -- or her -- fo'
	db	'rce against an opponent."'
	db	00
L019B:	db	'students'
	db	00
L01A4:	db	'force'
	db	00
L01AA:	db	'force'
	db	00
L01B0:	db	'"Yes, '
	db	00
L01B7:	db	'. The key to effective fighting is striking hard and accurat'
	db	'ely at one\'s foe."'
	db	00
L0206:	db	'force'
	db	00
L020C:	db	'accurately'
	db	00
L0217:	db	'hard'
	db	00
L021C:	db	'hard'
	db	00
L0221:	db	'"Physical strength permits the attacker a better chance of p'
	db	'enetrating the other fighter\'s armour. Obviously, in a leth'
	db	'al combat, that is an important objective."'
	db	00
L02C4:	db	'hard'
	db	00
L02C9:	db	'accurately'
	db	00
L02D4:	db	'"Needless to say, some targets on an individual are better t'
	db	'han others. \'Tis always best to hit something that will eit'
	db	'her seriously incapacitate one\'s foe, or create enough pain'
	db	' to distract him."'
	db	00
L0399:	db	'accurately'
	db	00
L03A4:	db	'train'
	db	00
L03AA:	db	'"I will train thee for 45 gold. Wilt thou pay?"'
	db	00
L03DA:	db	'"Fine."'
	db	00
L03E2:	db	'"Perhaps this would be a more appropriate topic when I am at'
	db	' work."'
	db	00
L0426:	db	'forge'
	db	00
L042C:	db	'"Dost thou wish to make a sword?"'
	db	00
L044E:	db	'"Perhaps sometime when thou hast more time."'
	db	00
L047B:	db	'He smiles. "I would be very happy to show thee the steps nec'
	db	'essary to create a very fine blade." He quickly jots down a '
	db	'few things on a scroll and turns to give it to you.*'
	db	00
L0528:	db	'"May thy blade be sturdy and sharp!"*'
	db	00
L054E:	db	'"Perhaps when thou hast fewer things to occupy thy pack, I c'
	db	'an give this to thee."'
	db	00
L05A1:	db	'"I can help thee with that when I am at work."'
	db	00
L05D0:	db	'forge'
	db	00
L05D6:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L05DA:	db	'"May the strength in thine arms always match the strength of'
	db	' thy will."*'
	db	00
