L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You are greeted with a stern look on this man\'s face.'
	db	00
L0043:	db	'"^'
	db	00
L0046:	db	'." He nods at you.'
	db	00
L0059:	db	'statue'
	db	00
L0060:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0065:	db	'"Thou mayest call me Sir Pendaran."'
	db	00
L0089:	db	'name'
	db	00
L008E:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0092:	db	'"I am a knight here in Serpent\'s Hold. \'Tis my job to help'
	db	' protect the citizens of Britannia."'
	db	00
L00F1:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0100:	db	'protect'
	db	00
L0108:	db	'protect'
	db	00
L0110:	db	'"Aye, '
	db	00
L0117:	db	'. Britannia can be a dangerous place outside town boundaries'
	db	'. Especially now that the ruling faction have gone soft!"'
	db	00
L018D:	db	'protect'
	db	00
L0195:	db	'soft'
	db	00
L019A:	db	'ruling faction'
	db	00
L01A9:	db	'ruling faction'
	db	00
L01B8:	db	'"Well, I mean Lord British and his advisors."'
	db	00
L01E6:	db	'ruling faction'
	db	00
L01F5:	db	'worthless'
	db	00
L01FF:	db	'soft'
	db	00
L0204:	db	'"Though I\'d follow the land\'s ideals to the ends of the la'
	db	'nd, I find it difficult to accept how poor the conditions ar'
	db	'e in Britannia. Brigands populate the land, disease overruns'
	db	' the towns, and corruption fills the councils. Were it not f'
	db	'or The Fellowship, I would be hard pressed to avoid falling '
	db	'on mine own blade, despite how dishonorable an act that may '
	db	'seem."'
	db	00
L0371:	db	'worthless'
	db	00
L037B:	db	'soft'
	db	00
L0380:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L038B:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0396:	db	'"A noble group of people who strive to instill a greater sen'
	db	'se of spiritual knowledge throughout all of Britannia. \'Twi'
	db	'll be but a matter of time, '
	db	00
L042A:	db	', before all people will see the wisdom."'
	db	00
L0454:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L045F:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L046E:	db	'"I live here in the hold with my lady."'
	db	00
L0496:	db	'lady'
	db	00
L049B:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L04AA:	db	'lady'
	db	00
L04AF:	db	'"Her name is Jehanne, '
	db	00
L04C6:	db	'," he says suspiciously. "She is the provisioner."'
	db	00
L04F9:	db	'lady'
	db	00
L04FE:	db	'statue'
	db	00
L0505:	db	'"Terrible shame, '
	db	00
L0517:	db	'." He eyes you coldly.'
	db	00
L052E:	db	'Thou didst do it!'
	db	00
L0540:	db	'statue'
	db	00
L0547:	db	'Thou didst do it!'
	db	00
L0559:	db	'"What! Thou art accusing me! Preposterous. I had nothing to '
	db	'do with it!"'
	db	00
L05A2:	db	'Thou didst do it!'
	db	00
L05B4:	db	'Lady Jehanne'
	db	00
L05C1:	db	'Lady Jehanne'
	db	00
L05CE:	db	'He shakes his head.~~"Thou wouldst take the word of a woman '
	db	'over that of a knight of the Hold? Thou art lower than a wor'
	db	'm!" He glares at you for a moment, and then his expression c'
	db	'hanges.~~"All right," he says, "I am the one\twho defaced th'
	db	'e statue, but only because the government has become so wort'
	db	'hless and soft!" He quickly turns away from\tyou, ashamed.~~'
	db	'"If thou dost think it best," he sighs, "tomorrow I shall be'
	db	'g forgiveness from my fellow knights."'
	db	00
L0797:	db	'no need'
	db	00
L079F:	db	'\'tis best'
	db	00
L07A9:	db	'\'tis best'
	db	00
L07B3:	db	'Nodding his agreement, he sighs again, and turns away.*'
	db	00
L07EB:	db	'no need'
	db	00
L07F3:	db	'"No, no, '
	db	00
L07FD:	db	'. Thou hast shown me the way. I must repent." He turns away '
	db	'from you to reflect on his decision.*'
	db	00
L085F:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0863:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
	db	00
L0877:	db	'."*'
	db	00
