L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'The very serious man breaks into a half-smile as he greets y'
	db	'ou.'
	db	00
L004D:	db	'Horffe is standing at attention just behind him.'
	db	00
L007E:	db	'Standing at attention just behind him is a wingled gargoyle.'
	db	00
L00BB:	db	'"Good day to thee," says Lord John-Paul.'
	db	00
L00E4:	db	'Sir Horffe responsible'
	db	00
L00FB:	db	'Sir Pendaran responsible'
	db	00
L0114:	db	'Sir Horffe responsible'
	db	00
L012B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0130:	db	'"I am Lord John-Paul of Serpent\'s Hold. Thou art '
	db	00
L0162:	db	', the Avatar, correct?"'
	db	00
L017A:	db	'"I remember thee."'
	db	00
L018D:	db	'"Excellent."'
	db	00
L019A:	db	'"I have something that might interest thee."'
	db	00
L01C7:	db	'I am interested'
	db	00
L01D7:	db	'He looks surprised. "Forgive me, '
	db	00
L01F9:	db	', I could have sworn... Ah, well, no matter."'
	db	00
L0227:	db	'name'
	db	00
L022C:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L023B:	db	'job'
	db	00
L023F:	db	'"I am charged with overseeing the Hold."'
	db	00
L0268:	db	'overseeing'
	db	00
L0273:	db	'overseeing'
	db	00
L027E:	db	'"It is not a difficult job. Sir Richter and Sir Horffe insur'
	db	'e that things run smoothly as often as possible."'
	db	00
L02EC:	db	'overseeing'
	db	00
L02F7:	db	'Sir Horffe'
	db	00
L0302:	db	'Sir Richter'
	db	00
L030E:	db	'Sir Richter'
	db	00
L031A:	db	'"He is in charge of the Hold when I am otherwise occupied. H'
	db	'e has seemed somewhat changed of late, but I trust him nonet'
	db	'heless."'
	db	00
L039B:	db	'Sir Richter'
	db	00
L03A7:	db	'changed'
	db	00
L03AF:	db	'changed'
	db	00
L03B7:	db	'"It began when he joined The Fellowship. He became more... w'
	db	'hat is the word... orderly."~~He smiles. "I suppose there is'
	db	' a regimented structure within The Fellowship that has done '
	db	'him good, no?"'
	db	00
L047A:	db	'changed'
	db	00
L0482:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L048D:	db	'orderly'
	db	00
L0495:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L04A0:	db	'"I\'m afraid I know so little about them. They seem to help '
	db	'many people. However, I have noticed Sir Horffe has become r'
	db	'ather apprehensive since Richter joined."'
	db	00
L0541:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L054C:	db	'orderly'
	db	00
L0554:	db	'"It is difficult to explain. He seems more disciplined," he '
	db	'gives a short laugh, "which, of course, is rather fitting fo'
	db	'r the Hold."'
	db	00
L05D9:	db	'orderly'
	db	00
L05E1:	db	'Sir Horffe'
	db	00
L05EC:	db	'"He is the captain of the guards. I would have no other for '
	db	'his position. He is the most honorable warrior I have ever m'
	db	'et."'
	db	00
L0669:	db	'"To thank you, Sir!"'
	db	00
L067E:	db	'"He seems to have taken a dislike for The Fellowship, howeve'
	db	'r. I have noticed he is reluctant to mention this around Sir'
	db	' Richter." He shrugs.'
	db	00
L070C:	db	'Sir Horffe'
	db	00
L0717:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0726:	db	'"It has changed little since thy last visit, '
	db	00
L0754:	db	'. Of course, all of the people are new."'
	db	00
L077D:	db	'people'
	db	00
L0784:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0793:	db	'people'
	db	00
L079A:	db	'"I am afraid I must attend to other business shortly, and ca'
	db	'nnot show thee around. But I recommend that thou visitest th'
	db	'e Hallowed Dock. Many of the Hold\'s knights frequent there '
	db	'in the evening."'
	db	00
L085E:	db	'people'
	db	00
L0865:	db	'I am interested'
	db	00
L0875:	db	'He smiles gratefully at you and begins pacing.~~ "Very recen'
	db	'tly, a terrible crime was committed. It seems the statue of '
	db	'Lord British, the one in the Hold commons, was defaced by an'
	db	' unknown vandal.~~ "Perhaps," he looks at you hopefully, "th'
	db	'ou couldst help track down the villain?"'
	db	00
L098E:	db	'"Very good. The best way to begin is by speaking with Sir De'
	db	'nton, the tavernkeeper at the Hallowed Dock. His ability to '
	db	'solve puzzles and problems is remarkable. When thou hast sol'
	db	'ved this little mystery, please inform me of thy findings."'
	db	00
L0A7E:	db	'"Of course. I understand. Thou dost have much more important'
	db	' matters to resolve. I will call for an official from Yew to'
	db	' handle this issue."'
	db	00
L0B0B:	db	'"Oh, yes, I forgot. I am terribly sorry to have disturbed th'
	db	'ee twice with this matter. Please excuse my forgetfulness, '
	db	00
L0B83:	db	'. The matter is being handled."'
	db	00
L0BA3:	db	'handled?'
	db	00
L0BAC:	db	'I am interested'
	db	00
L0BBC:	db	'handled?'
	db	00
L0BC5:	db	'"I have sent for a judge from the High Court in Yew. I reali'
	db	'ze thou dost not have the time for such petty matters."'
	db	00
L0C39:	db	'I have the time'
	db	00
L0C49:	db	'handled?'
	db	00
L0C52:	db	'I have the time'
	db	00
L0C62:	db	'"Yes, yes, thou art very kind, but I am sure there are much '
	db	'more important matters thou must attend to. I thank thee non'
	db	'e the less."'
	db	00
L0CE7:	db	'I have the time'
	db	00
L0CF7:	db	'-I- -want- -to- -do- -it-!'
	db	00
L0D12:	db	'-I- -want- -to- -do- -it-!'
	db	00
L0D2D:	db	'"Oh, I see. Well, in that case. The best way to begin is by '
	db	'speaking with Sir Denton, the tavernkeeper at the Hallowed D'
	db	'ock. His ability to solve puzzles and problems is remarkable'
	db	'. Please come to me with thy findings after thou hast solved'
