L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'help'
	db	00
L0012:	db	'got fragments'
	db	00
L0020:	db	'help'
	db	00
L0025:	db	'"Greetings to thee, Sir Dupre. Art thou back again for thy s'
	db	'tudy of wines for Brommer?"'
	db	00
L007D:	db	'"Why, ah, yes, my good friend, Denton. I am, uh, still condu'
	db	'cting that study." He turns to you and shrugs, grinning shee'
	db	'pishly.'
	db	00
L00FD:	db	'The man before you seems to stare at you blankly.'
	db	00
L012F:	db	'"Hello, '
	db	00
L0138:	db	'," says Denton.'
	db	00
L0148:	db	'name'
	db	00
L014D:	db	'"I am Sir Denton, '
	db	00
L0160:	db	'."'
	db	00
L0163:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0168:	db	'help'
	db	00
L016D:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0171:	db	'"I am the tavernkeeper, '
	db	00
L018A:	db	'. I sell refreshment to the citizens of Britannia, most nota'
	db	'bly, the knights in Serpent\'s Hold."'
	db	00
L01EB:	db	'knights'
	db	00
L01F3:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0202:	db	'sell'
	db	00
L0207:	db	'knights'
	db	00
L020F:	db	'"Almost every resident here is a noble warrior. The exceptio'
	db	'ns would be Lady Jehanne, the provisioner; Lady Tory; Lady L'
	db	'eigh, the healer; and Menion, the trainer. I can also tell t'
	db	'hee about all the other residents."'
	db	00
L02E7:	db	'residents'
	db	00
L02F1:	db	'Menion'
	db	00
L02F8:	db	'Lady Leigh'
	db	00
L0303:	db	'Lady Tory'
	db	00
L030D:	db	'Lady Jehanne'
	db	00
L031A:	db	'knights'
	db	00
L0322:	db	'sell'
	db	00
L0327:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0336:	db	'"Serpent\'s Hold is located at precisely 53 degrees east and'
	db	' 165 degrees south."'
	db	00
L0386:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0395:	db	'residents'
	db	00
L039F:	db	'"Yes, '
	db	00
L03A6:	db	', I can tell thee about the following people: '
	db	00
L03D5:	db	'Sir Pendaran'
	db	00
L03E2:	db	'Sir Jordan'
	db	00
L03ED:	db	'Sir Horffe'
	db	00
L03F8:	db	'Sir Richter'
	db	00
L0404:	db	'Lord John-Paul'
	db	00
L0413:	db	'no one'
	db	00
L041A:	db	'no one'
	db	00
L0421:	db	'residents'
	db	00
L042B:	db	'Lord John-Paul'
	db	00
L043A:	db	'"He is the Lord of Serpent\'s Hold. He is a capable leader a'
	db	'nd a fair man."'
	db	00
L0485:	db	'Lord John-Paul'
	db	00
L0494:	db	'Lady Leigh'
	db	00
L049F:	db	'"Her healing skills are said to be unparalleled."'
	db	00
L04D1:	db	'Lady Leigh'
	db	00
L04DC:	db	'Sir Richter'
	db	00
L04E8:	db	'"He is second in command to Lord John-Paul. He is teaching m'
	db	'e how to gamble well. In fact, he began increasing the lesso'
	db	'ns after joining The Fellowship."'
	db	00
L0582:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L058D:	db	'Sir Richter'
	db	00
L0599:	db	'Sir Horffe'
	db	00
L05A4:	db	'"Sir Horffe is an excellent warrior. He is a gargoyle that w'
	db	'as found by two knights when he was very young. They chose t'
	db	'o raise him as their own child. He is very honorable."'
	db	00
L0653:	db	'Sir Horffe'
	db	00
L065E:	db	'Gargish accent'
	db	00
L066D:	db	'Gargish accent'
	db	00
L067C:	db	'"Sir Horffe has chosen to use the Gargish syntax of our lang'
	db	'uage so he may better maintain his cultural ties."'
	db	00
L06EB:	db	'Gargish accent'
	db	00
L06FA:	db	'Sir Jordan'
	db	00
L0705:	db	'"Despite his blindness, Sir Jordan perceives objects around '
	db	'him very well. He is an excellent tinkerer, and can repair m'
	db	'any items."'
	db	00
L0789:	db	'Sir Jordan'
	db	00
L0794:	db	'Lady Tory'
	db	00
L079E:	db	'"I believe she is a druid. She was showing me how to be more'
	db	' compassionate than I was before. She is very good at knowin'
	db	'g what others are feeling and why they are experiencing such'
	db	' emotions."'
	db	00
L085E:	db	'Lady Tory'
	db	00
L0868:	db	'Menion'
	db	00
L086F:	db	'"He is the fighting instructor. In his spare time, he likes '
	db	'to make swords. Menion has been kind enough to give me one o'
	db	'f his creations."'
	db	00
L08F9:	db	'Menion'
	db	00
L0900:	db	'Sir Pendaran'
	db	00
L090D:	db	'"Sir Pendaran is a knight of the Hold. He is very friendly, '
	db	'but I have been told he can be overbearing at times."'
	db	00
L097F:	db	'Sir Pendaran'
	db	00
L098C:	db	'Lady Jehanne'
	db	00
L0999:	db	'"She is the lady of Sir Pendaran. She has been helping me be'
	db	'tter my sense of humor."'
	db	00
L09EE:	db	'humor'
	db	00
L09F4:	db	'Lady Jehanne'
	db	00
L0A01:	db	'humor'
	db	00
L0A07:	db	'"My jokes are very bad. If thou wouldst like, I will tell th'
	db	'ee one."'
	db	00
L0A4C:	db	'"Why did the chicken cross the road?"'
	db	00
L0A72:	db	'"To get to the other side! Oh, that joke is new," he says sa'
	db	'rcastically."*'
	db	00
L0ABD:	db	'Iolo whispers in your ear.~~"'
	db	00
L0ADB:	db	', we have heard that one before. \'Tis best we leave him bef'
	db	'ore he indulges in another joke."'
	db	00
L0B38:	db	'I don\'t know'
	db	00
L0B45:	db	'to get to the other side'
	db	00
L0B5E:	db	'He almost appears disappointed, but it seems more likely tha'
	db	't it\'s your imagination.'
	db	00
L0BB3:	db	'humor'
	db	00
L0BB9:	db	'I don\'t know'
	db	00
L0BC6:	db	'humor'
	db	00
L0BCC:	db	'He gives a partial smile.~~"To get to the other side. Didst '
	db	'thou think that was funny?"'
	db	00
L0C24:	db	'He appears confused. "That is odd, no one else thinks that j'
	db	'oke is humorous.~~"Perhaps I am more funny than I thought...'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L0C9E:	db	'"No one else finds it humorous either. I will continue pract'
	db	'icing to be funny."'
	db	00
L0CEE:	db	'I don\'t know'
	db	00
L0CFB:	db	'to get to the other side'
	db	00
L0D14:	db	'to get to the other side'
	db	00
L0D2D:	db	'humor'
	db	00
L0D33:	db	'"Oh. Thou hast heard it before."'
	db	00
L0D54:	db	'to get to the other side'
	db	00
L0D6D:	db	'I don\'t know'
	db	00
L0D7A:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0D85:	db	'"The Fellowship is a twenty-year-old organization that holds'
	db	' many festivals, parades, and celebrations. In addition, the'
	db	'y maintain a shelter in the town of Paws. They have an under'
	db	'lying philosophy called the Triad of Inner Strength. This tr'
	db	'iad is broken into the three principles known as `strive for'
	db	' unity,\' `trust thy brother,\' and `worthiness precedes rew'
	db	'ard.\'I will now explain the meaning of each principple."'
	db	00
L0F24:	db	'"This Denton fellow is really long-winded."*'
	db	00
L0F51:	db	'"Strive for unity seems to mean that The Fellowship wants ot'
	db	'hers to work together for the weal of society. Trust thy bro'
	db	'ther implies that each person should not question the action'
	db	's of others. Worthiness precedes reward indicates that The F'
	db	'ellowship\'s attitude towards reward is that one must do wel'
	db	'l to be rewarded."'
	db	00
L108F:	db	'He looks at your medallion.~~"Is mine information correct?"'
	db	00
L10CB:	db	'"I thank thee. I always endeavor to be correct."'
	db	00
L10FC:	db	'"I shall attempt to become better informed."'
	db	00
L1129:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L1134:	db	'help'
	db	00
L1139:	db	'"Yes, '
	db	00
L1140:	db	', I can help thee investigate the crime. I believe the best '
	db	'way to begin would be by speaking with Sir Richter, since he'
	db	' is the one who searched the statue after the incident."'
	db	00
L11F1:	db	'help'
	db	00
L11F6:	db	'got fragments'
	db	00
L1204:	db	'"Perhaps thou shouldst have these stone chips examined by th'
	db	'e healer, Lady Leigh."'
	db	00
L1257:	db	'gargoyle blood'
	db	00
L1266:	db	'got fragments'
	db	00
L1274:	db	'gargoyle blood'
	db	00
L1283:	db	'"That behavior does not seem typical of Sir Horffe. Thou may'
	db	'est wish to report to Lord John-Paul, but I expect there is '
	db	'more to this. It would be a good idea to visit Lady Tory. Sh'
	db	'e is very good at sensing the feelings of others, and may ha'
	db	've learned something by observing the residents after the ev'
	db	'ent."'
	db	00
L13B5:	db	'gargoyle blood'
	db	00
L13C4:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L13C8:	db	'"Good day, '
	db	00
L13D4:	db	'."*'
	db	00
