L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'examine chips'
	db	00
L001B:	db	'This attractive woman gives you an approving look.'
	db	00
L004E:	db	'"Greetings, '
	db	00
L005B:	db	'." Leigh smiles at you.'
	db	00
L0073:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0078:	db	'She blushes. "I am Lady Leigh."'
	db	00
L0098:	db	'name'
	db	00
L009D:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00A1:	db	'"I am the Healer of Serpent\'s Hold."'
	db	00
L00C6:	db	'heal'
	db	00
L00CB:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L00DA:	db	'examine chips'
	db	00
L00E8:	db	'heal'
	db	00
L00ED:	db	'"I am sorry, but I have too many other patients to help thee'
	db	' now. Perhaps when I next open my shop."'
	db	00
L0152:	db	'heal'
	db	00
L0157:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0166:	db	'"Lord Jean-Paul is in charge of keeping the order here, but '
	db	'Sir Denton would be an even better source of information abo'
	db	'ut Serpent\'s Hold."'
	db	00
L01F2:	db	'Denton'
	db	00
L01F9:	db	'John-Paul'
	db	00
L0203:	db	'Serpent\'s Hold'
	db	00
L0212:	db	'John-Paul'
	db	00
L021C:	db	'"He is an easy man to find, for Sir Horffe hardly ever leave'
	db	's his side. Watch for the tall, muscular gargoyle."'
	db	00
L028C:	db	'"In fact," she says, looking off in the distance, "I believe'
	db	' he may have a desire to speak with thee. Perhaps thou shoul'
	db	'dst truly seek him out."'
	db	00
L031D:	db	'"If thou hast business about the town, and are not able to l'
	db	'ocate John-Paul, thou mightest wish to speak with Sir Richte'
	db	'r."'
	db	00
L0399:	db	'John-Paul'
	db	00
L03A3:	db	'Richter'
	db	00
L03AB:	db	'Horffe'
	db	00
L03B2:	db	'Horffe'
	db	00
L03B9:	db	'"He was found at a very young age, apparently abandoned by h'
	db	'is father. Two people took and raised him as their own. As t'
	db	'hou couldst see simply by meeting him, he is a very noble pe'
	db	'rson and a stout warrior."'
	db	00
L0488:	db	'Horffe'
	db	00
L048F:	db	'Richter'
	db	00
L0497:	db	'"He is the armourer. His shop is in the back of the Hold."'
	db	00
L04D2:	db	'Richter'
	db	00
L04DA:	db	'Denton'
	db	00
L04E1:	db	'"He is the tavern keeper at the Hallowed Dock, just inside t'
	db	'he Hold\'s doors. He is wonderful at remembering and discuss'
	db	'ing important facts."'
	db	00
L056E:	db	'Denton'
	db	00
L0575:	db	'examine chips'
	db	00
L0583:	db	'She looks at you, puzzled. "Did I not do that already?"'
	db	00
L05BB:	db	'She takes the stone chips from you and examines them. Using '
	db	'several vials of strange and unusual mixtures, she analyzes '
	db	'the blood. Finally, after a few silent minutes, she looks up'
	db	', grinning.~~"I have determined the nature of the blood. It '
	db	'is definitely not human. In fact," she looks back down at th'
	db	'e sample and raises one eyebrow, "it is gargoyle blood."'
	db	00
L0720:	db	'gargoyle blood'
	db	00
L072F:	db	'"I am afraid that I must be able to see them to examine them'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L076E:	db	'examine chips'
	db	00
L077C:	db	'gargoyle blood'
	db	00
L078B:	db	'She appears thoughtful.~~"What is odd, '
	db	00
L07B3:	db	', is that there is only one gargoyle in Serpent\'s Hold. But'
	db	' I cannot imagine Sir Horffe would have had anything to do w'
	db	'ith this wanton destruction."'
	db	00
L0848:	db	'gargoyle blood'
	db	00
L0857:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L085B:	db	'"Farewell, '
	db	00
L0867:	db	'."*'
	db	00
