L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'The man before you narrows his eyes to slits as he sees you.'
	db	00
L004A:	db	'Blorn sighs heavily. "Why dost thou bother me now?"'
	db	00
L007E:	db	'gargoyles'
	db	00
L0088:	db	'return amulet'
	db	00
L0096:	db	'Lap-Lem'
	db	00
L009E:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00A3:	db	'"Blorn, if thou must know."'
	db	00
L00BF:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00C4:	db	'gargoyles'
	db	00
L00CE:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00D2:	db	'"I don\'t believe I wish to tell thee."'
	db	00
L00F9:	db	'gargoyles'
	db	00
L0103:	db	'A growl escapes his throat.~~"What about the bloody gargoyle'
	db	's? Don\'t tell me thou art a gargoyle lover."'
	db	00
L016C:	db	'"Thou art disgusting, swine!" He spits on your boot.*'
	db	00
L01A2:	db	'"That is good, my friend."~~A sudden inspiration seems to fl'
	db	'ash across his face.~~"Perhaps thou canst help me. As thou u'
	db	'ndoubtedly knowest, I was set upon by a cruel gargoyle not t'
	db	'oo long ago. He nearly took my life!~~"\'Twould be a great h'
	db	'onor, '
	db	00
L0298:	db	', if thou wouldst agree to avenge me! Art thou willing?"'
	db	00
L02D1:	db	'"I thank thee, '
	db	00
L02E1:	db	', thank thee. But I must warn thee, he is a very violent gar'
	db	'goyle. His name is Lap-Lem, which means `man slayer.\' And, '
	db	'do not mention my name, for he hates me more than any other '
	db	'human and would surely attack thee without provocation if my'
	db	' name were to be mentioned."'
	db	00
L03ED:	db	'"Fine, '
	db	00
L03F5:	db	'. Thou art nothing more than a coward." He shakes his head.'
	db	00
L0431:	db	'gargoyles'
	db	00
L043B:	db	'return amulet'
	db	00
L0449:	db	'He glares at you for a moment, then shrugs, muttering, "It'
	db	'\'s not like he earned it honestly or anything..."'
	db	00
L04B5:	db	'"Here! I hope it strangles him!" He thrusts the amulet into '
	db	'your palm. "And I hope he bloody strangles thee, too!"'
	db	00
L0528:	db	'"Thou dost not even have room for it! Get thee away, thou so'
	db	'n of a jackal!"*'
	db	00
L0575:	db	'return amulet'
	db	00
L0583:	db	'Lap-Lem'
	db	00
L058B:	db	'"Thou hast killed the jackal?"'
	db	00
L05AA:	db	'"Wonderful! Thou art truly a trusted friend. I thank thee fo'
	db	'r thine assistance!" He grins at you.'
	db	00
L060C:	db	'"Well, I am sure thou wilt have time soon enough, for he wil'
	db	'l surely head this way to attack me again."'
	db	00
L0674:	db	'Lap-Lem'
	db	00
L067C:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0680:	db	'He gives a slight nod and a quiet grunt, and returns to his '
	db	'business.*'
	db	00
