L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0019:	db	'You see a fat, cheerful-looking merchant.'
	db	00
L0043:	db	'"Hello, hello my friend! Thou dost look like thou needest to'
	db	' spend money!"*'
	db	00
L008F:	db	'"This place looks quite well-off."*'
	db	00
L00B3:	db	'"The entire island is very opulent. It is not the same islan'
	db	'd we once knew."*'
	db	00
L0101:	db	'"Hello! How art thou, my friend?"'
	db	00
L0123:	db	'"How may I help thee?" Budo asks.'
	db	00
L0145:	db	'name'
	db	00
L014A:	db	'"Budo the Fourth at thy service! \'Tis a fine day today, is '
	db	'it not?"'
	db	00
L018E:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0193:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0197:	db	'thou hast come to the right place!@'
	db	00
	db	00
	db	00
L01BD:	db	'ship deed'
	db	00
L01C7:	db	'provisions'
	db	00
L01D2:	db	'armour'
	db	00
L01D9:	db	'weapons'
	db	00
L01E1:	db	'thou shouldst come to my shoppe when '
	db	00
L0207:	db	'it is open! I would be so pleased to '
	db	00
L022D:	db	'help thee then.@'
	db	00
L023E:	db	'"I am a provisioner, like my father before me, and like his '
	db	'father before him, and like his father before him. Budo\'s i'
	db	's an island tradition! Just as The Fellowship will be someda'
	db	'y!~~"If thou art interested in weapons, armour, provisions, '
	db	'or a ship deed, '
	db	00
	db	00
	db	00
	db	00
L0341:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L034C:	db	'armour'
	db	00
L0353:	db	'"Budo\'s carries nothing but the finest quality armour in al'
	db	'l Britannia. I have all the best types of equipment availabl'
	db	'e."'
	db	00
L03CE:	db	'weapons'
	db	00
L03D6:	db	'"Budo\'s offers thee excellent weaponry with superb craftsma'
	db	'nship. Thou wilt not find a better buy for thy money anywher'
	db	'e else!"'
	db	00
L0456:	db	'provisions'
	db	00
L0461:	db	'"Budo\'s also carries a variety of useful things for thy con'
	db	'venience."'
	db	00
L04A7:	db	'ship deed'
	db	00
L04B1:	db	'"But I have already sold thee the deed to \'The Lusty Wench'
	db	'\'! She was the only ship I had at this particular time! I a'
	db	'm sorry!"'
	db	00
L0530:	db	'"I can sell thee the deed to my ship \'The Lusty Wench.\' Sh'
	db	'e is beautiful, my friend. She is guaranteed to last and is '
	db	'the sleekest vessel on the seas! She goes for 800 gold. Want'
	db	' her?"'
	db	00
L05E9:	db	'"A wise move. A magnificent ship for thee!" He takes your go'
	db	'ld.'
	db	00
L0629:	db	'"Thou art carrying too much, my friend! Unload thyself of so'
	db	'me of thy belongings and I will sell thee the deed to this b'
	db	'eautiful ship."'
	db	00
L06B1:	db	'"But thou dost not have enough gold! Perhaps thou shouldst v'
	db	'isit the House of Games and increase the bulges in thy pocke'
	db	'ts!"'
	db	00
L072E:	db	'"But thou wilt never see a ship like this one anywhere in th'
	db	'e world! Too bad!"'
	db	00
L077D:	db	'ship deed'
	db	00
L0787:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L0792:	db	'"The Fellowship has helped me to become a very rich man! Alt'
	db	'hough the business is an inherited enterprise, I owe everyth'
	db	'ing to The Fellowship!"'
	db	00
L0822:	db	'Fellowship'
	db	00
L082D:	db	'everything'
	db	00
L0838:	db	'inherited'
	db	00
L0842:	db	'rich man'
	db	00
L084B:	db	'rich man'
	db	00
L0854:	db	'"My great-grandfather started this business many, many years'
	db	' ago. He was moderately successful, thanks to the Thieves\' '
	db	'Guild. But that era has passed."'
	db	00
L08EC:	db	'Thieves\' Guild'
	db	00
L08FB:	db	'rich man'
	db	00
L0904:	db	'inherited'
	db	00
L090E:	db	'"My great-grandfather passed the shoppe on to his son, and s'
	db	'o forth, down to me. We are born merchants! That is why I kn'
	db	'ow why thou hast come to Budo\'s! Thou wantest to become a p'
	db	'art of the great Budo Legacy! Thou dost need to buy somethin'
	db	'g!"'
	db	00
L0A01:	db	'inherited'
	db	00
L0A0B:	db	'everything'
	db	00
L0A16:	db	'"There was a period shortly after my father died, just as I '
	db	'had inherited the shoppe, when business was poor. There was '
	db	'a danger that I would not be able to keep the shoppe open. B'
	db	'ut The Fellowship convinced me that I should join them. I pr'
	db	'oved my worthiness and The Fellowship helped me financially.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L0B44:	db	'everything'
	db	00
L0B4F:	db	'worthiness'
	db	00
L0B5A:	db	'worthiness'
	db	00
L0B65:	db	'"I do not mind telling thee. The Fellowship shares in one ha'
	db	'lf of my profit."'
	db	00
L0BB3:	db	'worthiness'
	db	00
L0BBE:	db	'Thieves\' Guild'
	db	00
L0BCD:	db	'"It is no more. They dwindled away during my grandfather\'s '
	db	'time. By the time The Fellowship arrived, when I was a boy, '
	db	'there was no trace of them except in family mementos. Even t'
	db	'he pirates are different."'
	db	00
L0C9B:	db	'Thieves\' Guild'
	db	00
L0CAA:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0CB6:	db	'The cube vibrates a moment.~~"That ship sails here frequentl'
	db	'y. I know it makes regular runs to the mainland, stops here,'
	db	' then moves on to the Isle of the Avatar the next morning. T'
	db	'hen it repeats the trip, going the other direction."'
	db	00
L0D9F:	db	'"It stops here regularly. Don\'t know much more about it. Th'
	db	'e crew is very secretive." Budo looks away, obviously not wa'
	db	'nting to talk about the ship.'
	db	00
L0E34:	db	'Crown Jewel'
	db	00
L0E40:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0E44:	db	'"I hope I can help thee again some time, my friend!"*'
	db	00
L0E7A:	db	'@Weapons? Armour?@'
	db	00
L0E8D:	db	'@Provisions here!@'
	db	00
L0EA0:	db	'@Budo\'s is open for business!@'
	db	00
L0EBF:	db	'@Step right in! We\'re open!@'
	db	00
