	; Function at file offset 000FE3EFH
	.funcnumber  04E7H
	.data
	.msize       19E4H
	.dsize       1515H
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L0011:	db	'room'
	db	00
L0016:	db	'drink'
	db	00
L001C:	db	'food'
	db	00
L0021:	db	'You see a woman in her fifties who might have been a pirate '
	db	'wench in her earlier years. Though she is coarse, she has a '
	db	'certain motherly quality.'
	db	00
L00B3:	db	'"Hello, again," Mandy says.'
	db	00
L00CF:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00D4:	db	'"I am Mandy."'
	db	00
L00E2:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00E7:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00EB:	db	'"I run the Fallen Virgin Inn and Tavern. We are open for bre'
	db	'akfast, dinner, and late night hours.'
	db	00
L014D:	db	'"If thou dost want food or drink, or perhaps a room, please '
	db	'say so."'
	db	00
L0192:	db	'Mandy looks at Dupre and says, "Don\'t I know thee?"*'
	db	00
L01C7:	db	'"Yes, milady. I was here a few months ago."*'
	db	00
L01F4:	db	'"I remember! Thou art working for Brommer\'s Britannian trav'
	db	'el guides! Thou art a pub critic!"*'
	db	00
L0253:	db	'"That is right, milady."*'
	db	00
L026D:	db	'"Welcome back! Please try anything on the menu. It is all st'
	db	'ill very good."*'
	db	00
L02BA:	db	'"I thank thee, milady."*'
	db	00
L02D3:	db	'"Thou art a swine, Dupre."*'
	db	00
L02EF:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L02F3:	db	'room'
	db	00
L02F8:	db	'drink'
	db	00
L02FE:	db	'food'
	db	00
L0303:	db	'"Please come to the Tavern then and I will be happy to serve'
	db	' thee."'
	db	00
L0347:	db	'Fallen Virgin'
	db	00
L0355:	db	'food'
	db	00
L035A:	db	'"We serve a good plate of slop, if I do say so myself! That '
	db	'Silverleaf is something. Thou shouldst try that."'
	db	00
L03C8:	db	'food'
	db	00
L03CD:	db	'Silverleaf'
	db	00
L03D8:	db	'drink'
	db	00
L03DE:	db	'"I can offer thee wine and ale."'
	db	00
L03FF:	db	'drink'
	db	00
L0405:	db	'room'
	db	00
L040A:	db	'"Our rooms are 10 gold per person. The only one available no'
	db	'w is the southwest room. The other two already have occupant'
	db	's. Dost thou want one?"'
	db	00
L049A:	db	'"Look there now. Thou hast too many bundles to take the room'
	db	' key!"'
	db	00
L04DD:	db	'"Here is the room key. It is good only until thou dost leave'
	db	' the inn."'
	db	00
L0524:	db	'"It doth seem that thou art a trifle short, '
	db	00
L0551:	db	'."'
	db	00
L0554:	db	'"All right. Some other time."'
	db	00
L0572:	db	'room'
	db	00
L0577:	db	'buy'
	db	00
L057B:	db	'Silverleaf'
	db	00
L0586:	db	'"Best bloody swill thou wilt eat on the face of the earth!"'
	db	00
L05C2:	db	'Silverleaf'
	db	00
L05CD:	db	'Fallen Virgin'
	db	00
L05DB:	db	'"Yes, I have run this tavern and inn since my wenching days.'
	db	'" Mandy laughs. "I was quite a beauty back then, but thou ca'
	db	'nst not tell it now. I know everyone in town and they all kn'
	db	'ow me. If thou dost need to know something about anyone, let'
	db	' me know."'
	db	00
L06D6:	db	'Fallen Virgin'
	db	00
L06E4:	db	'Danag'
	db	00
L06EA:	db	'Blacktooth'
	db	00
L06F5:	db	'Mole'
	db	00
L06FA:	db	'Budo'
	db	00
L06FF:	db	'Glenno'
	db	00
L0706:	db	'Wench'
	db	00
L070C:	db	'Martine'
	db	00
L0714:	db	'Roberto'
	db	00
L071C:	db	'Lucky'
	db	00
L0722:	db	'Gordy'
	db	00
L0728:	db	'Sintag'
	db	00
L072F:	db	'Smithy'
	db	00
L0736:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L073B:	db	'Danag'
	db	00
L0741:	db	'"He helps out at that Fellowship place. He is always interim'
	db	' branch leader for some reason. The real leader, a fellow na'
	db	'med Abraham, is never here. Danag is all right. Kind of gull'
	db	'ible."'
	db	00
L07FC:	db	'Danag'
	db	00
L0802:	db	'Blacktooth'
	db	00
L080D:	db	'"He is a former pirate and rogue, and he can be fairly mean.'
	db	' If he does not warm up to thee immediately, he may not at a'
	db	'll. But once he does, thou wilt learn he is quite a sensitiv'
	db	'e man."'
	db	00
L08C9:	db	'Blacktooth'
	db	00
L08D4:	db	'Mole'
	db	00
L08D9:	db	'"I was a wench with Mole\'s gang of pirates back in... well,'
	db	' it seems a century ago. Mole was rough and tough and a trou'
	db	'ble-maker. Until he joined The Fellowship. That changed him '
	db	'into...," Mandy shrugs. "I know not, a middle-aged former pi'
	db	'rate or some such."'
	db	00
L09DC:	db	'Mole'
	db	00
L09E1:	db	'Budo'
	db	00
L09E6:	db	'"His family has been on Buccaneer\'s Den for generations. Co'
	db	'mes on a trifle too strong with the barking of wares, if tho'
	db	'u dost ask me."'
	db	00
L0A6D:	db	'Budo'
	db	00
L0A72:	db	'Glenno'
	db	00
L0A79:	db	'"He makes me laugh. He is a dear. Thou wouldst not find a mo'
	db	're pleasant, and eager-to-please, man on the island. He is a'
	db	' surprisingly good person." Mandy pauses then adds, "For a p'
	db	'imp."'
	db	00
L0B33:	db	'Glenno'
	db	00
L0B3A:	db	'Wench'
	db	00
L0B40:	db	'"She is a very private person. Works at The Baths. I hear sh'
	db	'e won some kind of competition -- that is why she is fortuna'
	db	'te to be there. I understand Glenno pays them well over ther'
	db	'e."'
	db	00
L0BF8:	db	'Wench'
	db	00
L0BFE:	db	'Martine'
	db	00
L0C06:	db	'"She is a very private person. Works at The Baths. I have no'
	db	't spoken three words to her in my life."'
	db	00
L0C6B:	db	'Martine'
	db	00
L0C73:	db	'Roberto'
	db	00
L0C7B:	db	'"He is a very private person, but, oh, is he an attractive m'
	db	'an, I must say! He works at The Baths. I will admit I am one'
	db	' of his clients. He doth truly clean my dishes, if thou dost'
	db	' know what I mean."'
	db	00
L0D43:	db	'Roberto'
	db	00
L0D4B:	db	'Lucky'
	db	00
L0D51:	db	'"He is a former rogue, I can tell thee that! And to think he'
	db	' makes a living now by teaching others to be the same!" Mand'
	db	'y shrugs. "To each their own."'
	db	00
L0DE8:	db	'Lucky'
	db	00
L0DEE:	db	'Gordy'
	db	00
L0DF4:	db	'"I do not know him that well, although he seems to be a sinc'
	db	'ere man. He runs the House of Games like a ship. He is a for'
	db	'mer pirate as well. Must have been a captain."'
	db	00
L0E9B:	db	'Gordy'
	db	00
L0EA1:	db	'Smithy'
	db	00
L0EA8:	db	'"He was another pirate. I know he works at the House of Game'
	db	's. I suppose he is the man in charge of the actual games. I '
	db	'do not know him well."'
	db	00
L0F37:	db	'Smithy'
	db	00
L0F3E:	db	'Sintag'
	db	00
L0F45:	db	'"Brrrr! He is a scary man. Thou canst tell that he has kille'
	db	'd. He is the guard at the House of Games. Thou dost not want'
	db	' to be caught cheating by him!"'
	db	00
L0FDD:	db	'Sintag'
	db	00
L0FE4:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L0FE9:	db	'You feel your Cube vibrate, but somehow you know that Mandy '
	db	'would have told you the truth without it.'
	db	00
L104F:	db	'Mandy whispers to you. "I know who thou dost mean. He lives '
	db	'somewhere on the island, but I am not sure where. He rarely '
	db	'comes in to the tavern, but I have seen him on occasion."'
	db	00
L1101:	db	'"He scares me to death."'
	db	00
L111A:	db	'Hook'
	db	00
L111F:	db	'scares'
	db	00
L1126:	db	'scares'
	db	00
L112D:	db	'"Well, he is a killer. Some think he is the one responsible '
	db	'for the murder that happened last year."'
	db	00
L1192:	db	'scares'
	db	00
L1199:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L11A0:	db	'killer'
	db	00
L11A7:	db	'killer'
	db	00
L11AE:	db	'"This man they call Hook has the way of the killer about him'
	db	'. Thou canst see it in his eyes. I would be extremely carefu'
	db	'l if I were to run afoul of him."'
	db	00
L1248:	db	'killer'
	db	00
L124F:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L1256:	db	'"There was a thief named Duncan who had stolen funds from th'
	db	'e House of Games and The Baths. I believe he may have broken'
	db	' into the Fellowship Hall as well. Anyway, he was arrested. '
	db	'But one morning, when the guard brought the man his breakfas'
	db	't, he was gone! Everyone thought he had escaped until his bo'
	db	'dy was found in the house where old Blacktooth lives. This w'
	db	'as before Blacktooth lived there."'
	db	00
L13E1:	db	'murder'
	db	00
L13E8:	db	'body'
	db	00
L13ED:	db	'body'
	db	00
L13F2:	db	'"It was mutilated -- his arms and legs had been cut off, and'
	db	' he had literally lost his head! To this day, no one knows w'
	db	'ho did it. But when Hook is around, people talk behind his b'
	db	'ack. He is certainly capable of doing it!"'
	db	00
L14D1:	db	'body'
	db	00
L14D6:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L14DA:	db	'"Nice talking with thee. I shall see thee later, I hope."*'
	db	00
