	; Function at file offset 001030FDH
	.funcnumber  04EFH
	.data
	.msize       1F62H
	.dsize       1C6AH
L0000:	db	'Before you is a skinny man with a silly smile on his face. H'
	db	'e is holding a lantern in one hand and a dirty spoon in the '
	db	'other.'
	db	00
L007F:	db	'"Hello, again," says Owings. He smiles and tips his mining h'
	db	'at to you.'
	db	00
L00C6:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L00CA:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00CE:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00D3:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00D8:	db	'"My name is Owings," he says giving you a rapid up and down '
	db	'handshake. "Pleased to meet thee."'
	db	00
L0137:	db	'"My partner\'s name is Malloy."'
	db	00
L0156:	db	'"Thou dost already know my partner, Malloy."'
	db	00
L0183:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0188:	db	'job'
	db	00
L018C:	db	'"I do what he does." Owings jerks his thumb towards Malloy d'
	db	'igging away next to him. The fat man is trying to chisel thr'
	db	'ough the rock wall using only a spoon. Owings\'s thumb hits '
	db	'him in the back.'
	db	00
L0250:	db	'Malloy looks over at you and gives you a friendly wave as he'
	db	' goes to stand up. As he does this, he bumps his head. There'
	db	' is a loud knocking noise. He says, "Oooooooohh!" very loudl'
	db	'y. His cry echoes through the length of the mineshaft. You c'
	db	'an feel dust from the cracks in the ceiling settling on your'
	db	' shoulder.*'
	db	00
L0388:	db	'Owings suddenly looks very nervous and throws both of his ar'
	db	'ms over his head. There is a terrible rumble and you feel th'
	db	'e ground beneath you start to shake. After a moment the trem'
	db	'or subsides. Both of them look very relieved.*'
	db	00
L046B:	db	'Malloy puts one hand up to his bruised head and feels around'
	db	' on the ground with the other. He eventually finds and picks'
	db	' up a metal mining helmet. He gingerly places it over his he'
	db	'ad which appears to still be causing him pain. You can see t'
	db	'hat the top of Malloy\'s head barely fits into it.*'
	db	00
L058E:	db	'"Allow me to rephrase that. I do what he does, except I alwa'
	db	'ys wears me helmet." With that Owings gives a big nod, throw'
	db	'ing his head up and down. This causes his helmet to fall dow'
	db	'n over his eyes.*'
	db	00
L0654:	db	'Malloy looks over at you and at Owings, giving both of you a'
	db	'n incredulous pouting grimace.*'
	db	00
L06B0:	db	'eyes'
	db	00
L06B5:	db	'helmet'
	db	00
L06BC:	db	'tremor'
	db	00
L06C3:	db	'"Normally I am digging, but as of late I cannot seem to find'
	db	' my partner Malloy. So I suppose my job is to look for him. '
	db	'I wonder where he has gone to?"'
	db	00
L075B:	db	'tremor'
	db	00
L0762:	db	'Owings puts his hand on your shoulder and puts a finger up t'
	db	'o his lips. "Shhhhh! Be very quiet! This is an old tunnel. M'
	db	'ikos, the foreman, says that any sudden loud noise could tri'
	db	'gger a cave-in!"*'
	db	00
L0828:	db	'Malloy goes back to digging. The exertion from his work caus'
	db	'es his helmet to fall off. He sighs, picks it up, puts it ba'
	db	'ck on and goes back to work. Almost immediately it falls off'
	db	' again. He puts it back on. It falls off. He puts it back on'
	db	'. Malloy grunts and sighs. It falls off. Dejected, he puts i'
	db	't back on. This happens again and again so many times that i'
	db	't is almost painful to watch. Finally, Malloy just lets the '
	db	'helmet lie there and throws a tantrum. He trembles and bites'
	db	' into his hand to keep from crying out in frustration.*'
	db	00
L0A40:	db	'Owings steps up to Malloy and puts his finger to his lips. "'
	db	'Shhhhhh!" Looking down, Owings sees Malloy\'s helmet on the '
	db	'ground. "Dost thou not remember Mikos telling thee to always'
	db	' wear thine helmet?" he says. Owings picks it up and dusts i'
	db	't off. He pushes it down on top of Malloy\'s sore head, caus'
	db	'ing Malloy to wrinkle his face in pain. "No need to thank me'
	db	'!" Owings says. With that, he nods his head up and down, cau'
	db	'sing the front of his helmet to fall down over his eyes. He '
	db	'reaches out with his arms blindly.*'
	db	00
L0C42:	db	'Malloy looks over at Owings and at you, giving you both a po'
	db	'uting grimace.*'
	db	00
L0C8E:	db	'tremor'
	db	00
L0C95:	db	'eyes'
	db	00
L0C9A:	db	'eyes'
	db	00
L0C9F:	db	'You reach up and tip Owings\'s helmet back so that it is no '
	db	'longer covering his eyes. He smiles at you thankfully. He ta'
	db	'kes off his helmet to scratch at the top of his head. He put'
	db	's it back on and it immediately tilts back down over his eye'
	db	's.*'
	db	00
L0D92:	db	'Malloy watches this, smirks and slowly shakes his head.*'
	db	00
L0DCB:	db	'eyes'
	db	00
L0DD0:	db	'Owings\'s helmet'
	db	00
L0DE0:	db	'helmet'
	db	00
L0DE7:	db	'"Mikos, the foreman of this mine told us to always wear a he'
	db	'lmet. It is very important. The two of us even sent a mining'
	db	' helmet to Lord British. A funny man dressed just like the A'
	db	'vatar told us of how Lord British had been hit in the head w'
	db	'ith falling objects - twice! So we sent a helmet to him."*'
	db	00
L0F12:	db	'It appears Malloy can no longer stand being left out of the '
	db	'conversation. "It was -mine- idea to send Lord British the h'
	db	'elmet," he says proudly. "While we have not yet heard back f'
	db	'rom him about it I am sure he will find some way to thank us'
	db	'." Malloy\'s helmet falls off and he stands there a long tim'
	db	'e before regaining the composure to pick it up again.*'
	db	00
L1074:	db	'helmet'
	db	00
L107B:	db	'Owings\'s helmet'
	db	00
L108B:	db	'"Thou art a kind person to fix mine helmet for me," Owings s'
	db	'ays, giving you a big grin.'
	db	00
L10E3:	db	'You see Malloy look very suspiciously at Owings\'s helmet. "'
	db	'Thou art wearing mine hat!" He lets out a growling "Hmmmf!" '
	db	'and snatches Owings\'s helmet off of his head. Malloy remove'
	db	's his helmet, casually tossing it to the ground. He then put'
	db	's Owings\'s helmet on. It fits him perfectly. Malloy flashes'
	db	' you both a big condescending smile. With a curt nod he turn'
	db	's to go back to work.*'
	db	00
L125F:	db	'Owings looks at Malloy and then back to you. He is very conf'
	db	'used. "That was not very nice, Malloy! Thou didst take mine '
	db	'hat!" Owings\'s face is covered with a large frown. His lowe'
	db	'r lip starts to tremble.'
	db	00
L132B:	db	'eyes'
	db	00
L1330:	db	'Owings\'s helmet'
	db	00
L1340:	db	'mine hat'
	db	00
L1349:	db	'mine hat'
	db	00
L1352:	db	'Owings reaches over and takes the mining helmet off Malloy'
	db	'\'s head so carefully that he does not notice. Owings puts t'
	db	'he helmet back on with a little sneaky laugh of triumph. Poi'
	db	'nting to the hat he taps Malloy on the back to let him know '
	db	'what he\'s done.*'
	db	00
L1450:	db	'Malloy stops digging and goes to stand up. As he does this h'
	db	'e hits his head on the ceiling. Once again it makes a loud k'
	db	'nocking noise. Malloy says "Oooooh!" After shaking his head '
	db	'clear, he slowly steps toward Owings. He is quite angry - so'
	db	' angry that he does not notice that he has stepped into the '
	db	'other helmet and it is stuck onto his foot. Taking his spoon'
	db	' he whaps Owings in the nose with it.*'
	db	00
L15DF:	db	'Upon getting hit in the nose, Owings jerks his head back, ca'
	db	'using his helmet to fall off. "Ooh! Mine helmet!" he cries.*'
	db	00
L1658:	db	'Malloy is so angry that he can no longer contain himself. "T'
	db	'hat is not thine helmet! It is mine helmet!" he shouts. This'
	db	' sends a thunderous echo down the mineshaft. You can feel a '
	db	'shower of falling dust and rocks. There is a low rumble and '
	db	'an ominous vibration of the earth. Owings and Malloy are so '
	db	'scared that in their panic they run right into each other. M'
	db	'alloy\'s foot - the one with the helmet stuck on it - slides'
	db	' out from under him and he lands on his posterior. Both cove'
	db	'r their heads in anticipation of a massive cave-in.*'
	db	00
L186C:	db	'mine hat'
	db	00
L1875:	db	'cave-in'
	db	00
L187D:	db	'cave-in'
	db	00
L1885:	db	'After a few moments of fearful anticipation, the tremor subs'
	db	'ides. The tunnel is still standing, none the worse for wear.'
	db	' "I thought I was done for!" says Owings. With that, a large'
	db	' piece of rock falls from the ceiling and lands squarely on '
	db	'Owings\'s head. It makes a loud knocking noise. Owings start'
	db	's to pout and cry very childishly.'
	db	00
L19D3:	db	'Malloy points at Owings and laughs until tears run down his '
	db	'face. Glancing up at the ceiling, Malloy starts feeling arou'
	db	'nd for his helmet. Finally, feeling underneath himself, he p'
	db	'ulls out his helmet, on top of which he had fallen! Looking '
	db	'at the hat, Malloy discovers that his bulk has crumpled it. '
	db	'It is ruined. He puts it on anyway, looking most ridiculous,'
	db	' and his tears of laughter turn to tears of sorrow. Now, bot'
	db	'h of them break down into fits of childish bawling. Malloy l'
	db	'ooks at Owings and says "This is another fine mess thou hast'
	db	' gotten us into!"*'
	db	00
L1C02:	db	'cave-in'
	db	00
L1C0A:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1C0E:	db	'Owings and Malloy, both unable to stop their crying, wave go'
	db	'odbye.*'
	db	00
L1C52:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
	db	00
L1C66:	db	'."*'
	db	00
