L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'The warrior carries himself with confidence.'
	db	00
L003A:	db	'"Hail, '
	db	00
L0042:	db	'," says Cairbre.'
	db	00
L0053:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0058:	db	'"Thou mayest call me Cairbre, '
	db	00
L0077:	db	'."'
	db	00
L007A:	db	'name'
	db	00
L007F:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0083:	db	'"I am a sell-sword. But at the moment, I am trying to help m'
	db	'y friend regain his senses."'
	db	00
L00DC:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00E0:	db	'senses'
	db	00
L00E7:	db	'friend'
	db	00
L00EE:	db	'friend'
	db	00
L00F5:	db	'"I was not about to let Cosmo venture down here by himself. '
	db	'So, I offered to accompany him, as did Kallibrus."'
	db	00
L0164:	db	'He points to the gargoyle.'
	db	00
L017F:	db	'Kallibrus'
	db	00
L0189:	db	'friend'
	db	00
L0190:	db	'Kallibrus'
	db	00
L019A:	db	'"He is a comrade in arms of mine, and also a friend of Cosmo'
	db	'\'s. I have yet to meet a more trustworthy companion, for he'
	db	' more than disproves all the rumors about gargoyles."'
	db	00
L0247:	db	'Kallibrus'
	db	00
L0251:	db	'senses'
	db	00
L0258:	db	'"\'Tis a long story. Cosmo is looking for the unicorn that s'
	db	'upposedly inhabits this cavern." He looks you in the eye and'
	db	' shrugs.~~"He is a fool."'
	db	00
L02E9:	db	'*'
	db	00
L02EB:	db	'"I heard that, Cairbre!"*'
	db	00
L0305:	db	'senses'
	db	00
L030C:	db	'fool'
	db	00
L0311:	db	'unicorn'
	db	00
L0319:	db	'unicorn'
	db	00
L0321:	db	'"The unicorn is traditionally a way to prove the purity of a'
	db	' young maiden. However, less commonly known is that it will '
	db	'also reveal a young man\'s, uh, lack of, um, wild oats."'
	db	00
L03D1:	db	'unicorn'
	db	00
L03D9:	db	'fool'
	db	00
L03DE:	db	'"Ophelia does not love him! She simply sent him on this ques'
	db	't to be rid of him. I doubt she expects him to find the unic'
	db	'orn, let alone return to her."'
	db	00
L0475:	db	'fool'
	db	00
L047A:	db	'rid'
	db	00
L047E:	db	'Ophelia'
	db	00
L0486:	db	'Ophelia'
	db	00
L048E:	db	'"He met her in Jhelom. She was serving in the Bunk and Stool'
	db	'. Apparently it was `love at first sight,\' as he calls it."'
	db	00
L0506:	db	'Ophelia'
	db	00
L050E:	db	'rid'
	db	00
L0512:	db	'"The nature of her request is quite ironic, for I would expe'
	db	'ct that the unicorn would have shunned her quite some time a'
	db	'go. He is not to her tastes, I would imagine, and, were he t'
	db	'o truly know her, she would not be to his. But, alas, love i'
	db	's blind, as they say."'
	db	00
L0619:	db	'they'
	db	00
L061E:	db	'rid'
	db	00
L0622:	db	'they'
	db	00
L0627:	db	'"I do not know who `they\' are, but that is what they say, i'
	db	's it not?"'
	db	00
L066D:	db	'they'
	db	00
L0672:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0676:	db	'"\'Til next time, '
	db	00
L0688:	db	'."*'
	db	00
