	; Function at file offset 0010DD09H
	.funcnumber  04F8H
	.data
	.msize       1884H
	.dsize       143FH
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a scholarly-looking man with a friendly expression.'
	db	00
L0049:	db	'"Salutations, '
	db	00
L0058:	db	'." Brion smiles.'
	db	00
L0069:	db	'Caddellite'
	db	00
L0074:	db	'crystals'
	db	00
L007D:	db	'have crystal'
	db	00
L008A:	db	'Zelda\'s feelings'
	db	00
L009B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00A0:	db	'"Why, thou mayest call me Brion."'
	db	00
L00C2:	db	'Zelda\'s feelings'
	db	00
L00D3:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00D8:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00DC:	db	'"I am the head of the observatory here in Moonglow," he says'
	db	' proudly. "This is where the telescope is kept."'
	db	00
L0149:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L0152:	db	'telescope'
	db	00
L015C:	db	'event'
	db	00
L0162:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L016B:	db	'"Why, I love living here in Moonglow. I very much like the p'
	db	'eople here."'
	db	00
L01B4:	db	'people'
	db	00
L01BB:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L01C4:	db	'people'
	db	00
L01CB:	db	'"Hast thou spoken with my twin, Nelson? He heads the Lycaeum'
	db	'. Or Elad? And surely thou knowest about the mage, Penumbra.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L0245:	db	'Penumbra'
	db	00
L024E:	db	'Elad'
	db	00
L0253:	db	'Nelson'
	db	00
L025A:	db	'people'
	db	00
L0261:	db	'Zelda\'s feelings'
	db	00
L0272:	db	'"Oh, I see," he shrugs. "I never really thought about my bro'
	db	'ther\'s assistant in such a manner. That is too bad, for my '
	db	'time permits nothing but mine observations. Ah, well, what e'
	db	'lse can I help thee with?"'
	db	00
L0340:	db	'Zelda\'s feelings'
	db	00
L0351:	db	'Nelson'
	db	00
L0358:	db	'"I do not see him as often as I would like, for we are so he'
	db	'avily involved with our work. He will be easy to recognize s'
	db	'houldst thou see him, for people tell us we look identical. '
	db	'I do not see it, of course, for, not only was he born with t'
	db	'he brains, but also the handsome face."'
	db	00
L0470:	db	'Nelson'
	db	00
L0477:	db	'Elad'
	db	00
L047C:	db	'"Poor Elad. He sometimes joins me at night to view the heave'
	db	'ns. He has been trying to leave Moonglow for many years. He '
	db	'likes the island, but is filled with wanderlust." He smiles.'
	db	00
L0531:	db	'Elad'
	db	00
L0536:	db	'Penumbra'
	db	00
L053F:	db	'"Thou hast not heard? Why, two hundred years ago she put her'
	db	'self to sleep."'
	db	00
L058B:	db	'Penumbra'
	db	00
L0594:	db	'telescope'
	db	00
L059E:	db	'"I have it upstairs, of course. Thou art welcome to use it a'
	db	's often as thou wishest. In fact, I also have an orrery, sho'
	db	'uldst thou desire to see that as well."'
	db	00
L063E:	db	'orrery'
	db	00
L0645:	db	'telescope'
	db	00
L064F:	db	'Caddellite'
	db	00
L065A:	db	'He looks at you strangely, shrugs, and says, "Why, Caddellit'
	db	'e is a mineral that is not native to Britannia. In fact, it '
	db	'only comes from meteorites.~~ "And the last known meteor to '
	db	'strike the planet landed somewhere in the North East sea. Wh'
	db	'y dost thou want to know?"'
	db	00
L0765:	db	'helmet'
	db	00
L076C:	db	'Caddellite'
	db	00
L0777:	db	'helmet'
	db	00
L077E:	db	'"Thou dost want a helmet made of Caddellite?" He thinks care'
	db	'fully. "Perhaps Zorn in Minoc would have the skills to build'
	db	' a helmet such as thou desirest. If thou findest the Caddell'
	db	'ite, take it to him.~~"I have heard rumors of an island that'
	db	' once existed in the North East sea. Perhaps my brother at t'
	db	'he Lycaeum could help with that."'
	db	00
L08CC:	db	'helmet'
	db	00
L08D3:	db	'orrery'
	db	00
L08DA:	db	'The orrery? Why, \'tis a model of all the planets in our sol'
	db	'ar system, including the two moons of Britannia. The orrery '
	db	'moves to match the actual, current orbits of our real system'
	db	'.'
	db	00
L098F:	db	'"I am very excited, for shortly a very rare event will occur'
	db	'!"'
	db	00
L09CE:	db	'event'
	db	00
L09D4:	db	'orrery'
	db	00
L09DB:	db	'event'
	db	00
L09E1:	db	'"Thou art referring to what we in the business call the Astr'
	db	'onomical Alignment. The planets and the moons will all line '
	db	'up perfectly, something that happens only once every 800 yea'
	db	'rs!"'
	db	00
L0A9A:	db	'event'
	db	00
L0AA0:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0AA4:	db	'"Good day, '
	db	00
L0AB0:	db	'. Thou mayest use mine observatory as often as thou wishest.'
	db	'"*'
	db	00
L0AEF:	db	'"Before thou dost depart, let me show thee a few of my trink'
	db	'ets. Here is my..."'
	db	00
L0B3F:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
L0B47:	db	'crystals'
	db	00
L0B50:	db	'kite'
	db	00
L0B55:	db	'sextant'
	db	00
L0B5D:	db	'moon'
	db	00
L0B62:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
L0B6A:	db	'moon'
	db	00
L0B6F:	db	'"This represents one of the moons that orbit Britannia." He '
	db	'hands the model to you. Taking it, you quickly realize that '
	db	'it is made up entirely of green cheese.~~"I carved it myself'
	db	'," he says as you return it to him.'
	db	00
L0C47:	db	'"Now where did that go?" he says, scratching his head. "Well'
	db	', it is around here somewhere. I can show thee at a later ti'
	db	'me." He seems more distraught than he is willing to convey.'
	db	00
L0CFB:	db	'moon'
	db	00
L0D00:	db	'sextant'
	db	00
L0D08:	db	'He hands you a solid gold sextant. "This has been passed on '
	db	'to each and every individual who has ever held a position at'
	db	' the observatory here in Moonglow. \'Tis more than 200 years'
	db	' old." He beams as you return it to him.'
	db	00
L0DE4:	db	'"Damn! \'Tis gone! That has been here for more than 200 year'
	db	's." He does not seem pleased.'
	db	00
L0E3D:	db	'sextant'
	db	00
L0E45:	db	'kite'
	db	00
L0E4A:	db	'He shows you a kite. "I made this myself by reading one of t'
	db	'he books in my brother\'s library."'
	db	00
L0EA9:	db	'"Where did that disappear to?" He scratches his chin, obviou'
	db	'sly puzzled. "I do hope it has not disappeared. I constructe'
	db	'd it from a book in my brother\'s library."'
	db	00
L0F4C:	db	'kite'
	db	00
L0F51:	db	'crystals'
	db	00
L0F5A:	db	'"This," he says, presenting a collection of crystals that se'
	db	'em to be attached in some indeterminable fashion, "is an orr'
	db	'ery viewer. It permits one to see mine orrery here from anyw'
	db	'here in Britannia."~~He seems thoughtful.~~"I know thou cann'
	db	'ot stay around here to see the alignment.'
	db	00
L1074:	db	'Wouldst thou like to have this to view mine orrery and bette'
	db	'r predict the planet\'s position?"'
	db	00
L10D2:	db	'He smiles proudly. "I thought thou wouldst. However, there i'
	db	's one problem. I still need one more crystal to completely f'
	db	'inish the viewer. If thou wouldst visit the tavern, thou mig'
	db	'htest find one of the merchants or travellers there who some'
	db	'times provide me with crystals. If thou canst find another c'
	db	'rystal, I will be able to give thee the completed viewer."'
	db	00
L1239:	db	'"Very well, '
	db	00
L1246:	db	'. I hope thou dost not regret this later."'
	db	00
L1271:	db	'crystals'
	db	00
L127A:	db	'have crystal'
	db	00
L1287:	db	'"Thou hast the crystal? Excellent." He takes the crystal tha'
	db	't you got from the adventurer and begins attaching it to his'
	db	' orrery viewer. Shortly he is finished.'
	db	00
L1327:	db	'have crystal'
	db	00
L1334:	db	'want crystal'
	db	00
L1341:	db	'"I am sorry, '
	db	00
L134F:	db	', but I must have the crystal to complete the viewer."'
	db	00
L1386:	db	'want crystal'
	db	00
L1393:	db	'"Use it well, '
	db	00
L13A2:	db	'." He gives the contraption to you.'
	db	00
L13C6:	db	'He shakes his head. "Thou dost not have enough room for it. '
	db	'Perhaps when thou dost return at a later time."'
	db	00
L1432:	db	'want crystal'
	db	00
