	; Function at file offset 0010F591H
	.funcnumber  04F9H
	.data
	.msize       1696H
	.dsize       12B6H
L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a scholarly-looking man with a friendly expression.'
	db	00
L0049:	db	'"Salutations, '
	db	00
L0058:	db	'."'
	db	00
L005B:	db	'North East sea'
	db	00
L006A:	db	'Zelda\'s response'
	db	00
L007B:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0080:	db	'"Thou mayest call me Nelson."'
	db	00
L009E:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00A3:	db	'North East sea'
	db	00
L00B2:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00B6:	db	'"I am the Lycaeum head here in Moonglow, but," he leans clos'
	db	'e to you, "mine assistant, Zelda, does most of the work."'
	db	00
L012C:	db	'Zelda'
	db	00
L0132:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L013B:	db	'Zelda'
	db	00
L0141:	db	'"She is an excellent assistant. The Lycaeum has never perfor'
	db	'med better. However, she is a little too stern, I believe, a'
	db	'nd," he leans in again, "I think she is quite beautiful."'
	db	00
L01F3:	db	'beautiful'
	db	00
L01FD:	db	'stern'
	db	00
L0203:	db	'Zelda'
	db	00
L0209:	db	'North East sea'
	db	00
L0218:	db	'"I have heard the rumors of an island, but I know nothing el'
	db	'se about it, I am afraid. Thou mightest wish to speak with J'
	db	'illian -- she should know a little about the area."'
	db	00
L02C4:	db	'North East sea'
	db	00
L02D3:	db	'stern'
	db	00
L02D9:	db	'"She has put an extraordinary amount of time and effort into'
	db	' ensuring the activities in this edifice happen smoothly. An'
	db	'd," he adds, "she takes it personally when they do not!"'
	db	00
L038A:	db	'stern'
	db	00
L0390:	db	'beautiful'
	db	00
L039A:	db	'"Dost thou not agree? I am flushed whenever her fair presenc'
	db	'e passes by. But!" he holds up his index finger, "I fear she'
	db	' does not share a mutual attraction. And she is far too seri'
	db	'ous for me to feel comfortable with a proposal."'
	db	00
L047F:	db	'Zelda\'s feelings'
	db	00
L0490:	db	'beautiful'
	db	00
L049A:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L04A3:	db	'"I love the island and the people. Mostly the people."'
	db	00
L04DA:	db	'people'
	db	00
L04E1:	db	'Moonglow'
	db	00
L04EA:	db	'people'
	db	00
L04F1:	db	'"Hast thou met my twin brother? He heads the Observatory her'
	db	'e. And somewhere in the Lycaeum thou canst find Mariah. Sadl'
	db	'y, she is not well up here." He touches his head.~~"Jillian,'
	db	' the sage, also studies here in the Lycaeum. A good person t'
	db	'o see about other residents of Moonglow would be the bartend'
	db	'er at the Friendly Knave. Phearcy knows almost all of us her'
	db	'e on the island.~~"Oh, and thou must not forget the legend o'
	db	'f Penumbra. \'Twas two hundred years ago she cast herself in'
	db	'to a deep slumber. Now that I think about it, '
	db	00
L06FF:	db	', thou art the one she predicted would awaken her.~~"Better '
	db	'hasten, '
	db	00
L0744:	db	'," he chuckles.'
	db	00
L0754:	db	'people'
	db	00
L075B:	db	'Penumbra'
	db	00
L0764:	db	'Phearcy'
	db	00
L076C:	db	'Jillian'
	db	00
L0774:	db	'Mariah'
	db	00
L077B:	db	'twin'
	db	00
L0780:	db	'twin'
	db	00
L0785:	db	'"His name is Brion. People often mistake us for each other, '
	db	'but I think we are nothing alike -- he got all the looks -an'
	db	'd- the brains!"'
	db	00
L080D:	db	'twin'
	db	00
L0812:	db	'Mariah'
	db	00
L0819:	db	'"She was once an adept mage, but ever since the wizards bega'
	db	'n losing their, er, faculties, she followed suit."'
	db	00
L0888:	db	'Mariah'
	db	00
L088F:	db	'Jillian'
	db	00
L0897:	db	'"She rarely has time for visitors, but I know she takes on s'
	db	'tudents every now and then."'
	db	00
L08F0:	db	'Jillian'
	db	00
L08F8:	db	'Phearcy'
	db	00
L0900:	db	'"That one keeps up on his politics, or rather, his gossip," '
	db	'he says, grinning. "If thou dost want to learn about a resid'
	db	'ent of Moonglow, visit him."'
	db	00
L0995:	db	'Phearcy'
	db	00
L099D:	db	'Penumbra'
	db	00
L09A6:	db	'"Interestingly enough, no one has ever discovered how to ent'
	db	'er her house. I believe those mysterious signs on the door r'
	db	'equire one to have specific items to place next to the plaqu'
	db	'es."'
	db	00
L0A5F:	db	'Penumbra'
	db	00
L0A68:	db	'Zelda\'s response'
	db	00
L0A79:	db	'He smiles broadly. "Truly that was her response? I am please'
	db	'd to no end! I thank thee, '
	db	00
L0AD1:	db	', for bringing this joyful message."'
	db	00
L0AF6:	db	'Zelda\'s response'
	db	00
L0B07:	db	'Zelda\'s feelings'
	db	00
L0B18:	db	'"Oh. Oh well," he shrugs in an attempt at indifference. "She'
	db	' was not truly important anyway."'
	db	00
L0B76:	db	'Zelda\'s feelings'
	db	00
L0B87:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0B8B:	db	'"Good day, '
	db	00
L0B97:	db	'. Thou of course dost have free reign of the Lycaeum."*'
	db	00
L0BCF:	db	'"Of course thou mayest have free reign of the building. But '
	db	'first," he grins, "let me show thee my..."'
	db	00
L0C36:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
L0C3E:	db	'book'
	db	00
L0C43:	db	'quill holder'
	db	00
L0C50:	db	'bookmark'
	db	00
L0C59:	db	'bookstand'
	db	00
L0C63:	db	'bookstand'
	db	00
L0C6D:	db	'"This solid brass bookstand has matching, overhanging candle'
	db	'holder for late-night exploration in literature. I invented '
	db	'it myself."'
	db	00
L0CF1:	db	'"\'Twas just here..." he scratches his chin. "Oh well, never'
	db	' mind."'
	db	00
L0D34:	db	'bookstand'
	db	00
L0D3E:	db	'bookmark'
	db	00
L0D47:	db	'"This," he says, holding a solid-gold sheet shaped like a ma'
	db	'ple leaf, "I purchased at an auction for only half of its va'
	db	'lue."'
	db	00
L0DC5:	db	'He appears upset. "I knew someday that would be stolen," he '
	db	'says angrily.~~"I should have known better than to show it t'
	db	'o every person who comes to visit."'
	db	00
L0E61:	db	'bookmark'
	db	00
L0E6A:	db	'quill holder'
	db	00
L0E77:	db	'He shows you a serpent-shaped, oaken quill holder and its ma'
	db	'tching scroll opener. "This I picked up\twhile travelling th'
	db	'rough -- thou canst guess it -- Serpent\'s Hold."'
	db	00
L0F1F:	db	'He shows you a serpent-shaped, oaken quill holder.\t"This I '
	db	'picked up while travelling through -- thou\tcanst guess it -'
	db	'- Serpent\'s Hold. But," he appears puzzled, "I could have s'
	db	'worn the matching letter opener was here as well. How odd."'
	db	00
L100C:	db	'"The quill holder is gone?" he exclaims. "And what about the'
	db	'..." he seems to be searching for something.~~"The matching '
	db	'scroll opener is also missing!"'
	db	00
L10A4:	db	'quill holder'
	db	00
L10B1:	db	'book'
	db	00
L10B6:	db	'He gingerly pulls out a leatherbound tome. From his robe, he'
	db	' removes a handkerchief and meticulously wipes away the dust'
	db	'.~~"This was given to me by Lord British himself. See, \'tis'
	db	' the first edition."~~The book he carefully places in your p'
	db	'alms is very old, and the gold leaf plating of the title has'
	db	' been almost entirely rubbed off. Turning the book right sid'
	db	'e up, you can read the title: "Stranger in a Strange Land."'
	db	00
L1259:	db	'"\'Tis not here... Oh well, Zelda must have put it back on t'
	db	'he shelf." He sighs.'
	db	00
L12A9:	db	'book'
	db	00
L12AE:	db	'nothing'
	db	00
