	; Function at file offset 00115004H
	.funcnumber  04FEH
	.data
	.msize       20DCH
	.dsize       1CB4H
L0000:	db	'You see a creature the size and shape of a horse. From its h'
	db	'ead protrudes a single straight horn. It looks at you with e'
	db	'yes that shine with intelligence.'
	db	00
L009A:	db	'"I greet thee once again, Avatar," says Lasher, the unicorn.'
	db	00
L00D7:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L00DB:	db	'job'
	db	00
L00DF:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00E4:	db	'name'
	db	00
L00E9:	db	'The creature speaks. "My name is Lasher."'
	db	00
L0113:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0118:	db	'job'
	db	00
L011C:	db	'Lasher looks at you and blinks. "Come now, Avatar! I do not '
	db	'live by the rules that govern the society of Mankind. There '
	db	'is what I am, which is a unicorn. Then there is my purpose, '
	db	'which is another thing altogether."'
	db	00
L01F4:	db	'purpose'
	db	00
L01FC:	db	'unicorn'
	db	00
L0204:	db	'unicorn'
	db	00
L020C:	db	'Lasher stares at you, stupefied. "Tell me, dost thou know wh'
	db	'at a unicorn is?"'
	db	00
L025A:	db	'Lasher stares blankly at you. His mouth hangs open. "Very we'
	db	'll. Then I shall tell thee what a unicorn is.'
	db	00
L02C4:	db	'Lasher shakes his head sadly. "No, thou merely thinks thou d'
	db	'ost know what a unicorn is, but I shall tell thee the truth.'
	db	00
L033D:	db	'"A unicorn is one of a family of nature spirits that were on'
	db	'ce called upon to aid a very powerful wizard many, many year'
	db	's ago."'
	db	00
L03BD:	db	'unicorn'
	db	00
L03C5:	db	'wizard'
	db	00
L03CC:	db	'purpose'
	db	00
L03D4:	db	'"Oh, do not be coy with me, Avatar. Thou dost know very well'
	db	' the purpose of a unicorn. ~~We are foolproof virgin detecto'
	db	'rs!"'
	db	00
L0451:	db	'purpose'
	db	00
L0459:	db	'virgin detector'
	db	00
L0469:	db	'wizard'
	db	00
L0470:	db	'"I do not remember the wizard\'s name, for much time has pas'
	db	'sed since then, but suffice it to say that he was a royal ba'
	db	'stard. Anyway, for one reason or another, the chieftain of o'
	db	'ur clan, who at that time was a horse\'s ass named Sharp-Hoo'
	db	'f, decided that rather than heed this wizard\'s rightful and'
	db	' properly performed ritual of calling, he was going to take '
	db	'the herd and chase after this bevy of really fine fillies."'
	db	00
L0611:	db	'wizard'
	db	00
L0618:	db	'Sharp-Hoof'
	db	00
L0623:	db	'Sharp-Hoof'
	db	00
L062E:	db	'"Where was I? Oh, yes, Sharp-Hoof! The next morning, after w'
	db	'e had had our way with these fillies, this wizard called us '
	db	'again. This time Sharp-Hoof realized that we had best answer'
	db	', and were we sorry that we did! The wizard was horribly ang'
	db	'ry! And, well, I will just say that our agreements with such'
	db	' people are very, very binding."'
	db	00
L077B:	db	'Sharp-Hoof'
	db	00
L0786:	db	'binding'
	db	00
L078E:	db	'binding'
	db	00
L0796:	db	'"Not only were we bound in service to this wizard for a thou'
	db	'sand years, but he also placed a dreadful curse upon us."'
	db	00
L080C:	db	'binding'
	db	00
L0814:	db	'curse'
	db	00
L081A:	db	'service'
	db	00
L0822:	db	'service'
	db	00
L082A:	db	'"As it fell out, we did not actually have to serve the wizar'
	db	'd for a thousand years. He reduced the time by a few weeks a'
	db	'fter placing that curse on us." Lasher snorts sarcastically,'
	db	' "I was heartbroken."'
	db	00
L08F4:	db	'service'
	db	00
L08FC:	db	'curse'
	db	00
L0902:	db	'"We nature spirits used to be renowned for our randiness, an'
	db	'd this wizard had called upon us to assist him in the seduct'
	db	'ion of some maiden. When we stood him up... Well, let us jus'
	db	't say that he was one magician who was having a problem conv'
	db	'incing his magic wand to work. Anyway, in a pathetic attempt'
	db	' to bolster his diminished feelings of manhood, he ruined us'
	db	' with an awesomely powerful Curse of Chastity."'
	db	00
L0A9A:	db	'curse'
	db	00
L0AA0:	db	'Chastity'
	db	00
L0AA9:	db	'Chastity'
	db	00
L0AB2:	db	'"It was a terrible curse. First, it drove us to kill all of '
	db	'the female members of our clan. Then it afflicted us with th'
	db	'e particular sensitivity for which we have become known."'
	db	00
L0B64:	db	'Chastity'
	db	00
L0B6D:	db	'virgin detector'
	db	00
L0B7D:	db	'"That is correct. So sensitive are members of my race to all'
	db	' forms of sexual energy that we can only tolerate physical c'
	db	'ontact with one who has not yet had any experience in that f'
	db	'orm of procreation - or recreation, if thou dost prefer."'
	db	00
L0C6B:	db	'virgin detector'
	db	00
L0C7B:	db	'sensitive'
	db	00
L0C85:	db	'sensitive'
	db	00
L0C8F:	db	'"Yes, I find it most unpleasant to actually come into physic'
	db	'al contact with anyone who is not a virgin, and I will avoid'
	db	' doing so whenever possible."'
	db	00
L0D25:	db	'sensitive'
	db	00
L0D2F:	db	'unpleasant'
	db	00
L0D3A:	db	'avoid'
	db	00
L0D40:	db	'avoid'
	db	00
L0D46:	db	'"Yes, well, I did not wish to get this personal with thee, b'
	db	'ut if thou does not mind, art thou a virgin?"'
	db	00
L0DB0:	db	'"I thought as much!" Lasher starts to pace nervously. "If th'
	db	'ou wouldst not mind standing back a bit, I would be most app'
	db	'reciative."'
	db	00
L0E34:	db	'Lasher slowly shakes his head. "Thou dost not have to brag i'
	db	'n order to impress me, or fear any sort of verbal chastiseme'
	db	'nts, honestly. By the way, I have an itch right betwixt my s'
	db	'houlder blades. Wouldst thou mind scratching it for me?" Las'
	db	'her stretches out toward you. "Thank thee so much."'
	db	00
L0F58:	db	'"There\'s no shame in it, milord," says Iolo, looking very s'
	db	'erious.*'
	db	00
L0F9C:	db	'"No, it is perfectly understandable. Thou hast been so busy '
	db	'lately," says Shamino. You sense he is struggling to maintai'
	db	'n a straight face.*'
	db	00
L1028:	db	'"Why dost thou not go and pet the nice horsey. We would do i'
	db	't, but I think he prefers thee." With that, you hear an expl'
	db	'osion of snorts and giggles.*'
	db	00
L10BE:	db	'virginity'
	db	00
L10C8:	db	'"I beg thy pardon, but perhaps thou shouldst go to the Lycae'
	db	'um and have someone look up the definition of the word \'vir'
	db	'ginity\' for thee. Wouldst thou mind stepping back, please?!'
	db	' Thou dost make me nervous."'
	db	00
L1197:	db	'"Yes, I could tell the answer to my question before thou did'
	db	'st even speak it. Art thou a virgin by choice or by circumst'
	db	'ance?"'
	db	00
L1216:	db	'circumstance'
	db	00
L1223:	db	'choice'
	db	00
L122A:	db	'avoid'
	db	00
L1230:	db	'virginity'
	db	00
L123A:	db	'"Surely, Avatar, thou knowest that thou dost magically regai'
	db	'n thy virginity each time upon returning to Britannia! Hast '
	db	'thou remained a virgin since then by choice or by circumstan'
	db	'ce?"'
	db	00
L12F3:	db	'virginity'
	db	00
L12FD:	db	'circumstance'
	db	00
L130A:	db	'choice'
	db	00
L1311:	db	'choice'
	db	00
L1318:	db	'"Well, I am sure thou wilt find the right person one day."'
	db	00
L1353:	db	'circumstance'
	db	00
L1360:	db	'choice'
	db	00
L1367:	db	'circumstance'
	db	00
L1374:	db	'"That is too bad, I am very sorry. I would love to be able t'
	db	'o help thee, but that is no longer my purpose."'
	db	00
L13E0:	db	'choice'
	db	00
L13E7:	db	'circumstance'
	db	00
L13F4:	db	'help'
	db	00
L13F9:	db	'help'
	db	00
L13FE:	db	'"Oh, I do not know. It has been so long since I was personal'
	db	'ly involved in such matters. Art thou seeking love or art th'
	db	'ou seeking lust?"'
	db	00
L1488:	db	'lust'
	db	00
L148D:	db	'love'
	db	00
L1492:	db	'help'
	db	00
L1497:	db	'love'
	db	00
L149C:	db	'"Hmmm, love is usually a very elusive quarry. I suppose that'
	db	' thou canst try thy luck in the city of Cove. It is a city o'
	db	'f lovers, or so I have heard."'
	db	00
L1533:	db	'lust'
	db	00
L1538:	db	'love'
	db	00
L153D:	db	'lust'
	db	00
L1542:	db	'"If quenching thy lust is thine only concern, then thou shou'
	db	'ldst find satisfaction at the Baths, in Buccaneer\'s Den. Bu'
	db	't be sure to take a full purse."'
	db	00
L15DA:	db	'lust'
	db	00
L15DF:	db	'love'
	db	00
L15E4:	db	'unpleasant'
	db	00
L15EF:	db	'"Actually, the part of being a virgin detector that I find t'
	db	'he most intolerable is having to perform upon demand for som'
	db	'e clever mage or bard or hero who wants a potential wife to '
	db	'try to touch me."'
	db	00
L16B5:	db	'unpleasant'
	db	00
L16C0:	db	'wife'
	db	00
L16C5:	db	'wife'
	db	00
L16CA:	db	'"It is a tragedy. The man always gets nervous, then places a'
	db	' condition on the marriage that his bride must be a virgin. '
	db	'They call me to put her to the test, and the man\'s bachelor'
	db	'hood is granted a reprieve. I have destroyed more engagement'
	db	's than the Bubonic Plague."'
	db	00
L17D5:	db	'wife'
	db	00
L17DA:	db	'bachelorhood'
	db	00
L17E7:	db	'bachelorhood'
	db	00
L17F4:	db	'"Just like those fools who are wandering around down here lo'
	db	'oking for me for the same reason, I would wager. Well, they '
	db	'can lose that notion. I like women, I truly do, and frankly,'
	db	' I am sick and tired of being used as the instrument of thei'
	db	'r humiliation."'
	db	00
L18F4:	db	'marriages'
	db	00
L18FE:	db	'male virginity test'
	db	00
L1912:	db	'fools'
	db	00
L1918:	db	'bachelorhood'
	db	00
L1925:	db	'fools'
	db	00
L192B:	db	'"I am a magical creature. I can avoid them down here as long'
	db	' as I want. They will die of old age before they catch me. I'
	db	' refuse to assist them in weaseling out of some breach of pr'
	db	'omise. Thou canst tell them that if thou dost see them."'
	db	00
L1A18:	db	'fools'
	db	00
L1A1E:	db	'male virginity test'
	db	00
L1A32:	db	'"They want the virginity test for a man who is getting marri'
	db	'ed?!" Lasher lets out a long surprised laugh. "In all mine e'
	db	'xistence, I have never heard of such a thing!"'
	db	00
L1AD9:	db	'male virginity test'
	db	00
L1AED:	db	'getting married'
	db	00
L1AFD:	db	'getting married'
	db	00
L1B0D:	db	'"Oh, she must be quite a ravishing maiden if he is willing t'
	db	'o risk life and limb to come down here and prove his virtue.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L1B87:	db	'getting married'
	db	00
L1B97:	db	'ravishing maiden'
	db	00
L1BA8:	db	'ravishing maiden'
	db	00
L1BB9:	db	'"This boy must be smitten something fierce by this maid. I s'
	db	'uppose that I should go and investigate this further. If he '
	db	'is as sincere about this as thou dost say, then perhaps I wi'
	db	'll help the poor lad."'
	db	00
L1C84:	db	'ravishing maiden'
	db	00
L1C95:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1C99:	db	'"Fare thee well, Avatar."*'
	db	00
