L00B7:	db	'     Found almost exclusively in the dungeon Destard, dragon'
	db	's are an ancient race of large reptiles. They possess great '
	db	'intelligence, and a few also use magic, sometimes summoning '
	db	'other creatures to fight with -- or for -- them in battle.~'
	db	00
L01A7:	db	'     However, in combat, they are quite formidable without a'
	db	'ny aid, for in addition to their sharp claws and the rows of'
	db	' razor-like teeth that fill their maws, they are capable of '
	db	'producing large clouds of fiery death. That, combined with t'
	db	'heir ability to become invisible makes them more than a matc'
	db	'h for any foolish enough to cross one.~'
	db	00
L02FB:	db	'     Shouldst one ever be found that is willing to bargain w'
	db	'ith thee, I strongly suggest doing so, for very few can surv'
	db	'ive a battle with one of these terrible lizards, and even fe'
	db	'wer can emerge victorious.'
	db	00
L03CA:	db	'~~ ~~THE JOURNAL OF GARRET MOORE*'
	db	00
L03EC:	db	'Day 1: I arrived upon this forsaken isle.~~'
	db	00
L0418:	db	'Day 3: Found the ruins of an edifice. A tower?~~'
	db	00
L0449:	db	'Day 4: Need shelter. Beginning to rebuild the tower.~~'
	db	00
L0480:	db	'Day 7: Tower.~~'
	db	00
L0490:	db	'Day 12: Tower.~~'
	db	00
L04A1:	db	'Day 21: Basic support foundation almost completed. Moving fr'
	db	'om temporary shelter tomorrow.~~'
	db	00
L04FE:	db	'Day 29: Expanding tower. Began research and experiments to p'
	db	'roduce livestock breeds for food.~~'
	db	00
L055E:	db	'Day 45: Tower complete. Near miss with experiments. Life soo'
	db	'n, I am sure of it!~~'
	db	00
L05B0:	db	'Day 73: I have done it! A combination of cells that reproduc'
	db	'e without my assistance! Self-sustaining life is not far awa'
	db	'y!~~'
	db	00
L062D:	db	'Day 97: I am near the answer, there is no doubt. But there a'
	db	're others who would see me fail! They change the sky to purp'
	db	'le and hurl bolts of lightning towards me.~~'
	db	00
L06D2:	db	'Day 111: The others still seek to thwart me! I hear their vo'
	db	'ices commanding me to cease. I will never rest until I am do'
	db	'ne!~~'
	db	00
L0750:	db	'Day 101: Again they come. They have sent a succubus to tempt'
	db	' me. "Kiss me, kiss me," is all she would say. "Nay" was my '
	db	'reply. I will be strong!~~'
	db	00
L07E3:	db	'Day 40232: Hah! The voices now beg, but I will not finish un'
	db	'til he is gone. The night is my haven and the dogs will bark'
	db	'!~~'
	db	00
L085F:	db	'~~ ~~THE TRANSITIVE VAMPIRE, by Karen Elizabeth Gordon*'
	db	00
L0897:	db	'     This richly-detailed tome is a "handbook of grammar for'
	db	' the Innocent, the Eager, and the Doomed."'
	db	00
L08FE:	db	'~~ ~~THE TOME OF THE DEAD~~ ~~by Suvol Shadowface*'
	db	00
L0931:	db	'     The crinkled pages of this book appear to be made of an'
	db	' odd sort of leather. It contains various essays concerning '
	db	'the treatment of the deceased, especially the bodily remains'
	db	'.'
	db	00
L09E7:	db	'     One chapter is entitled 101 uses for the human heart. A'
	db	'nother passage describes the method by which human skin is t'
	db	'anned and pressed for use as writing material...'
	db	00
L0A90:	db	'~~ ~~ARTIFACTS OF DARKNESS~~ ~~by Mordra Morgaelin*'
	db	00
L0AC4:	db	'     Within the pages of this handwritten book are many refe'
	db	'rences to devices of destructive power. Amongst them are Mon'
	db	'dain\'s Skull and Gem of Immortality, Minax\'s Crystal Ring,'
	db	' and the Dark Core of Exodus\' memories.'
	db	00
L0B9E:	db	'     More recent entries describe the Crown of the Liche Kin'
	db	'g, the Well of Souls, and a mysterious Blackrock Sword which'
	db	' apparently has the power to slay even one so powerful as Lo'
	db	'rd British.'
	db	00
L0C5E:	db	'     A short essay, involving a metal plate hung above a doo'
	db	'r, explains what seems to be a far simpler method of dispatc'
	db	'hing the noble monarch.'
	db	00
L0CEE:	db	'~~ ~~THE LIGHT UNTIL DAWN~~ ~~by Drennal*'
	db	00
L0D18:	db	'     Herein is the short book that discusses both moons of B'
	db	'ritannia, Trammel and Felucca, in detail, explaining their o'
	db	'rbits, approximate sizes, and expected compositions. In addi'
	db	'tion, there is a short essay about the possibility of people'
	db	' who live on these moons, and how to contact them. The work '
	db	'also includes a short story about a sorceress who discovers '
	db	'a way to change the color of Felucca. After testing her obse'
	db	'rvations, she quickly learns that the changes have little af'
	db	'fect on anything or anyone.'
	db	00
L0F14:	db	'~~ ~~CODAVAR~~ ~~by Nexa*'
	db	00
L0F2E:	db	'     Within the pages of this novel is the parable of an usu'
	db	'rping lord seemingly inspired by Blackthorn\'s tyrranical ru'
	db	'le during Lord British\'s disappearance more than two hundre'
	db	'd years ago.'
	db	00
L0FED:	db	'~~ ~~RITUAL MAGIC~~ ~~by Nicodemus*'
	db	00
L1011:	db	'     The ability to combine one\'s power with that of anothe'
	db	'r mage\'s is fundamental to the casting of enchantments. Whi'
	db	'le standing in an outer triangle of a pentagram, up to five '
	db	'wizards may enhance the effects of their spells. The bloodle'
	db	'tting from either a goat, sheep, or cat -- one per mage -- i'
	db	's necessary, in addition to the consumption of the secretion'
	db	' of a type three acid slug.~'
	db	00
L1194:	db	'     Once all the materials are gathered, each mage must sta'
	db	'nd within one of the five corners of a pentagram drawn from '
	db	'the dust of a dragon\'s thigh bone...'
	db	00
L1231:	db	'~~ ~~PATHWAYS OF PLANAR TRAVEL~~ ~~by Nicodemus*'
	db	00
L1262:	db	'     Herein are the many complex formulae necessary for trav'
	db	'el between and through the many diverse planes of existence.'
	db	' Each plane is accessed by a moongate, and even our very own'
	db	' Lord British came to Britannia from one of these planes via'
	db	' a moongate.~'
	db	00
L1360:	db	'     However, this also leads to some concern. To this point'
	db	', every individual who has entered Britannia from another pl'
	db	'ane has been benevolent (most notably Lord British and the A'
	db	'vatar). But if they have the ability to employ these gates, '
	db	'is there not the chance that other, evil beings might, too, '
	db	'be able to venture into our fair lands at their whimsy? A th'
	db	'ought to be considered for the future.'
	db	00
L14EF:	db	'~~ ~~ENCHANTING ITEMS FOR HOUSEHOLD USE~~ ~~by Nicodemus*'
	db	00
L1529:	db	'     Found upon the pages of this tome are many a recipe for'
	db	' the creation of "mundane" magic utensils and apparatuses, i'
	db	'ncluding such items as the SELF-PROPELLED BROOM, the GHOST W'
	db	'RITING QUILL, and the ALARM GEM.'
	db	00
L15FE:	db	'Toward the unfinished end of the book, the entries become er'
	db	'ratic and almost unreadable, as if written down in a hurry. '
	db	'Many of the latter items seem a little demented: the GIANT O'
	db	'BSIDIAN FLYSWATTER, the EXPLODING CORNCOB HOLDER, and the CO'
	db	'MB OF MANY BLADES. It would seem that this mage was not conj'
	db	'uring with all of his reagents.'
	db	00
L174A:	db	'~~ ~~MISCELLANEOUS CANTRIPS~~ ~~Anonymous*'
	db	00
L1775:	db	'     As the title says, this book describes the minor spells'
	db	' that fall into the bailiwick of charlatans and prestidigita'
	db	'tors.'
	db	00
L17F3:	db	'~~ ~~MODERN NECROMANCY~~ ~~by Horance*'
	db	00
L181A:	db	'     The author of this poetic treatise attempts to show how'
	db	' necromancy has been maligned throughout the years and expla'
	db	'ins the beneficial knowledge that can be garnered by studyin'
	db	'g the effects of magic on a lifeless corpse, including the m'
	db	'ore recent art of returning life to a dead companion, known '
	db	'as resurrection.'
	db	00
L1957:	db	'~~ ~~THE SYMBOLOGY OF RUNES~~ ~~by Smidgeon the Green*'
	db	00
L198E:	db	'     Found within is the complete dictionary of terms for un'
	db	'derstanding and translating runes. In addition, the work dis'
	db	'cusses in depth the relation between runes and magic. Based '
	db	'on the intense text within, it would seem that the author is'
	db	' either a profound dolt or a simple genius.'
	db	00
