L1FC3:	db	'~~ ~~A GUIDE TO CHILDCARE FOR THE RICH AND FAMOUS~~ ~~by Lad'
	db	'y M ~~ ~~with love for Samantha Meng Ling*'
	db	00
L202A:	db	'     Within is the extensive guide for nannies, describing c'
	db	'ontemporary techniques and the latest in trouble shooting wi'
	db	'th children of all ages.~'
	db	00
L20BC:	db	'     A special chapter details the art of diaper changing, a'
	db	'nd adds a touch of humor by describing (for the more soldier'
	db	'ly sorts who may be reading) the effects of hurling soiled d'
	db	'iapers at one\'s enemies.'
	db	00
L2189:	db	'~~ ~~ ~~ALAGNER\'S BOOK OF MARVELOUS AND ASTONISHING THINGS'
	db	00
L21C4:	db	'~~A compiled volume of items of interest both magical and mu'
	db	'ndane~~by Alagner*'
	db	00
L2213:	db	'     In this volume, compiled for easy reference, are some o'
	db	'f the many fascinating constructions I have found during my '
	db	'researches. These items range from interesting uses for mund'
	db	'ane items to fascinating miscarriages of magic. Please read '
	db	'and enjoy the varied realm of My Brittannia.*'
	db	00
L2331:	db	'Potions: An historical point of interest from the last sever'
	db	'al hundred years.~'
	db	00
L2380:	db	'     Circa 0207 there was a rather infamous case of a resour'
	db	'ceful peeping-tom. One may ask what this has to do with poti'
	db	'ons, but the publicity generated from this trail about the u'
	db	'se and misuse of magical potions of X-ray vision encouraged '
	db	'all honorable mages and alchemists to cease making the amazi'
	db	'ng potions. And, as these potions fell into disuse, the affe'
	db	'ctation of calling them white potions also slowly ceased, an'
	db	'd a lesser known concoction (which, ironically, is appreciab'
	db	'ly more white than the original X-ray potion I was able to v'
	db	'iew (see Alagners Index of Treasures, entry 15, for more inf'
	db	'ormation), that of common illumination, became its replaceme'
	db	'nt.*'
	db	00
L2619:	db	'Flying Carpets: A recurring magic.~'
	db	00
L263D:	db	'     As many of you undoubtedly know the Flying Carpet was e'
	db	'ssential to the Avatar in his legendary quest to save Lord B'
	db	'ritish from the Three Shadowlords. However,few people realiz'
	db	'e that this fascinating piece of lore has been rediscovered '
	db	'and, according to my sources, hidden just inside the dungeon'
	db	' Destard, (or is it Despise, I always get those mixed up (NO'
	db	'TE: look this up before publication)). This amazing carpet c'
	db	'ould fly over water and swamps with no adverse effects, a ma'
	db	'rvelous tool for the common adventurer and essential for the'
	db	' Avatar. (An interesting side note: according to an ancient '
	db	'tome, the carpet was actual believed a failure by its create'
	db	'r for its inability to rise more than a few inches off the g'
	db	'round)*'
	db	00
L2915:	db	'Wands: A trio of terrible weaponry.~'
	db	00
L293A:	db	'     The three identified varieties of magical wand all seem'
	db	' to have been made for the express purpose of changing the c'
	db	'ombat-weak spellcaster into a killing machine. And, for thos'
	db	'e with the ability to keep them from wearing out (no small f'
	db	'eat of magic, mind you, but simple for anyone capable of cra'
	db	'fting the wand in the first place), they are perhaps the mos'
	db	't formidable weapons of their size.~~'
	db	00
L2AC8:	db	'Fire Wand: This wand fires a bolt of flaming death. Accordin'
	db	'g to all known texts on the subject, the carnage was called '
	db	'"amazing."~'
	db	00
L2B4C:	db	'Lightning Wand: The effects of a bolt of lightning as it bur'
	db	'sts forth from the wand is as devastating, as its counterpar'
	db	't, the fire wand. However, according to one of its proponent'
	db	's, "the corpses look and smell much less offensive."~'
	db	00
L2C36:	db	'Magicians Wand: While only slightly more lethal than the typ'
	db	'ical bow, this wand is rendered quite effective due to two i'
	db	'nteresting facets: Its damage is of a most magical nature an'
	db	'd more than quite powerful against monsters likely to hassle'
	db	' a mage, and, it NEVER runs out of charges. If thou art inte'
	db	'rested in power and duration, this is the wand for thee.*'
	db	00
L2D9C:	db	'Silver Serpent venom: mage\'s dream, youth\'s bane.~Once upo'
	db	'n a time, the ability to gather this reagent was heralded as'
	db	' the beginning of a new era of magicry. It was the epitome o'
	db	'f High Wizardry, but alas, as frequently happens, the promis'
	db	'e paid but little.\tWhile direct doses of this reagent give '
	db	'a boost to strength, the permanent damage done to the body f'
	db	'ar outweighs any temporary advantage. Unfortunately, these a'
	db	'dverse effects tend to carry over to the spells cast using t'
	db	'his reagent.~ Before his illness, Garok Al-Mat, a mage of th'
	db	'e high mountains, was experimenting with the vemom in conjun'
	db	'ction with spider silk and giant bee pollen. His hope was to'
	db	' bind the qualities into an effective casting reagent for di'
	db	'vination. But his work is now lost forever.*'
	db	00
L3096:	db	'Hoe of Destruction: accidental glory. One of the most recent'
	db	' magic items created, this once ordinary hoe dates back to o'
	db	'nly a few years ago when one of the first mages (a bush mage'
	db	' of no real merit) to succumb to the illness that now plague'
	db	's all mages, was asked to both repair a broken hoe for a loc'
	db	'al farmer and enchant a sword for a warrior. Unfortunately, '
	db	'his perhaps-never-to-be-repeated- enchantment has made this '
	db	'hoe one of the better melee weapons around today. This hoe c'
	db	'an be distinguished by it distinctive red, glowing head. Be '
	db	'wary if thou dost ever face it.*'
	db	00
L32D3:	db	'(Items below this point need more research before publicatio'
	db	'n.)~~'
	db	00
L3315:	db	'FireDoom Staff: lethality personified.~'
	db	00
L333D:	db	'This staff, which hurls exploding fireballs that actually se'
	db	'ek out a target, is perhaps the most lethal of all magic wea'
	db	'pons created in the era of human-gargoyle cooperation. But, '
	db	'as with most of the more powerful magic weapons, its limited'
	db	' life span means it may fail thee at the worst of times.*'
	db	00
L3467:	db	'Great Dagger: A great idea but shy of a wonder.~'
	db	00
L3498:	db	'This dagger is perhaps one of the most ingeniously economica'
	db	'l items ever produced. It appears to be naught more than an '
	db	'ordinary dagger, save for large, red stone for a pommel. How'
	db	'ever, when one strikes with it, it is magically transormed i'
	db	'nto a two-handed sword. It hides well, and is light on the b'
	db	'elt, but no more dangerous that an ordinary two-handed sword'
	db	' (which, of course, is in no way feeble).~~'
	db	00
L362C:	db	'Glass Swords : A historical legacy of death.~'
	db	00
L365A:	db	'These single-use swords will almost always kill any creature'
	db	' in a single blow, but they are seldom useful for a second o'
	db	'pponent.*'
	db	00
L36DC:	db	'Other Miscellaneous Magical Weaponry.~'
	db	00
L3703:	db	'As a general case, any person with a modicum of magical tale'
	db	'nt can identify magical weapons, armour and other apparatuse'
	db	's by their pulsating glow. Often, however, the color indicat'
	db	'es even more about the item than just the existence of the e'
	db	'nchantment. For example, a green field often denotes a poiso'
	db	'ning weapon.~~'
	db	00
L383E:	db	'Starbursts: clouds of flying death.~'
	db	00
L3863:	db	'Originally designed as a small transportable weapon, this ma'
	db	'gically laminated throwing star bursts into a cloud of simil'
	db	'ar stars upon contact with its target. Although not terribly'
	db	' devasting, it is the tiny size that makes it such an effect'
	db	'ive defence. Its small size also makes it a valuable backup '
	db	'missile weapon, for many can be carried together.~~'
	db	00
L39C3:	db	'Burst Arrows:  an area effect arrow.~'
	db	00
L39E9:	db	'The arrow functions as a regular arrow, but upon impact, exp'
	db	'lodes into a thousand flying shards of death.~~'
	db	00
L3A55:	db	'Magic Boomerangs: there and back again.~'
	db	00
L3A7E:	db	'These magical boomerangs are to the gargoyle race as the mag'
	db	'ical sword it to human warriors. Their most common weapon, b'
	db	'oomerangs have the amazing ability to pass through walls and'
	db	' other solid objects and still return to the thrower. Excell'
	db	'ent for hunting in the mountains~~'
	db	00
L3B91:	db	'Venom Dagger : the assassins tool.~'
	db	00
L3BB5:	db	'This shimmering green dagger is actually the enchanted tooth'
	db	' of a poisonous sea serpent, joined to the hilt of a regular'
	db	' dagger. Its envenomed blade injects the slow poison into it'
	db	's victim, but it frequently breaks. It is the perfect assass'
	db	'ination weapon (see Alagners History, Assassination of Baron'
	db	' Johann IV (page 54)).*'
	db	00
L3CF9:	db	'Stone Harpy: The Stone harpy is the creation of the twisted '
	db	'mind of the magus and paranoid lord of Spectran. It is reput'
	db	'ed to be magically triggered by the approaching close approa'
	db	'ch of any creature.'
	db	00
L3DC1:	db	'BATHS - PROFITS~~...April, 0360 - 9000~May, 0360 - 8700~June'
	db	', 0360 - 8300~July, 0360 - 8000~August, 0630 - 6300~Septembe'
	db	'r, 0630 - 7600~ October, 0360 - 10,000...~...January, 0361 -'
	db	' 9600'
	db	00
L3E7B:	db	'~~ ~~THE HISTORY OF STONEGATE~~ ~~by Shazle*'
	db	00
L3EA8:	db	'     The story of Stonegate Castle is, indeed, an interestin'
	db	'g one. At one time the keep was occupied by the Shadowlords,'
	db	' during Lord British\'s disappearance and Blackthorn\'s evil'
	db	' rule. However, once the Avatar returned our noble monarch t'
	db	'o his throne, eliminating the Shadowlords from Britannia, a '
	db	'family of cyclops made the castle their home.~'
	db	00
L4001:	db	'     Not more than three decades from then the walls were ab'
	db	'andoned. This lasted but for a short time, however, for a sm'
	db	'all colony of wingless gargoyles found refuge within the con'
	db	'fines of the keep. Three years later they were driven out by'
	db	' Lord Vemelon of Jhelom , who chose to retain the castle for'
	db	' his own purposes~'
	db	00
L4140:	db	'     For several generations ownership was passed down the V'
	db	'emelon line until one day the very mountains nearby opened u'
	db	'p, and the swamps engulfed the castle.~'
	db	00
L41E0:	db	'     Now, rumors purport that a colony of trolls have taken '
	db	'up residence amongst the ruins, along with an ancient wizard'
	db	', but no one has ever confirmed\ttheir existence.'
	db	00
L4289:	db	'~~ ~~THE WAY OF THE SWALLOW~~ ~~by Foiles*'
	db	00
L42B4:	db	'     Within the pages of this tome lies the story of a mothe'
	db	'r who loved, and was deeply loved by, her family. Though the'
	db	' work ends sadly with the death of the mother, her family ga'
	db	'ins comfort in the knowledge that her inner spirit has found'
	db	' a better place to rest.'
	db	00
L43BD:	db	'~~ ~~VETRONS GUIDE TO WEAPONS AND ARMOUR~~ ~~Their effective'
	db	'ness and value*'
	db	00
L4409:	db	'Here is listed, for easy comparison, the various weapons and'
	db	' their effect upon opponents:~~Axe, two-handed: 10~~Blowgun:'
	db	' 1, can be used with poison or sleep~~ Bow: 8~~Cannon: 90~~C'
	db	'lub 2~~Crossbow: 10~~Dagger: 1~~Halberd: 10~~ Hammer: 4~~Ham'
	db	'mer, two-handed: 9~~Knife: 2~~Mace: 5~~Main gauche: 2~~ Morn'
	db	'ingstar: 5~~Powder keg: 16~~Sling: 3~~Sword: 6~~Sword, two-h'
	db	'anded: 11~~ Throwing axe: 4~~Torch: 3~~Triple crossbow: 28~~'
	db	'Whip: 4*'
	db	00
