L0000:	db	'I don\'t know'
	db	00
L000D:	db	'Have Faith'
	db	00
L0018:	db	'Strive for Unity'
	db	00
L0029:	db	'No Answers'
	db	00
L0034:	db	'Be Good'
	db	00
L003C:	db	'No Answers'
	db	00
L0047:	db	'The sage smiles. "Thou hast begun thy journey on the road to'
	db	' enlightenment. As thou hast heard, all is not what one has '
	db	'been taught by one\'s teachers. \'Tis a pity. Now I suppose '
	db	'thou dost want to borrow the notebook?"'
	db	00
L0121:	db	'"Very well. Dost thou promise to return my notebook?"'
	db	00
L0157:	db	'"Then go find it! Thou hast the key!"'
	db	00
L017D:	db	'"Very well. I am counting on thee to return it to me persona'
	db	'lly. No telling what misfortune may befall thee if thou dost'
	db	' fail to do so. And as further incentive, I just might give '
	db	'thee something else which will help thee in thy quest if tho'
	db	'u dost return it to me safely.~~"Here is the key to my store'
	db	'room, the first building to the south of here." He grins sly'
	db	'ly. "Thou must determine how to find the notebook thyself!"'
	db	00
L0321:	db	'"Thou hast not enough room to take my key! Unload thy belong'
	db	'ings and we shall try all of this again!"*'
	db	00
L0388:	db	'"Then I cannot let thee borrow the notebook!"'
	db	00
L03B6:	db	'"Oh. Very well, then."*'
