	; Function at file offset 0014214FH
	.funcnumber  0850H
	.data
	.msize       15A6H
	.dsize       1386H
L0000:	db	'The ceremony begins as Batlin stands before the gathered Fel'
	db	'lowship members. The hall fills with thunderous cheers. They'
	db	' look at him with a mixture of awe and sheer adoration. Batl'
	db	'in stands and basks in the warm reception for a moment, a tr'
	db	'iumphant smile on his face. With a slight gesture of his han'
	db	'd the crowd becomes quiet.'
	db	00
L0147:	db	'"It is good to see you here this evening!" Batlin says. "Sur'
	db	'ely you make me feel proud to be part of what we lovingly ca'
	db	'll The Fellowship." There is another eruption of applause.'
	db	00
L01FA:	db	'"In thine heart be glad for thou dost walk with The Fellowsh'
	db	'ip! The people of Britannia live in a fevered state of illus'
	db	'ory thoughts and emotions. But those whom I look upon here t'
	db	'onight are seekers of what is good and true in the world! Th'
	db	'ey walk the path which leads to becoming truly cognizant. Bu'
	db	't how dost thou find thy way? Ask any Fellowship member and '
	db	'they will tell thee! The path to complete awareness is easy '
	db	'to find. One must apply to one\'s life the Triad of Inner St'
	db	'rength.'
	db	00
L03E1:	db	'"The Triad of Inner Strength is a series of three values tha'
	db	't can bring the mind to a perfect state of sanguine cognitio'
	db	'n. The first value is Strive For Unity. When the totality of'
	db	' the people of the world want to accomplish something, then '
	db	'it becomes done. Thus once the people of the world all striv'
	db	'e towards the same ends there is nothing that is impossible.'
	db	' Just think of it! A world where any dream can be fulfilled,'
	db	' any good can be achieved. But as thou canst see plainly by '
	db	'looking at our own sad society, when the people of the world'
	db	' are disunited, it is a miracle that anything gets accomplis'
	db	'hed!'
	db	00
L063E:	db	'"The second value is Trust Thy Brother. Thou must surrender '
	db	'thy fear, prejudice and suspicion. Look to thine own self! B'
	db	'efore thou dost question anything, question thyself! The wor'
	db	'ld is a place where the balances of nature are at work to pr'
	db	'otect thee every second without thee even realizing it! What'
	db	' canst thou accomplish in this world if thou dost spend all '
	db	'thy time questioning thy brother?! Is he working as hard as '
	db	'I? What are his true motivations? As thou dost waste thine e'
	db	'nergies wondering, he sees thee and starts wondering these s'
	db	'ame things about thee. Thus is the world diminished!'
	db	00
L088F:	db	'"The third value is Worthiness Precedes Reward. There is not'
	db	' one among us who is without desire. Much of the misery in t'
	db	'he world can be traced to unfulfilled desires. But one momen'
	db	't! Why dost thou deserve what thou dost desire? Most people '
	db	'get what they are worthy of in this life. If thou art not wo'
	db	'rthy of thy desire then thou shouldst not be surprised if th'
	db	'y desires are unfulfilled. If thou dost become worthy only t'
	db	'hen hast thou become open to fulfilling thy desires. Desire '
	db	'is a strange thing. Many long for things they do not really '
	db	'want. What they really desire is worthiness itself!'
	db	00
L0ADF:	db	'"I have just told thee all that thou dost need to follow the'
	db	' Triad Of Inner Strength. The lessons are simple. The true m'
	db	'easure of thine understanding comes in how absolutely thou w'
	db	'ilt apply them to thy life. Thou now knowest all thou wilt e'
	db	'ver need. Thou dost not need the arcane knowledge of the dyi'
	db	'ng art of magic. Thou dost not need the unsure hand of the h'
	db	'ealer and his limited knowledge. All that thou wilt ever nee'
	db	'd is to continuously seek out the best in thyself and to liv'
	db	'e amongst those that would do the same. Only then art thou t'
	db	'ruly walking with The Fellowship.'
	db	00
L0D1D:	db	'"Now I think would be a good time to hear the words of our f'
	db	'ellow members. To hear them share with us how The Fellowship'
	db	' has been bringing positive change to their lives."'
	db	00
L0DC9:	db	'"The Fellowship has shown me that I was afraid of myself and'
	db	' that I had to open myself up to life\'s experiences," says '
	db	'Candice.*'
	db	00
L0E4A:	db	'"The Fellowship helps me be more honest with people," says P'
	db	'atterson.*'
	db	00
L0E91:	db	'"Thank thee for sharing, Patterson."*'
	db	00
L0EB7:	db	'"The Fellowship has taught me how to better perform my dutie'
	db	's as the Caretaker of the Royal Orchards," says Figg.*'
	db	00
L0F2A:	db	'"The Fellowship has taught me to, first and foremost, treat '
	db	'people with respect," says Gaye.*'
	db	00
L0F88:	db	'"After joining The Fellowship I learned how to be a man\'s m'
	db	'an," says Grayson.*'
	db	00
L0FD7:	db	'"The Fellowship is helping me back from the brink of persona'
	db	'l and financial oblivion," says Gordon.*'
	db	00
L103C:	db	'"Right thou art, brother!"*'
	db	00
L1058:	db	'"The Fellowship has freed me from the illusory appeals of me'
	db	'diocrity," says Sean.*'
	db	00
L10AB:	db	'"In The Fellowship I am learning that I need to devote my li'
	db	'fe to a special purpose," says Millie.*'
	db	00
L110F:	db	'"This whole ceremony and everyone in it doth give me the wil'
	db	'lies!"*'
	db	00
L1153:	db	'"\'Tis a sad thing to see so many people who have nothing el'
	db	'se better in their lives than blindly following this dubious'
	db	' spiritual leader."*'
	db	00
L11DF:	db	'"\'Tis a sad thing that Britannia has fallen so far as to le'
	db	'ave itself open to a group like this Fellowship."*'
	db	00
L124D:	db	'"\'Tis a sad thing when I cannot even keep my eyes open from'
	db	' the boredom of this Fellowship ceremony!"*'
	db	00
L12B4:	db	'From watching Batlin and the others you get the feeling that'
	db	' the Fellowship ceremony is going to last long into the nigh'
	db	't. Now would be a good moment to slip away without drawing m'
	db	'uch attention to yourself...*'
	db	00
