	; Function at file offset 0014B960H
	.funcnumber  0877H
	.data
	.msize       0686H
	.dsize       0651H
L0000:	db	'"I shall tell thee the story of the only unhappy person in C'
	db	'ove -- Nastassia. She is the only person in town without a l'
	db	'over. Not that she does not have suitors -- she is quite bea'
	db	'utiful! All she thinks about is the Shrine of Compassion, wh'
	db	'ich is where thou wouldst probably find her at this moment."'
	db	'~~De Maria strums his lute and sings:~~'
	db	00
L0154:	db	'"There once was a maid Ariana~ Who held the shrine so dear.~'
	db	' She asked that her offspring do likewise~ And keep it so ye'
	db	'ar after year.'
	db	00
L01DB:	db	'"Her son Mikhail became mayor~ With a goal to keep in fashio'
	db	'n~ The towne\'s old, belov\'d reputation~ As the city of lov'
	db	'e and passion!'
	db	00
L0260:	db	'"Mikhail\'s oldest child was Magda;~ She built Lovers\' Walk'
	db	', a fine park,~ Where Cove\'s lovers, both young and old,~ C'
	db	'ould court outdoors in the dark!'
	db	00
L02F6:	db	'Ah, but the clouds of misfortune do hide~ Where the sun\'s b'
	db	'rightness seemeth most fair.~ And poor Nadia, Magda\'s daugh'
	db	'ter,~ Of misfortune had more than her share!'
	db	00
L0399:	db	'"It began when Nadia did wed one day~ To Julius, a not-so-we'
	db	'althy young lad.~ He left her with child and went far away.~'
	db	' As for Nadia\'s poor heart, \'twas sad.'
	db	00
L0438:	db	'"One day from Yew the fateful news came~ That Julius by a be'
	db	'ast was killed;~ The child came early, \'twas a difficult bi'
	db	'rth;~ And Nadia\'s soul became chilled.'
	db	00
L04D6:	db	'"With dagger in hand and child in arm~ To the Shrine did Nad'
	db	'ia run.~ She plunged the dagger into her own breast;~ Never '
	db	'again would she see the sun.'
	db	00
L056B:	db	'"Nastassia grew up an orphan, you see,~ Unloved and unwanted'
	db	' by all;~ Today she walks cloaked in solitude~ Awaiting her '
	db	'destiny\'s call.'
	db	00
L05F3:	db	'"And that is poor Nastassia\'s tale. Perhaps thou canst chee'
	db	'r her. Find her, I beseech thee!"*'
	db	00
