L0000:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0004:	db	'sacrificed'
	db	00
L000F:	db	'Don\'t know'
	db	00
L001A:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L001E:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0022:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0027:	db	'what next'
	db	00
L0031:	db	'Don\'t know'
	db	00
L003C:	db	'He kneels over the body and inspects the other golem. As his'
	db	' fingers trace around the gaping hole in Bollux\'s chest, an'
	db	' expression of understanding fills his visage.~"H-his heart '
	db	'is gone!"~ He stares down at his own chest. "He sacrificed h'
	db	'imself by giving me his heart... the fool!" His words are in'
	db	'sulting but his tone is affectionate.'
	db	00
L018D:	db	'sacrificed'
	db	00
L0198:	db	'Don\'t know'
	db	00
L01A3:	db	'"I must help him, as he helped me! Wilt thou assist?"'
	db	00
L01D9:	db	'"Very good," he says, noticeably relieved. "I thank thee in '
	db	'advance."'
	db	00
L021F:	db	'fool'
	db	00
L0224:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0228:	db	'name'
	db	00
L022D:	db	'"Then I must go this one myself," he says angrily. "\'Tis no'
	db	' more than one friend would do for another... no more than B'
	db	'ollux did for me!"'
	db	00
L02B7:	db	'He looks at you carefully. His stoney features do nothing to'
	db	' hide the suspicion on his face, or in his voice.~"It is qui'
	db	'te obvious to me thou art but a lost traveler and certainly '
	db	'not the Avatar for whom I mistook thee."*'
	db	00
L0395:	db	'sacrificed'
	db	00
L03A0:	db	'You quickly relate the details of Bollux\'s death as he pull'
	db	'ed the object from his chest and placed it in the other gole'
	db	'm\'s.~"He sacrificed himself by giving me his heart... the f'
	db	'ool!" His words are insulting but his tone is affectionate.'
	db	00
L048E:	db	'sacrificed'
	db	00
L0499:	db	'Don\'t know'
	db	00
L04A4:	db	'"I must help him, as he helped me! Wilt thou assist?"'
	db	00
L04DA:	db	'"Very good," he says, notably relieved. "I thank thee in adv'
	db	'ance."'
	db	00
L051D:	db	'fool'
	db	00
L0522:	db	'job'
	db	00
L0526:	db	'name'
	db	00
L052B:	db	'"Then I must go this one myself," he says angrily. "\'Tis no'
	db	' more than one friend would do for another... no more than B'
	db	'ollux did for me!"'
	db	00
L05B5:	db	'He looks at you carefully. His stoney features do nothing to'
	db	' hide the suspicion on his face, or in his voice.~"It is qui'
	db	'te obvious to me thou art but a lost traveler and certainly '
	db	'not the Avatar for whom I mistook thee."*'
	db	00
L0693:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0698:	db	'name'
	db	00
L069D:	db	'"I am the golem called Adjhar, at thy service."'
	db	00
L06CD:	db	'job'
	db	00
L06D1:	db	'"I am one of the guardians of the Shrines of the Principles.'
	db	' That was exactly what Bollux and I were doing when the wall'
	db	' fell and crushed me."'
	db	00
L0760:	db	'wall'
	db	00
L0765:	db	'Shrines'
	db	00
L076D:	db	'Bollux'
	db	00
L0774:	db	'Shrines'
	db	00
L077C:	db	'Shrines'
	db	00
L0784:	db	'"Surely thou hast heard of the Shrines of the Three Principl'
	db	'es: Truth, Love, and Courage! We golems were fabricated to p'
	db	'rotect the Shrines, for only an Avatar -- -the- Avatar -- ma'
	db	'y utilize the awesome power they can convey."'
	db	00
L0866:	db	'wall'
	db	00
L086B:	db	'wall'
	db	00
L0870:	db	'"I do not remember the incident clearly. However, I will rel'
	db	'ate what I can recall. Bollux and I were standing guard in t'
	db	'he Shrine Room of the Principles when we detected an intrusi'
	db	'on into the the castle. I remember nothing more than being a'
	db	'ware of great heat, and then part of the wall crumbling atop'
	db	' me, crushing my legs. I suppose Bollux was more forunate. W'
	db	'as it he who carried me here?"'
	db	00
L09F7:	db	'"Then it is imperative that we find a way to bring him back!'
	db	' If nothing else, I owe him my gratitude."'
	db	00
L0A5E:	db	'"Strange," he says, puzzled. "I am at a loss then to explain'
	db	' my arrival here.~Regardless, I -must- find a way to restore'
	db	' life to him!"'
	db	00
L0AE5:	db	'Bollux'
	db	00
L0AEC:	db	'"Hast thou not already met him? He is my older brother, and '
	db	'my friend."'
	db	00
L0B34:	db	'Bollux'
	db	00
L0B3B:	db	'older'
	db	00
L0B41:	db	'older'
	db	00
L0B47:	db	'"Master Astelleron -- we actually called him our father -- c'
	db	'reated him before he did me. And he instilled Bollux with a '
	db	'personality first."'
	db	00
L0BD3:	db	'older'
	db	00
L0BD9:	db	'what next'
	db	00
L0BE3:	db	'what next'
	db	00
L0BED:	db	'"Dost thou have the book entitled, `The Stone of Castambre?'
	db	'\'"'
	db	00
L0C2B:	db	'His eyes reveal his hope. As he takes the book from you, it '
	db	'almost appears as if he is smiling."'
	db	00
L0C8C:	db	'"I must see the book the book to use it. Perhaps thou hast m'
	db	'islaid it about somewhere." He stares directly at you. "\'Ti'
	db	's vital that I have that tome. I beg thee, retrieve it for m'
	db	'e!"'
	db	00
L0D43:	db	'"Please go and recover it then. I believe it contains inform'
	db	'ation that may help my companion."'
	db	00
L0DA2:	db	'fool'
	db	00
L0DA7:	db	'fool'
	db	00
L0DAC:	db	'"Poor Bollux did not know of the Stone of Castambre. His sac'
	db	'rifice was, perhaps, unnecessary. Hast thou, perchance, come'
	db	' across MacCuth\'s "The Stone of Castambre?"'
	db	00
L0E50:	db	'"Dost thou have it with thee?"'
	db	00
L0E6F:	db	'His eyes reveal his hope. As he takes the book from you, it '
	db	'almost appears as if he is smiling."'
	db	00
L0ED0:	db	'"I must see the book the book to use it. Perhaps thou hast m'
	db	'islaid it about somewhere." He stares directly at you. "\'Ti'
	db	's vital that I have that tome. I beg thee, retrieve it for m'
	db	'e!"'
	db	00
L0F87:	db	'"Please go and recover it then. I believe it contains inform'
	db	'ation that may help my companion."'
	db	00
L0FE6:	db	'"Then I recommend thou dost search within my master\'s chamb'
	db	'ers for it. The pages contain words which may help my compan'
	db	'ion."'
	db	00
L1063:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L1067:	db	'"I can offer nothing more for thine assistance than my deepe'
	db	'st appreciation. Please journey in peace."*'
	db	00
