	; Function at file offset 0015258AH
	.funcnumber  0891H
	.data
	.msize       0494H
	.dsize       0462H
L0000:	db	'"\'Tis as I suspected. Bollux thought he must sacrifice his '
	db	'own heart to return my life."~If you were to believe it poss'
	db	'ible, you would feel positive you had just seen a drop of wa'
	db	'ter fall from the golem\'s right eye.~"The poor fool gave hi'
	db	's life for mine. I can only hope I would have done the same.'
	db	'~"Doing so now, however, would help nothing, for once I was '
	db	'gone Bollux would simply repeat his act." You hear a sigh co'
	db	'me from the golem.'
	db	00
L01B5:	db	'I don\'t mean to be irreverent, but did the matter not invol'
	db	've death, \'twould be a humorous sight: the two golems poppi'
	db	'ng up and down as each one passed the `heart\' to the other.'
	db	'..@'
	db	00
L026A:	db	'"However," smiles Adjhar, "\'tis not necessary, for had Boll'
	db	'ux known what is covered by this smudge, he could have told '
	db	'thee that a new heart may be cut from the Tree of Life. Look'
	db	' here," he says, pointing to a line in the tome smeared with'
	db	' dried mud. "I remember this from before. Thou canst take th'
	db	'e very same pick with which thou didst collect the blood and'
	db	' procure a `heart\' for Bollux. Of course, after thou dost p'
	db	'lace the heart upon Bollux\'s body, thou must again perform '
	db	'the same ritual of blood."'
	db	00
