	; Function at file offset 0015327FH
	.funcnumber  0894H
	.data
	.msize       0FD3H
	.dsize       0CF4H
L0000:	db	'"I -must- return his life to him. He -will- have a new heart'
	db	'!" The determination is quite evident by his forceful glare '
	db	'and stance.'
	db	00
L0084:	db	'The stone statue stands with a lowered head. Despite its gra'
	db	'nite features, a downcast look is apparent on its face. Surp'
	db	'risingly, it turns to speak with you.'
	db	00
L0122:	db	'@Why, by the stars, I believe it \r\n\t\t\t\tis a creature!@'
	db	00
L0159:	db	'Slowly, as if with great effort, it raises it head.'
	db	00
L018D:	db	'"What dost thou... want?" it asks slowly.'
	db	00
L01B7:	db	'"Help him?" it asks carefully, pointing to the fallen statue'
	db	' lying beside it.'
	db	00
L0205:	db	'help'
	db	00
L020A:	db	'Creature?'
	db	00
L0214:	db	'"In what way may I assist thee?"'
	db	00
L0235:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0239:	db	'job'
	db	00
L023D:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0242:	db	'name'
	db	00
L0247:	db	'name'
	db	00
L024C:	db	'He tilts his head and stares at you quizzicaly.~ "I apologiz'
	db	'e. Did I not already tell thee my master called me Bollux?"'
	db	00
L02C4:	db	'"My master named me Bollux.'
	db	00
L02E0:	db	'master'
	db	00
L02E7:	db	'job'
	db	00
L02EB:	db	'"I am a guardian of the Shrines of the Principles."'
	db	00
L031F:	db	'guardian'
	db	00
L0328:	db	'guardian'
	db	00
L0331:	db	'guardian'
	db	00
L033A:	db	'"We were... created to protect the Shrines of the Principles'
	db	'. Only the... Avatar should use their power. Adjhar and I we'
	db	're... keeping watch... when the wall fell on Adjhar. And the'
	db	' loud noise came...  I carried him here so that I could rest'
	db	'ore him, but I do not... know how."'
	db	00
L044E:	db	'Creature?'
	db	00
L0458:	db	'Creature?'
	db	00
L0462:	db	'"We are called stone golems... because we are made out of st'
	db	'one and rock."'
	db	00
L04AD:	db	'made'
	db	00
L04B2:	db	'stone'
	db	00
L04B8:	db	'Astelleron'
	db	00
L04C3:	db	'master'
	db	00
L04CA:	db	'master'
	db	00
L04D1:	db	'Astelleron'
	db	00
L04DC:	db	'"Astelleron made us. He is our master."'
	db	00
L0504:	db	'made'
	db	00
L0509:	db	'stone'
	db	00
L050F:	db	'stone'
	db	00
L0515:	db	'"We were... fashioned... out of the rock from the quarry on '
	db	'this small island."'
	db	00
L0565:	db	'made'
	db	00
L056A:	db	'made'
	db	00
L056F:	db	'"I know nothing about the process, but Astelleron once told '
	db	'me he used something called... magic to give us life and... '
	db	'animation." The golem pauses, obviously conscious of his nex'
	db	't thought.~"He did not like his... solitude. He said he was.'
	db	'.. lonely."'
	db	00
L066B:	db	'lonely'
	db	00
L0672:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L0678:	db	'Astelleron'
	db	00
L0683:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L0689:	db	'magic'
	db	00
L068F:	db	'"I do not know what... it is, but there are many books in hi'
	db	's house. Perhaps... there is something there about... magic.'
	db	'"'
	db	00
L0709:	db	'books'
	db	00
L070F:	db	'books'
	db	00
L0715:	db	'books'
	db	00
L071B:	db	'"I have a book here that Adjhar said told about... our... cr'
	db	'eation. This might help bring Adjhar back."'
	db	00
L0783:	db	'He hands to you a very old tome. It is evident the book has '
	db	'seen much use, for the leather covering is wearing away to r'
	db	'eveal the wood beneath and the pages are quite dog-earred.~"'
	db	'I already put rocks down," he adds, "just like the... book s'
	db	'aid to."'
	db	00
L087C:	db	'Thou art... carrying too much. Put something down and I can '
	db	'give this to you."'
	db	00
L08CB:	db	'"There are several... more books lying about the house. I do'
	db	' not... know what they are about.  Adjhar read them."'
	db	00
L093D:	db	'lonely'
	db	00
L0944:	db	'lonely'
	db	00
L094B:	db	'"Astelleron said it was how... a person feels when no one is'
	db	' around. He told us how... happy he felt after we were... bo'
	db	'rn.~ He called me... a son."'
	db	00
L09E0:	db	'help'
	db	00
L09E5:	db	'help'
	db	00
L09EA:	db	'"My companion... Adjhar... He is dying. Thou must help repai'
	db	'r him. Please, I beg... thee."'
	db	00
L0A45:	db	'"I have a book here that Adjhar said told about... our... cr'
	db	'eation. This might help bring him back."'
	db	00
L0AAA:	db	'He hands to you a very old tome. It is evident the book has '
	db	'seen much use, for the leather covering is wearing away to r'
	db	'eveal the wood beneath and the pages are quite dog-earred. "'
	db	'I have already set up five... rocks to mark a spot for the..'
	db	'. blood."'
	db	00
L0BA4:	db	'blood'
	db	00
L0BAA:	db	'Thou art... carrying too much. Put something down and I can '
	db	'give this to you."'
	db	00
L0BF9:	db	'Adjhar'
	db	00
L0C00:	db	'Adjhar'
	db	00
L0C07:	db	'Adjhar'
	db	00
L0C0E:	db	'"He is my brother... and my friend. We protected the... Shri'
	db	'nes together. We cannot let him... stay like that. Help me..'
	db	'. assist him."'
	db	00
L0C95:	db	'blood'
	db	00
L0C9B:	db	'blood'
	db	00
L0CA1:	db	'"I did not... understand the book, but I remember... blood..'
	db	'."'
	db	00
L0CE0:	db	'bye'
	db	00
L0CE4:	db	'"Good... bye."*'
	db	00
