	; Function at file offset 0015AFFEH
	.funcnumber  08B1H
	.data
	.msize       0469H
	.dsize       03F6H
L0000:	db	'"Once again, Avatar, thou hast proven that thou art ever the'
	db	' defender of Britannia and the innocent. I cannot adequately'
	db	' express my gratitude; however, please take this small token'
	db	' of my thanks. I hope it will help thee in thy quest."'
	db	00
L00EB:	db	'He hands you his personal staff. It appears to be magical.'
	db	00
L0126:	db	'He places his personal staff on the ground. It appears to be'
	db	' magical.~"I have something for thee, Avatar, but I see that'
	db	' thou canst not carry it now. I will set it here upon the fl'
	db	'oor for thee."'
	db	00
L01E9:	db	'For a moment Horance looks downcast. "I feel that some of th'
	db	'e responsibility for what happened in this town is upon my s'
	db	'houlders. For, in my search to uncover the truths of the uni'
	db	'verse, I unwittingly released that foul spirit which destroy'
	db	'ed this town. I will spend the rest of my days in the attemp'
	db	't to restore this once lovely town.~~"I will make it into a '
	db	'shining example of Spirituality, a shrine where people of go'
	db	'od heart may live in peace and harmony. And again, I thank t'
	db	'hee for giving me this chance. Goodbye, '
	db	00
L03F2:	db	'."*'
	db	00
