	.dsize       0E52H
L0000:	db	'As the actors take their places and don masks, you settle do'
	db	'wn to watch the action.*'
	db	00
L0055:	db	'Spark whispers to you, "I wish there was a confectioner that'
	db	' sold candied apples!"*'
	db	00
L00A9:	db	'The music starts the play, as Paul takes center stage and ad'
	db	'dresses the audience.'
	db	00
L00FB:	db	'"Welcome to Our Tale, ~A tale so true to life. ~\'Tis a tale'
	db	' of tragedy ~A man has lost his wife.'
	db	00
L015C:	db	'"But the story need not be sad ~When The Fellowship is here.'
	db	' ~The Triad of Inner Strength ~Gives one no cause to fear."*'
	db	00
L01D5:	db	'Dustin takes the stage as Paul moves away. Meryl lies on the'
	db	' ground in front of him and assumes a death-like pose.'
	db	00
L0248:	db	'"\'Tis doom! \'Tis despair! \'Tis death! ~My beloved wife is'
	db	' gone! ~Disease has taken her away ~And left me with but a s'
	db	'ong."'
	db	00
L02C3:	db	'Dustin puts his head in his hands and mimes sobbing. As he s'
	db	'obs, Meryl rises from her "death" in a ghost-like fashion, t'
	db	'hen addresses Dustin.*'
	db	00
L0352:	db	'"Mine husband, my love! ~Do not despair! \'Tis not doom! ~Th'
	db	'ou shalt rise above ~All this melancholy and gloom!"*'
	db	00
L03C3:	db	'"Who doth speak to me? ~Could it be she? ~Or have I indeed g'
	db	'one mad? ~But who else -could- it be?"*'
	db	00
L0427:	db	'"Mine husband, thou must listen. ~Thou hast thy comfort with'
	db	'in thy grip. ~Thou must only seek them out -- ~Those that ca'
	db	'n help -- The Fellowship!"*'
	db	00
L04BB:	db	'Meryl drifts off stage, leaving Dustin alone.'
	db	00
L04E9:	db	'"The Fellowship, she said? ~But what do I need with it? ~I h'
	db	'ave mine eight virtues and mine healers ~With these nothing '
	db	'else will fit!"*'
	db	00
L0572:	db	'Paul enters the stage with Meryl, who now wears a different '
	db	'mask.'
	db	00
L05B4:	db	'"But that is where thou art wrong! ~The Fellowship exists to'
	db	' help thee! ~The Triad of Inner Strength is here ~To give th'
	db	'ee a sense of unity!"'
	db	00
L0642:	db	'"Join us now and thou wilt see. ~Join thy brothers and our p'
	db	'lan ~To promote the tenets of our group -- ~Thou wilt be a b'
	db	'etter man."'
	db	00
L06C6:	db	'At this point, an elaborate mimed sequence reveals how Dusti'
	db	'n joins The Fellowship, receives his medallion from a "branc'
	db	'h leader", portrayed by Paul, and receives congratulations f'
	db	'rom Meryl.'
	db	00
L0785:	db	'"Strive for Unity at all times, ~And Trust Thy Brother throu'
	db	'gh all ill, ~For Worthiness Precedes thine own Reward ~Hark '
	db	'to our words -- it surely will!"*'
	db	00
L081F:	db	'"I shall give half my wealth to thee! ~I shall do thy biddin'
	db	'g and then wait. ~My reward shall come one day ~And free me '
	db	'from mine awful fate."'
	db	00
L08AE:	db	'Dustin mimes giving Paul some money. Paul exits, then Dustin'
	db	' lies down on the stage and mimes going to sleep. After a mo'
	db	'ment, Meryl enters the stage, dances around Dustin\'s body, '
	db	'sprinkling some kind of sparkling dust on him.*'
	db	00
L0991:	db	'Iolo whispers to you. "I am particularly enjoying the visual'
	db	' effects. The script is a little weak, dost thou not think?"'
	db	'*'
	db	00
L0A0B:	db	'Meryl leaves the stage and Dustin \'wakes up\'. Lo and behol'
	db	'd, he finds a bag near his place of sleep. Upon opening it, '
	db	'he finds a bundle of gold!'
	db	00
L0A9C:	db	'"By Lord British I declare! ~\'Tis my reward! From the air! '
	db	'~The voice I heard at night was right ~About my wretched lif'
	db	'e I will not care!'
	db	00
L0B26:	db	'"The voice came to me in a dream ~\'Twas mine \'inner\' voic'
	db	'e, so fair. ~I now have a companion and provider, ~And a mas'
	db	'ter about whom I care."'
	db	00
L0BB3:	db	'You are jarred by the actor\'s choice of words -- \'companio'
	db	'n\', \'provider\', and \'master\'. You realize you have hear'
	db	'd them before.*'
	db	00
L0C34:	db	'"This is really awful."*'
	db	00
L0C4D:	db	'Paul and Meryl join Dustin on stage and they all hold hands.'
	db	'*'
	db	00
L0C8B:	db	'"The Fellowship can give thee purpose ~To join is thine only'
	db	' choice ~Commit thyself to our just cause ~And find thine in'
	db	'ner voice."'
	db	00
L0D0F:	db	'At that point, the actors bow, and you realize it is the end'
	db	'. You give them polite applause.*'
	db	00
L0D6D:	db	'"What do they mean about the voice? I am not sure I understa'
	db	'nd. \'Twas a confusing play. I did not like it at all. We ha'
	db	've wasted our time and money! That is the last time that I l'
	db	'et thee decide how best we entertain ourselves!"*'
	db	00
